[{"sha":"1168254bd9366faab73835a2cf8eb43d00acad78","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDExNjgyNTRiZDkzNjZmYWFiNzM4MzVhMmNmOGViNDNkMDBhY2FkNzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T22:07:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T22:07:05Z"},"message":"[codex] group blocking and postmerge CI workflows (#30146)\n\n## Why\n\nIt's hard to change the set of required jobs when they're managed in the\nGitHub UI, and when each workflow is responsible for choosing it's own\nscheduling it's easy to end up with skew between what we enforce on PRs\nvs. on main.\n\n## What\n\n- add a `blocking-ci` caller workflow, triggered by pull requests and\npushes to `main`, for Bazel, blob size, cargo-deny, Codespell,\n`repo-checks`, rust CI, and SDK CI\n- add an `always()` terminal job named `CI required` that fails unless\nevery called workflow succeeds\n- add a `postmerge-ci` caller workflow for `rust-ci-full` and\n`v8-canary`, with a terminal `Postmerge CI results` job\n- centralize V8 relevance detection in `v8_canary_changes.py`; unrelated\nPR and postmerge runs execute metadata only and skip the expensive build\nmatrices\n- leave `v8-canary` outside the blocking gate and leave the external\n`cla` check independent\n\n## Rollout\n\nA repository admin must replace the existing required GitHub Actions\ncontexts with `CI required` in the main-branch ruleset. Retain `cla` as\na separate required check. Until that change is coordinated, this PR\ncannot satisfy the old standalone check names. In-flight PRs will need\nto be rebased after this lands.","tree":{"sha":"d2ff427c63b30c8768f4be3e6e6da053d8b6136e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d2ff427c63b30c8768f4be3e6e6da053d8b6136e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1168254bd9366faab73835a2cf8eb43d00acad78","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPvgJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7l8QAJKaXy68Nrg/ig/YFt8+nrDE\n0j9qDVQq8lrFfTjS3IG/9emrL3Ip5EYEAincir2rO6P3daQbSx4ypF+guB6pv8B7\nxTGeE1z88fC7v1DYmk4rIEjOtJXMMinatcKhk7/wKalpiVw8A9BYDXbXzRmpuqyQ\n25/zv9O00V08izzjEmf3oA/p1bVbAp8xErZlqn3DOdwLSHEJ0y4M5BPWl5PE1iIW\nS6DYwrReM62zgxF85x7Lk11toimbx8guIzhZHidn3ZKd56PrxyJcKqBVKLwxijOm\nmnYEGn/WYUNHL5rv0uNMmyYSP18r64gtqFGWPPStZdUdEiwdxMaxeY9/P1fqL2bL\nLVexPw2r31T0m/Z+oPTMDgFkwTik2IQy4Q9YlunWllqpsgbK0iZ5UbQjMusX3gfI\nyyQVEh8z8UkNwRvArvhcphyje/WvC6N09wSsRXGnbvUOkfCwdAefebbIdDviYwfc\nA05xHpeKFWEARnqQwpZzOkxqFc3TlAcgcKb9E3HVMl9VKiY0dpYw5/7q2AhjVV2U\nQjYS1NBsIiIKuC7kUq/ic9QcFpra6sv14hySphMkR0gHlk2FsDWSxrv3rZEGJq+o\nObk39tHQfnWMJtphRd1Ceuwp+xMJs5Agep1vETTk4n9OqnnAGITmehd4Z69L2oBf\nNLc8RAMY8pqgPx2bhTUD\n=n7fR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d2ff427c63b30c8768f4be3e6e6da053d8b6136e\nparent 6509f3148a248f5da6c03cdf008f2ad70526cd31\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782511625 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782511625 -0700\n\n[codex] group blocking and postmerge CI workflows (#30146)\n\n## Why\n\nIt's hard to change the set of required jobs when they're managed in the\nGitHub UI, and when each workflow is responsible for choosing it's own\nscheduling it's easy to end up with skew between what we enforce on PRs\nvs. on main.\n\n## What\n\n- add a `blocking-ci` caller workflow, triggered by pull requests and\npushes to `main`, for Bazel, blob size, cargo-deny, Codespell,\n`repo-checks`, rust CI, and SDK CI\n- add an `always()` terminal job named `CI required` that fails unless\nevery called workflow succeeds\n- add a `postmerge-ci` caller workflow for `rust-ci-full` and\n`v8-canary`, with a terminal `Postmerge CI results` job\n- centralize V8 relevance detection in `v8_canary_changes.py`; unrelated\nPR and postmerge runs execute metadata only and skip the expensive build\nmatrices\n- leave `v8-canary` outside the blocking gate and leave the external\n`cla` check independent\n\n## Rollout\n\nA repository admin must replace the existing required GitHub Actions\ncontexts with `CI required` in the main-branch ruleset. Retain `cla` as\na separate required check. Until that change is coordinated, this PR\ncannot satisfy the old standalone check names. In-flight PRs will need\nto be rebased after this lands.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T22:07:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1168254bd9366faab73835a2cf8eb43d00acad78","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1168254bd9366faab73835a2cf8eb43d00acad78","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1168254bd9366faab73835a2cf8eb43d00acad78/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6509f3148a248f5da6c03cdf008f2ad70526cd31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6509f3148a248f5da6c03cdf008f2ad70526cd31","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6509f3148a248f5da6c03cdf008f2ad70526cd31"}]},{"sha":"6509f3148a248f5da6c03cdf008f2ad70526cd31","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY1MDlmMzE0OGEyNDhmNWRhNmMwM2NkZjAwOGYyYWQ3MDUyNmNkMzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T21:24:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T21:24:46Z"},"message":"[codex] Support npm marketplace plugin sources (#29375)\n\n## Why\n\nMarketplace source deserialization treated `{\"source\":\"npm\", ...}` as\nunsupported. The loader logged and skipped the entry, so npm-backed\nplugins never appeared in `plugin list --available` and `plugin add`\nreturned \"plugin not found\".\n\nCodex plugins are installed from a plugin root, not from an npm\ndependency tree. For npm-backed marketplace entries, Codex should fetch\nthe published package contents without running package scripts or\ninstalling unrelated dependencies.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `npm` marketplace plugin sources with `package`, optional semver\n`version` or version range, and optional HTTPS `registry`.\n- Reject unsafe npm source fields before materialization, including\ninvalid package names, non-semver version selectors, plaintext or\ncredential-bearing registry URLs, and registry query/fragment data.\n- Materialize npm plugins with `npm pack --ignore-scripts`, then unpack\nthe resulting tarball through the existing hardened plugin bundle\nextractor.\n- Enforce npm archive and extracted-size limits, require the standard\nnpm `package/` archive root, and verify the extracted `package.json`\nname matches the requested package before installing.\n- Keep plugin listings, install-source descriptions, CLI JSON/human\noutput, app-server v2 `PluginSource`, TUI source summaries, regenerated\nschema fixtures, and app-server documentation in sync.\n\n## Impact\n\nMarketplaces can distribute Codex plugins from public or configured\nprivate HTTPS npm registries using the same install flow as existing\nmaterialized plugin sources. `npm` must be available on `PATH` when an\nnpm-backed plugin is installed.\n\nFixes #27831\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server -p codex-cli`\n  - npm/schema/core-plugin coverage passed in the run.\n- The full focused command finished with `1739 passed`, `11 failed`, and\n`6 timed out`; the failures were unrelated local app-server environment\nfailures from `sandbox-exec: sandbox_apply: Operation not permitted`\nplus one missing `test_stdio_server` helper binary.\n- Installed an npm-published Codex plugin package through a throwaway\nlocal marketplace and throwaway `CODEX_HOME` to exercise the real npm\nmaterialization path end to end.","tree":{"sha":"e59a62aa579b743e6d5a1feec7473f4f3c660955","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e59a62aa579b743e6d5a1feec7473f4f3c660955"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6509f3148a248f5da6c03cdf008f2ad70526cd31","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPu4eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARPMQAHzTNkf8Ynv6kiRWRR1GE10d\n/6i545XnDMmNCZlQl+J9u7tmnJAaT4dpmI/Ae/+dNdWSx9RL0wMWwmhpZcxRqI0X\ntCrGBJEGs/T3HAIZModOyj09Ye7E5pACdIdW4rjrS/T/m6wNhGenLa+5eElnSUym\nJMKZzDDSu273sQWZ/debLq5VDQT1IhfVCKBFvkcW6rYxDzjS1dxkApXqoSNExH6M\nXpGm8422xKYHw3NBDg5XppKglKlb9ZkyNwtmjmiuS46kBzQwKLdTqHRn1dyv6aui\n9G+TzZljJaEPp8xO1Hu41WFXxD+TObyol8R57IXdUqZBylwXYLDe7J+2oREi1eYs\nKqTkP9fccbRrkC61ncelh+cNb+GEVEibu503ayLZZjq0amXgQBJekHOOxQfMdxlj\nbOJeCMsnA9iTbOyO0HSEehTOQ4z2u0LkpZ/vbbFZpfLIN5Lpp9g+d1lr5k44uqVV\nEqSAibaDLAdzXumj1BZlFi3qUH0WBJMTQAyGqU691uZDOOgLtCuvzBqPTFGY2aca\nLWubESPrJMj+5mgblNsL5JJM/kSGDT3djvluNOohILvbdPN5lOmJhoLBR30eswg5\n3intCtS0vED0HIJ2pBaoN4eZGSPO/IhtFZGWoK8ndoigJoL0/9Ge+lgc2aPlTRYl\nAZCV//mZRXjh2MA7WHdC\n=X6Jv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e59a62aa579b743e6d5a1feec7473f4f3c660955\nparent 526f495f3a904e29ec1d07a927992c904c8a1f5c\nauthor charlesgong-openai <charlesgong@openai.com> 1782509086 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782509086 -0400\n\n[codex] Support npm marketplace plugin sources (#29375)\n\n## Why\n\nMarketplace source deserialization treated `{\"source\":\"npm\", ...}` as\nunsupported. The loader logged and skipped the entry, so npm-backed\nplugins never appeared in `plugin list --available` and `plugin add`\nreturned \"plugin not found\".\n\nCodex plugins are installed from a plugin root, not from an npm\ndependency tree. For npm-backed marketplace entries, Codex should fetch\nthe published package contents without running package scripts or\ninstalling unrelated dependencies.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `npm` marketplace plugin sources with `package`, optional semver\n`version` or version range, and optional HTTPS `registry`.\n- Reject unsafe npm source fields before materialization, including\ninvalid package names, non-semver version selectors, plaintext or\ncredential-bearing registry URLs, and registry query/fragment data.\n- Materialize npm plugins with `npm pack --ignore-scripts`, then unpack\nthe resulting tarball through the existing hardened plugin bundle\nextractor.\n- Enforce npm archive and extracted-size limits, require the standard\nnpm `package/` archive root, and verify the extracted `package.json`\nname matches the requested package before installing.\n- Keep plugin listings, install-source descriptions, CLI JSON/human\noutput, app-server v2 `PluginSource`, TUI source summaries, regenerated\nschema fixtures, and app-server documentation in sync.\n\n## Impact\n\nMarketplaces can distribute Codex plugins from public or configured\nprivate HTTPS npm registries using the same install flow as existing\nmaterialized plugin sources. `npm` must be available on `PATH` when an\nnpm-backed plugin is installed.\n\nFixes #27831\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server -p codex-cli`\n  - npm/schema/core-plugin coverage passed in the run.\n- The full focused command finished with `1739 passed`, `11 failed`, and\n`6 timed out`; the failures were unrelated local app-server environment\nfailures from `sandbox-exec: sandbox_apply: Operation not permitted`\nplus one missing `test_stdio_server` helper binary.\n- Installed an npm-published Codex plugin package through a throwaway\nlocal marketplace and throwaway `CODEX_HOME` to exercise the real npm\nmaterialization path end to end.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:24:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6509f3148a248f5da6c03cdf008f2ad70526cd31","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6509f3148a248f5da6c03cdf008f2ad70526cd31","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6509f3148a248f5da6c03cdf008f2ad70526cd31/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"526f495f3a904e29ec1d07a927992c904c8a1f5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/526f495f3a904e29ec1d07a927992c904c8a1f5c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/526f495f3a904e29ec1d07a927992c904c8a1f5c"}]},{"sha":"526f495f3a904e29ec1d07a927992c904c8a1f5c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUyNmY0OTVmM2E5MDRlMjllYzFkMDdhOTI3OTkyYzkwNGM4YTFmNWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"felixxia-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T21:11:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T21:11:13Z"},"message":"[codex] Classify nested MCP authentication startup errors (#30257)\n\n## Summary\n\n- classify authentication-required RMCP startup failures, including\nerrors nested inside `ClientInitializeError::TransportError`\n- let `codex-mcp` consume that classification so the existing\n`reauthenticationRequired` startup failure reason is emitted\n- add a regression test that performs real startup with an expired\npersisted OAuth token and no refresh token\n\n## Why\n\nFollow-up to #29877.\n\nRMCP stores streamable HTTP initialization failures inside a dynamic\ntransport error whose payload is not exposed through the standard Rust\nerror source chain. The original `anyhow::Error::chain()` check\ntherefore missed the nested `AuthError::AuthorizationRequired` seen\nduring real MCP startup and emitted `failureReason: null`.\n\nThe transport-specific inspection now lives in `codex-rmcp-client`,\nwhile `codex-mcp` consumes only the domain-level authentication-required\nresult. This classifier does not distinguish first-time login from\nreauthentication; the existing auth-state logic remains responsible for\nthat distinction.\n\n## User impact\n\nWhen stored MCP OAuth credentials are expired and cannot be refreshed,\napp clients now receive `failureReason: \"reauthenticationRequired\"` on\nthe failed startup update and can show the reconnect action. First-time\nlogin and unrelated startup failures remain unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client --test streamable_http_oauth_startup\nidentifies_expired_unrefreshable_token_startup_error`\n- `just test -p codex-mcp\nstartup_outcome_error_identifies_authentication_required`\n- `just test -p codex-mcp\nmcp_startup_failure_reason_requires_existing_oauth_and_auth_failure`\n- `cargo build -p codex-cli --bin codex`\n- local app-server probe emitted `failureReason:\n\"reauthenticationRequired\"`\n- manual end-to-end reconnect flow confirmed\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"3fdfbe01e3d9c7f754019dc5b07c38a2fa39336e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3fdfbe01e3d9c7f754019dc5b07c38a2fa39336e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/526f495f3a904e29ec1d07a927992c904c8a1f5c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPurxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj2oQAKpHTSRta6ESFmwUQoabdZ2p\nPEFTWmrBcVTuYr8tx+5jxyx040Rp0lT9R+WgX6q2UGZlXL+5WcOPU5Qv6CLHRGn+\nmQs/mkCUqOZoMweUT5Rzj4ZD9LsqWC6svtBaxbE5691ik5jp/H8Tbl6r7LlVkyjQ\nuSx/yK6fwsBRRLPPDyi3IYJ8aaqkzkFjUcKzQ7I/1eZN45nN7VlMr+V+FrFMijTT\nn/FMEp3iHFZWB67i73uWSzn0kJBRjlXgxtbwX/+QpnOf1GsCA6Yc9uWA74c4sFwi\n5IhfanBomz7nODQ5wBLT/UwWI+da4BqWuWSRpR+IDZQiFn3U70f1WzZzomo4amT2\n4XAEzJyuCZJAM8yLjgvoTSnf5eFCLbm4JV7ZTYt0MjEu5ouxB1pmKuIkxn5PFDgx\nfRJR9MERTvxZQZbdszmmdY9BLqk65PJrqMrZESlwSMp5VR0LFhk6Wg8qHhw0FIQG\njD33jJu2OY6VdbCrhAyRGh370O8jUSp2SHzhsP9yYz9iMdl3yVNodWmejYniKjtA\n35+tbMJQ2d47OoFyp+g1qWlRpiLdj9tMf4j4vmgkAf6sR3vDpq7Zrsu+YXV5m5/t\nk5DnOl4TREytjZtHEr9dqeNFceOmJzbQmQc4VYGBwRPA0Ah9bF3qxpeiaWucnpX9\npaZn9qYG6oppcsHir9Tk\n=TU1Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3fdfbe01e3d9c7f754019dc5b07c38a2fa39336e\nparent c55ce3b51bc3b8bb2805cbee0afc1a8c6e1e7ee2\nauthor felixxia-oai <felixxia@openai.com> 1782508273 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782508273 -0700\n\n[codex] Classify nested MCP authentication startup errors (#30257)\n\n## Summary\n\n- classify authentication-required RMCP startup failures, including\nerrors nested inside `ClientInitializeError::TransportError`\n- let `codex-mcp` consume that classification so the existing\n`reauthenticationRequired` startup failure reason is emitted\n- add a regression test that performs real startup with an expired\npersisted OAuth token and no refresh token\n\n## Why\n\nFollow-up to #29877.\n\nRMCP stores streamable HTTP initialization failures inside a dynamic\ntransport error whose payload is not exposed through the standard Rust\nerror source chain. The original `anyhow::Error::chain()` check\ntherefore missed the nested `AuthError::AuthorizationRequired` seen\nduring real MCP startup and emitted `failureReason: null`.\n\nThe transport-specific inspection now lives in `codex-rmcp-client`,\nwhile `codex-mcp` consumes only the domain-level authentication-required\nresult. This classifier does not distinguish first-time login from\nreauthentication; the existing auth-state logic remains responsible for\nthat distinction.\n\n## User impact\n\nWhen stored MCP OAuth credentials are expired and cannot be refreshed,\napp clients now receive `failureReason: \"reauthenticationRequired\"` on\nthe failed startup update and can show the reconnect action. First-time\nlogin and unrelated startup failures remain unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client --test streamable_http_oauth_startup\nidentifies_expired_unrefreshable_token_startup_error`\n- `just test -p codex-mcp\nstartup_outcome_error_identifies_authentication_required`\n- `just test -p codex-mcp\nmcp_startup_failure_reason_requires_existing_oauth_and_auth_failure`\n- `cargo build -p codex-cli --bin codex`\n- local app-server probe emitted `failureReason:\n\"reauthenticationRequired\"`\n- manual end-to-end reconnect flow confirmed\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:11:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/526f495f3a904e29ec1d07a927992c904c8a1f5c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/526f495f3a904e29ec1d07a927992c904c8a1f5c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/526f495f3a904e29ec1d07a927992c904c8a1f5c/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c55ce3b51bc3b8bb2805cbee0afc1a8c6e1e7ee2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c55ce3b51bc3b8bb2805cbee0afc1a8c6e1e7ee2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c55ce3b51bc3b8bb2805cbee0afc1a8c6e1e7ee2"}]},{"sha":"c55ce3b51bc3b8bb2805cbee0afc1a8c6e1e7ee2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM1NWNlM2I1MWJjM2I4YmIyODA1Y2JlZTBhZmMxYThjNmUxZTdlZTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Abdulrahman Alfozan","email":"alfozan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T20:56:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T20:56:17Z"},"message":"Close thread persistence when submission channel closes (#30173)\n\n### Summary\n\nRelease live thread persistence when a session ends because its\nsubmission channel closes. This prevents a later same-process resume\nfrom failing with `thread ... already has a live local writer`.\n\n### Details\n\nThe issue is in the `codex-core` session teardown path used by Codex\nhosts, rather than in Managed Agents API or exec-server itself.\n\nExplicit shutdown already closes the `LiveThread`, which releases the\nprocess-scoped writer held by `LocalThreadStore`. The\nsubmission-channel-close fallback ran runtime and extension teardown but\nskipped that persistence shutdown, leaving the thread ID registered as\nhaving a live writer.\n\nThis change:\n\n- closes the `LiveThread` on the channel-close fallback path;\n- preserves the existing teardown order used by explicit shutdowns;\n- extends the lifecycle regression test to assert that the thread store\nreceives `shutdown_thread`.\n\nContext: [original\nreport](https://openai.slack.com/archives/C0B4NBHQGTV/p1782136364948039),\n[recent occurrence\n1](https://openai.slack.com/archives/C0B4NBHQGTV/p1782434817895839?thread_ts=1782136364.948039&cid=C0B4NBHQGTV),\n[recent occurrence\n2](https://openai.slack.com/archives/C0B4NBHQGTV/p1782335107474429?thread_ts=1782136364.948039&cid=C0B4NBHQGTV)\n\n### Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsubmission_loop_channel_close_runs_full_thread_teardown`\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib` (1,989 passed; 3 skipped)\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- Native code review: no findings\n\nI also attempted `just test -p codex-core`. The new regression passed;\n79 unrelated integration tests failed in the local harness, primarily\nbecause helper binaries such as `test_stdio_server` were unavailable,\nplus local proxy/shell timing failures.","tree":{"sha":"d69471ff5bbfd1aaf56da76e96b4674ef107f90e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d69471ff5bbfd1aaf56da76e96b4674ef107f90e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c55ce3b51bc3b8bb2805cbee0afc1a8c6e1e7ee2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPudxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmUMQAJpCAH5+lZP9Fk+Jqtj6c5WO\nCdxo4qNxtI3kH/bW99mbKJVbqK5vx2kK4z4FFp0EY8kq6ZawvccSszqVBTV0ZZfo\nHNod2vCmc05lZ2GJnINlnZg39zrj9/4G8gBPcXkHlWPpkJozvrbbmdkBWN/LVfVT\nMrMC7QS9Ed89f4yfECsp3KRjffN17hMiqdz/RhFRNLeCrxu+4CgfEDcQDH5z65Ti\nVs95/5fTjOvZkOFgKoNys40prA2bYS25vUv/L9IGF4Ce4z5wkZBXKn2TuaA70rmO\nmkdogOW4y22/V9r1G8ivE/AzE/yN1ryyciis3GsCGy0UookoFxOkEcavFCpUIvcK\nx+yG96THTYKIAahU51A9zZ/Qsb/e/PGWZExa+ppnjDGqk59VDwgbo+jvg4SS7Cvk\n4f8Bc/432v9H4aHxSuQfCzOjrqgFZl+rBloHhLE/U7wKl3PJnMIgNeaB2W/jfr+h\nfWdJD8zntJdtOhf97Bwh8nAKXyeOBR4ZzXjx0ecjAcbKmm/l5aek/ms51Sh8cyvo\nv8wj8x3DLdAs+mx5Cyq5vW0Frwx1dONAGZid2is2lJuEisjVLF5aQBoQN2z/pL7v\nl8N+eUXVotzDGsM/bYYD11QK6HwWm/w35lEXESyQG68eGhF68ck8+k1Yp8Nvhow+\nJPXI0IaYG2VAbplJexNr\n=uzxx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d69471ff5bbfd1aaf56da76e96b4674ef107f90e\nparent 69596f0e428ae6698b0b9f1174e05bac0a023ded\nauthor Abdulrahman Alfozan <alfozan@openai.com> 1782507377 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782507377 -0700\n\nClose thread persistence when submission channel closes (#30173)\n\n### Summary\n\nRelease live thread persistence when a session ends because its\nsubmission channel closes. This prevents a later same-process resume\nfrom failing with `thread ... already has a live local writer`.\n\n### Details\n\nThe issue is in the `codex-core` session teardown path used by Codex\nhosts, rather than in Managed Agents API or exec-server itself.\n\nExplicit shutdown already closes the `LiveThread`, which releases the\nprocess-scoped writer held by `LocalThreadStore`. The\nsubmission-channel-close fallback ran runtime and extension teardown but\nskipped that persistence shutdown, leaving the thread ID registered as\nhaving a live writer.\n\nThis change:\n\n- closes the `LiveThread` on the channel-close fallback path;\n- preserves the existing teardown order used by explicit shutdowns;\n- extends the lifecycle regression test to assert that the thread store\nreceives `shutdown_thread`.\n\nContext: [original\nreport](https://openai.slack.com/archives/C0B4NBHQGTV/p1782136364948039),\n[recent occurrence\n1](https://openai.slack.com/archives/C0B4NBHQGTV/p1782434817895839?thread_ts=1782136364.948039&cid=C0B4NBHQGTV),\n[recent occurrence\n2](https://openai.slack.com/archives/C0B4NBHQGTV/p1782335107474429?thread_ts=1782136364.948039&cid=C0B4NBHQGTV)\n\n### Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsubmission_loop_channel_close_runs_full_thread_teardown`\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib` (1,989 passed; 3 skipped)\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- Native code review: no findings\n\nI also attempted `just test -p codex-core`. The new regression passed;\n79 unrelated integration tests failed in the local harness, primarily\nbecause helper binaries such as `test_stdio_server` were unavailable,\nplus local proxy/shell timing failures.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T20:56:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c55ce3b51bc3b8bb2805cbee0afc1a8c6e1e7ee2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c55ce3b51bc3b8bb2805cbee0afc1a8c6e1e7ee2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c55ce3b51bc3b8bb2805cbee0afc1a8c6e1e7ee2/comments","author":{"login":"alfozan","id":979984,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3OTk4NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/979984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan","html_url":"https://github.com/alfozan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alfozan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"69596f0e428ae6698b0b9f1174e05bac0a023ded","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/69596f0e428ae6698b0b9f1174e05bac0a023ded","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/69596f0e428ae6698b0b9f1174e05bac0a023ded"}]},{"sha":"69596f0e428ae6698b0b9f1174e05bac0a023ded","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY5NTk2ZjBlNDI4YWU2Njk4YjBiOWYxMTc0ZTA1YmFjMGEwMjNkZWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T20:32:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T20:32:49Z"},"message":"feat: add GPT-5.6 variants to Bedrock catalog (#30285)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add Sol (`openai.gpt-5.6-sol`), Terra (`openai.gpt-5.6-terra`), and\nLuna (`openai.gpt-5.6-luna`) to the Amazon Bedrock static model catalog\n- derive all three entries from the bundled GPT-5.5 metadata and add the\nBedrock-only `max` reasoning effort\n- keep the new entries below the current GPT-5.5 and GPT-5.4 models at\npriorities 2, 3, and 4, preserving GPT-5.5 as the default\n- add deep-equality coverage for inherited model configuration, catalog\nordering, context windows, and service-tier behavior","tree":{"sha":"098d69fae3c3df6d8e86167118e247eae633314f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/098d69fae3c3df6d8e86167118e247eae633314f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/69596f0e428ae6698b0b9f1174e05bac0a023ded","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPuHxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxDQQADA/rJwjqL6s8Grzu/tV7AVU\nHMHwFUvYYNr8JpcytSLe/yEQ3oW48qkZuuK+j182oA7Q9Li+POtbCFRhSpW8ILBR\n9RatPdiCXvcRKraBqkHLP1SpxHJHyInG13opim+opiGZhRQ1f/KpzH04rilSFcju\nt62k3QjU4U4R/n4UitWFhY3khd2GAv5/V7HKCw60eaT8f3n3W9X5bP54Z5XLUPlJ\n60l0GojLzQmow05GI4BOjW/jlVbTek+bFM7FVoCry6DzwUflDf6JWSodqHWngBRI\nXCScGSWf60CRTcHbA6uj9wpREHVdZAv4rl6j+W5tHmVpL0S2hPMNNty/UhKovd7M\n+YWBNysKoZ4VXloU/wxuUkKztbMqtRz5a/PZ7VtUDak79YqRxcQjyi6vRDYyyeZn\nOAAWPIMV97HziuflTrbdtZkCc6mp/dCnZWZdveEmQkkdjalNR6I9blRLGBL41Z7I\n9640W62ktXd4VH36O5fv1BqhyzDEfjbzw0pQ/wiYuFExXoIf0/HfRA/VnnxeTqMi\nsxXOXt1ELfFNVY5t+22lu2dLDQy/yYw5aPsmjrjJcrv6f3CuPT7n4y0mrajUEpMg\nvOcG3R98PoLTU85Gfauoq9yDnO9LzF3yLZduNVDD0+oxbrS2JORsYhdwZcH2mgJZ\n5q1YI0+jiPNASR+6I3Bn\n=LA2z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 098d69fae3c3df6d8e86167118e247eae633314f\nparent ac85409b7b137843e1ec59d9ecaa063e88c60e6c\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1782505969 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782505969 +0000\n\nfeat: add GPT-5.6 variants to Bedrock catalog (#30285)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add Sol (`openai.gpt-5.6-sol`), Terra (`openai.gpt-5.6-terra`), and\nLuna (`openai.gpt-5.6-luna`) to the Amazon Bedrock static model catalog\n- derive all three entries from the bundled GPT-5.5 metadata and add the\nBedrock-only `max` reasoning effort\n- keep the new entries below the current GPT-5.5 and GPT-5.4 models at\npriorities 2, 3, and 4, preserving GPT-5.5 as the default\n- add deep-equality coverage for inherited model configuration, catalog\nordering, context windows, and service-tier behavior","verified_at":"2026-06-26T20:32:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/69596f0e428ae6698b0b9f1174e05bac0a023ded","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/69596f0e428ae6698b0b9f1174e05bac0a023ded","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/69596f0e428ae6698b0b9f1174e05bac0a023ded/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ac85409b7b137843e1ec59d9ecaa063e88c60e6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ac85409b7b137843e1ec59d9ecaa063e88c60e6c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ac85409b7b137843e1ec59d9ecaa063e88c60e6c"}]},{"sha":"ac85409b7b137843e1ec59d9ecaa063e88c60e6c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFjODU0MDliN2IxMzc4NDNlMWVjNTlkOWVjYWEwNjNlODhjNjBlNmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:36:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:36:40Z"},"message":"Let Codex consult user-level code-review-* skills. (#30143)\n\n## Why\n\nI use the `$code-review` skill a lot and it'd be nice to add my own\nadditional review criteria in `$CODEX_HOME/skills/code-review-*`.\n\n## What\n\nRemoves phrasing about \"code-review-* skills in this repository\" which\nin practice seems like enough to get Codex to consult my user-level code\nreview skills in addition to the repo-level ones.","tree":{"sha":"2b6b2ff6b7900eee1c0e968d20b5004868b6dac9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2b6b2ff6b7900eee1c0e968d20b5004868b6dac9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ac85409b7b137843e1ec59d9ecaa063e88c60e6c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPtTICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALWMQAH6GVI1w4g2tSuYxRyoZmZwm\np8vsBZ7o1HNOLs5ZppqLRdnVFrI+gPhtbdvSAXLWqyGPd2S0nWJ2C7gnr1ZDWlf7\nry0KC/gdcwFxhc6eUuFeLvTL08dzN2i5TE0hl8Te5QEOOjwkPnvndiOaQ1x2WKt5\n7zQwPnwHyVQOWWKsGcx9LJ411x6pErSvDn8MPhFav6hFBcc9V3qqaVm9s3UMx0li\nzd4A7BNt3WiQaGKdFH+MahBo+JvfeDH/afRe7B5v8uwLpPWWg9E6wkFkfUDiVjoc\n73DgwoV1ObZzxGo2+8T/BkztkaYVcwn+9JiX3APUvXgvhXoPYXyu9A3M3gJC+96r\nCFGmdIIkqm8fdeTs8IaRj6Gb4s1f3kKP2SHOawt4Qv4mu/Lj2oL7difhw7fb+GCa\nMe0yXWGn3wqsB8ZKCDFBxanXmZ5fTp55ob00R2SPbXjJXbFFrUQg+38jBe8eG63y\nGtw6k7/RkbG10Vr3eRJo8xMOYEKbvM921ydOtBAjVBvpgOmjY7ZaF4liE/8QcCia\ni562LjCyuU8TglbGXRbJFD26izK9CO+466ZwdFrjqAb7cYB6bN/dCsVr+0NnaVVH\nhz9stMHYZtWoCIo6ys5PJpxL8L7B+v384pDfVy7xpH7hbr7N00mkea/IVv2lgpV5\n888Osjy7tvfcjASSmMPq\n=n3Ld\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2b6b2ff6b7900eee1c0e968d20b5004868b6dac9\nparent f72976a5f1e5bba3e1af18cc2ddffedfb2687376\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782502600 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782502600 -0700\n\nLet Codex consult user-level code-review-* skills. (#30143)\n\n## Why\n\nI use the `$code-review` skill a lot and it'd be nice to add my own\nadditional review criteria in `$CODEX_HOME/skills/code-review-*`.\n\n## What\n\nRemoves phrasing about \"code-review-* skills in this repository\" which\nin practice seems like enough to get Codex to consult my user-level code\nreview skills in addition to the repo-level ones.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T19:36:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ac85409b7b137843e1ec59d9ecaa063e88c60e6c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ac85409b7b137843e1ec59d9ecaa063e88c60e6c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ac85409b7b137843e1ec59d9ecaa063e88c60e6c/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f72976a5f1e5bba3e1af18cc2ddffedfb2687376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f72976a5f1e5bba3e1af18cc2ddffedfb2687376","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f72976a5f1e5bba3e1af18cc2ddffedfb2687376"}]},{"sha":"f72976a5f1e5bba3e1af18cc2ddffedfb2687376","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY3Mjk3NmE1ZjFlNWJiYTNlMWFmMThjYzJkZGZmZWRmYjI2ODczNzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:35:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:35:54Z"},"message":"feat(app-server): add optional turn_id to thread/fork (#30277)\n\n## Description\n\nThis adds stable optional `turnId` support to `thread/fork`. When\nsupplied, the fork copies persisted history through that terminal turn,\ninclusive, and drops later turns from the new thread.\n\nOmitting or passing `null` preserves the existing full-history fork\nbehavior, including the interruption marker when the stored source\nhistory ends mid-turn.\n\n## Why\n\nWe're deprecating `thread/rollback` and this will help certain UX use\ncases work around it by using `thread/fork` + `turn_id` instead.","tree":{"sha":"e292e0c2f3e25d5f3cae58d6b6c721ed5abc2248","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e292e0c2f3e25d5f3cae58d6b6c721ed5abc2248"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f72976a5f1e5bba3e1af18cc2ddffedfb2687376","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPtSaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU44QAFoY6+6Kp9KndX94RF+nVN3l\n4AeoQPTdV39fMPRIAb2eGNIccWcQoxbYdkOpZEPUoDqdPV7n5oYsFe8f1HmHDrpn\nyP1AZUhTXPVaUcIq4Ny3PITXfSkWPEoxsEokog7uwmuRmQnmW5KxdaQQxhQhfiB1\nMli28L/ti1VuuWW5nIyhy48FZaCllBYYacc0Oig8cXhebcc5FP5ObcxwSatE9ncT\nuReb/Cp9IuO6p7zSf0BFHqcvFJKsuBWEbtNJH1gJQuVGWnTaHlefvmgGXwXvHJVc\n6wq0XfrLXKwnFmQDYk4EsAjWHhye2jKG2vwwxKIBycmm78YHuaOzKEfbgB/1BWVo\nxfjAwJOuUk0SROo6g/vnvRX0qotXxDGYFgIAB/xP/jqhSiW0qBEmpBQPcWgg4H/G\ndfhxv5G2EdtULUR6hyeSs3mF/4NCpTPgtdmYMJ+0bmZPLe5Uyc99cqrHLed+cmyG\nEZoMFD+k2OwGmmrrjneZmK/5Iux8or426d3GiTmlr5Y5jEf5wHTwz1FMzdHk08Mt\noNY55to6YiVRnDPzDtbrattAhPPxvf3lFpt90Tr1XfL5+7lhPdqM4EpiZlZOZlzz\nB+PZX3GRd6vwlFj/WhEe7mDhWOo74+/NI/cjAjG7p1v8IJJ6c7tSVr/TI6BvIner\nLFq6M5TbuEw+LtZ6mK+Q\n=dYvd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e292e0c2f3e25d5f3cae58d6b6c721ed5abc2248\nparent 812cd2bb57ddb3a04a10d59495ac0212d2eb52a3\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1782502554 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782502554 +0000\n\nfeat(app-server): add optional turn_id to thread/fork (#30277)\n\n## Description\n\nThis adds stable optional `turnId` support to `thread/fork`. When\nsupplied, the fork copies persisted history through that terminal turn,\ninclusive, and drops later turns from the new thread.\n\nOmitting or passing `null` preserves the existing full-history fork\nbehavior, including the interruption marker when the stored source\nhistory ends mid-turn.\n\n## Why\n\nWe're deprecating `thread/rollback` and this will help certain UX use\ncases work around it by using `thread/fork` + `turn_id` instead.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T19:35:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f72976a5f1e5bba3e1af18cc2ddffedfb2687376","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f72976a5f1e5bba3e1af18cc2ddffedfb2687376","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f72976a5f1e5bba3e1af18cc2ddffedfb2687376/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"812cd2bb57ddb3a04a10d59495ac0212d2eb52a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/812cd2bb57ddb3a04a10d59495ac0212d2eb52a3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/812cd2bb57ddb3a04a10d59495ac0212d2eb52a3"}]},{"sha":"812cd2bb57ddb3a04a10d59495ac0212d2eb52a3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDgxMmNkMmJiNTdkZGIzYTA0YTEwZDU5NDk1YWMwMjEyZDJlYjUyYTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:32:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:32:31Z"},"message":"ensure thread.history_mode is immutable (#30261)\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR makes `thread.history_mode` immutable after the thread's\ncanonical first `SessionMeta` has been written. Later same-thread\n`SessionMeta` lines are compatibility metadata writes, not a new thread\ndefinition.\n\nWithout this, an older binary could append a `SessionMeta` that omits\n`history_mode`; when a newer binary replays it, serde defaults that\nmissing field to `legacy` and SQLite could downgrade a paginated thread.\n\n## Why\n\n`history_mode` is the persisted thread storage contract.\nPaginated-thread fail-closed behavior and SQLite memory filtering depend\non it staying aligned with canonical rollout metadata, especially when\nmultiple Codex binary versions can touch the same local rollout.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Stop generic rollout metadata replay from overwriting `history_mode`\nfrom later `SessionMeta` items.\n- Remove `history_mode` from `ThreadMetadataPatch`, so mutable metadata\nsync and app-server metadata updates cannot rewrite it.\n- When local metadata sync has to recreate a missing SQLite row, recover\n`history_mode` from the rollout's canonical first `SessionMeta` instead\nof from a mutable patch.\n- Keep the in-memory thread store using the created thread's canonical\n`history_mode` instead of metadata patches.\n- Fill the one remaining core test `CreateThreadParams` initializer with\nthe new `history_mode` field; Bazel CI caught this after the parent\nhistory-mode PR landed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just test -p codex-state\nsession_meta_does_not_set_model_or_reasoning_effort`","tree":{"sha":"738952da04272fbfa8458f1f7efabad69c2f36d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/738952da04272fbfa8458f1f7efabad69c2f36d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/812cd2bb57ddb3a04a10d59495ac0212d2eb52a3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPtPPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtcMQAJhXsYKmNolY0mZ+dzUU242n\nUUz4K1beBnAExGop9Ij69FX4kp8gmSLRVNfFYIlAY7c4Ll66jToh0L/4CPjFAC1T\n94kF+Ed3oT/BMIt6tnhCy3G0N9JIVBaLBTgK2eOS2ZtvIDqiQU/38kLqb6Fqj3WL\nSqSJF38sk2O19s/aMNeexDEwTMLeRZiP93vsh16bQIiFpyMXLKt9CnBeCHPuBOwp\nAue5YUlBSWAGr/uI1ekFZOrLgPE68QkBw0h3JAu68nQIwprl+lW7HinQ/qsrSD5Z\nDCQXPcSS7rm6NBnjvKfDZfZFLIwLKpQR7RuZ2YiwiHrVZVJpIcyhHvNgAG8NOdXy\nUHhcHij3PAPgIQm07Aq/0Mrtvrskz78hfYrSnNClCrL5uZ5s8x/rRxOQhYV3BzxA\nkPrAEv6tmdmipw4YzmnwBj8dgOLLn29e0VVb5AlrE1zq+dc/dxVGRlki8L3zHrq4\npZEhuYigcm9jxQNAg9DRzACZvCEdCUEf9TZL8BmmxPz8n5JC3EsLfUq7OqOA9JEU\nbvlrohFejhW3dnp3K2xE0Ml38Dl5+OCsYu8QXD67Oof7ndelq+6IwhePLrzCoC74\neLoe9u2hlWzyK/EGr7krJtzcfIUeZXEb4f28GOCPUpJjAAD/56C2EcO5Vz6inhTY\nekspgohxrs49xfKwBY+s\n=CDDk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 738952da04272fbfa8458f1f7efabad69c2f36d5\nparent cf36c688b3d5c9122e818a93d272d4024c8a2bae\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1782502351 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782502351 -0700\n\nensure thread.history_mode is immutable (#30261)\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR makes `thread.history_mode` immutable after the thread's\ncanonical first `SessionMeta` has been written. Later same-thread\n`SessionMeta` lines are compatibility metadata writes, not a new thread\ndefinition.\n\nWithout this, an older binary could append a `SessionMeta` that omits\n`history_mode`; when a newer binary replays it, serde defaults that\nmissing field to `legacy` and SQLite could downgrade a paginated thread.\n\n## Why\n\n`history_mode` is the persisted thread storage contract.\nPaginated-thread fail-closed behavior and SQLite memory filtering depend\non it staying aligned with canonical rollout metadata, especially when\nmultiple Codex binary versions can touch the same local rollout.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Stop generic rollout metadata replay from overwriting `history_mode`\nfrom later `SessionMeta` items.\n- Remove `history_mode` from `ThreadMetadataPatch`, so mutable metadata\nsync and app-server metadata updates cannot rewrite it.\n- When local metadata sync has to recreate a missing SQLite row, recover\n`history_mode` from the rollout's canonical first `SessionMeta` instead\nof from a mutable patch.\n- Keep the in-memory thread store using the created thread's canonical\n`history_mode` instead of metadata patches.\n- Fill the one remaining core test `CreateThreadParams` initializer with\nthe new `history_mode` field; Bazel CI caught this after the parent\nhistory-mode PR landed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just test -p codex-state\nsession_meta_does_not_set_model_or_reasoning_effort`","verified_at":"2026-06-26T19:32:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/812cd2bb57ddb3a04a10d59495ac0212d2eb52a3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/812cd2bb57ddb3a04a10d59495ac0212d2eb52a3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/812cd2bb57ddb3a04a10d59495ac0212d2eb52a3/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cf36c688b3d5c9122e818a93d272d4024c8a2bae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cf36c688b3d5c9122e818a93d272d4024c8a2bae","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cf36c688b3d5c9122e818a93d272d4024c8a2bae"}]},{"sha":"cf36c688b3d5c9122e818a93d272d4024c8a2bae","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNmMzZjNjg4YjNkNWM5MTIyZTgxOGE5M2QyNzJkNDAyNGM4YTJiYWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"hefuc-oai","email":"hefuc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:27:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:27:31Z"},"message":"[codex] Use managed defaults for TUI threads (#30147)\n\n## Why\n\n#29683 exposes managed defaults for new-thread model settings through\n`configRequirements/read` without applying them server-wide. The TUI is\nan app-server client, so it should explicitly consume those defaults\nwhen it creates a fresh thread.\n\nThis lets plain `codex` start on the managed model while preserving the\nexisting ability to change model settings within the thread.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Read `requirements.models.newThread` during TUI app-server bootstrap.\n- Apply the managed model, reasoning effort, and service tier to the\ninitial fresh thread and subsequent `/new` or `/clear` threads.\n- Keep explicit launch overrides above the managed defaults.\n- Normalize the managed `fast` service tier to the `priority` request\nvalue.\n- Leave resumed and forked threads unchanged.\n\nThe application logic lives in a small TUI-only module; app-server\n`thread/start` behavior remains unchanged for other clients.\n\n## User experience\n\n- Plain `codex` starts with the managed new-thread settings.\n- A user can still change settings with `/model` or the existing\nservice-tier controls.\n- Starting another fresh thread reapplies the managed defaults.\n- Explicit launch choices such as `codex -m <model>` continue to win.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui managed_new_thread_defaults`\n- `just fix -p codex-tui`\n\nDepends on #29683.","tree":{"sha":"f22905b495a8ba02f77b02b64d7b72ed88896a83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f22905b495a8ba02f77b02b64d7b72ed88896a83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cf36c688b3d5c9122e818a93d272d4024c8a2bae","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPtKjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoowQADfja2h6Hir2uxadIheDmJ1L\ni4XtaDLGopvaiPzJpFfGojt9gWcwjpT3MeloHjdjJvAb3+onxf6uaN3zuSo7QA/n\nV1MV85lyRy9OjzILQkAYive14nwGlPMBFevecioBhd3iA/9B/ePIAKzjH6Thu+ks\noM/qbKiJWWVt7d2WIRLAEXRKQwZ+XeWx9xIkMvoAOsjJlIwHZcw8e32w79dCLlG6\neujA4Z5jkjWBEkw/HRVYd6VIF8NhOE86CQwWsBNO55nc7dB37gznx0wifR3s3XKP\ncM2YtFKLpB2eWTb+It0iQLZy0vtWW1KYqM8+h6qc5jMQ8OXGphebjPLvLG3eEDW1\nNbtZeK55AiIUUc2xLeCR20YV5SDhuIFy+HkogBdVLl0ec54Mk9MT5xIaC9Sg3QPs\nc5d7V2UHEpoDUOBGDaC90XJO6YDp4tg5UR1NdzLRrp2feiac1braai4rfxRN7Lk+\n2LPdLSjTD29VuwbDmB2mCz7b1N6KhYaWrDR/eXMp4tVOl4yUtwJydHFJR1eMKGYk\nXOtzuPayXt/5WqLpubklC+MyTozfpFMJn4c7sNfhDtdiDpWXncFKL3bkDXw5s2z6\nFo70/x59/V5PBKM9ZSH6K8+ZeRX/4bjcTEPIw276bPRowqWsGIcFJfUQhKMDc1NZ\nPF0AHD+wM//HbynyeeDi\n=gpqO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f22905b495a8ba02f77b02b64d7b72ed88896a83\nparent 79a8ffdbf7ca08820e0b44cab0261eb61ff72465\nauthor hefuc-oai <hefuc@openai.com> 1782502051 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782502051 +0000\n\n[codex] Use managed defaults for TUI threads (#30147)\n\n## Why\n\n#29683 exposes managed defaults for new-thread model settings through\n`configRequirements/read` without applying them server-wide. The TUI is\nan app-server client, so it should explicitly consume those defaults\nwhen it creates a fresh thread.\n\nThis lets plain `codex` start on the managed model while preserving the\nexisting ability to change model settings within the thread.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Read `requirements.models.newThread` during TUI app-server bootstrap.\n- Apply the managed model, reasoning effort, and service tier to the\ninitial fresh thread and subsequent `/new` or `/clear` threads.\n- Keep explicit launch overrides above the managed defaults.\n- Normalize the managed `fast` service tier to the `priority` request\nvalue.\n- Leave resumed and forked threads unchanged.\n\nThe application logic lives in a small TUI-only module; app-server\n`thread/start` behavior remains unchanged for other clients.\n\n## User experience\n\n- Plain `codex` starts with the managed new-thread settings.\n- A user can still change settings with `/model` or the existing\nservice-tier controls.\n- Starting another fresh thread reapplies the managed defaults.\n- Explicit launch choices such as `codex -m <model>` continue to win.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui managed_new_thread_defaults`\n- `just fix -p codex-tui`\n\nDepends on #29683.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T19:27:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cf36c688b3d5c9122e818a93d272d4024c8a2bae","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cf36c688b3d5c9122e818a93d272d4024c8a2bae","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cf36c688b3d5c9122e818a93d272d4024c8a2bae/comments","author":{"login":"hefuc-oai","id":289792942,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUXjrg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289792942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/hefuc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"79a8ffdbf7ca08820e0b44cab0261eb61ff72465","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/79a8ffdbf7ca08820e0b44cab0261eb61ff72465","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/79a8ffdbf7ca08820e0b44cab0261eb61ff72465"}]},{"sha":"79a8ffdbf7ca08820e0b44cab0261eb61ff72465","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc5YThmZmRiZjdjYTA4ODIwZTBiNDRjYWIwMjYxZWI2MWZmNzI0NjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Charles Du","email":"charlesdu@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:17:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T19:17:26Z"},"message":"[codex] allow AGENTS.md and skills to authorize delegation (#30274)\n\nPrompt update of MAv2 to include agents.md and skills more explicitly\n\nshould mimic: https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27919","tree":{"sha":"b42465e9889500b5fa8aaa5d8441e04aa2944fb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b42465e9889500b5fa8aaa5d8441e04aa2944fb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/79a8ffdbf7ca08820e0b44cab0261eb61ff72465","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPtBGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyygQAINxM0ZKqw6yBlVgSdRsqS/s\nVzfuxjmmgETGhCGNWmP5zBhNdWl2s9M44TPFxWpLsQ5FJJXPu+jBX122UvWANEW0\nFviKBRI6ZwC9pz0Kwdl6Ed6MGfBiW7lBkeep1UaWM9p75XaduhPo8m2ss0igVz8P\n1IEoov407MB451lC+O/1XI859NsQ8VX4MFvTnhJGZ6Rc0D1eM3c//40qDuaMWeuk\neL7Dcg817yuqdlOvf/RQFZ7PXYjbYQBtjwt1p8CJ2nj9iG0bAteUWSvypXlvxSna\nEEpL7/iqfDgRef4cUffqH7AdFtoS1FYSshoNaVxzTtB1erzAuwl28LjGemBmIYMA\nzZduQOuu2UvjP/x7WwMcRDxisgHPDrcdAqA1urMnwQZbkIZnpPvgxAEmY3Dv/4kq\nEnqlMiRRJY41ASzI8/AeqUn+XYKtUkUqDDqQ5QuNfYt/A3FDUNaWpLoX7Y/NxnZk\n8nEWZOb5ZaDxq2avGo5p6+B8sVTiOdGe+cwSNxhBjitcy3YyF94WDW1DaHPunoIb\nmXOgQlvLgG6OJ1s+uabi1CiI9QBIaavPVclvWKTQgrIpXv0Yh9Oh2O65SG5f4VYD\noCokfVkhqrM9IeNtD9vzsDlNsOy1jyaN+AimNjpGM8W064iKfFgC17XFJcJoJZi0\nwS5q4qhQRPf/MKQDT24k\n=L+Qh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b42465e9889500b5fa8aaa5d8441e04aa2944fb1\nparent a938d5f6071f0430b1ed05e381ad9239baeb26f7\nauthor Charles Du <charlesdu@openai.com> 1782501446 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782501446 -0700\n\n[codex] allow AGENTS.md and skills to authorize delegation (#30274)\n\nPrompt update of MAv2 to include agents.md and skills more explicitly\n\nshould mimic: https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27919","verified_at":"2026-06-26T19:17:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/79a8ffdbf7ca08820e0b44cab0261eb61ff72465","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/79a8ffdbf7ca08820e0b44cab0261eb61ff72465","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/79a8ffdbf7ca08820e0b44cab0261eb61ff72465/comments","author":{"login":"charlesdu-openai","id":179633612,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrT9zA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179633612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesdu-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesdu-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a938d5f6071f0430b1ed05e381ad9239baeb26f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a938d5f6071f0430b1ed05e381ad9239baeb26f7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a938d5f6071f0430b1ed05e381ad9239baeb26f7"}]},{"sha":"a938d5f6071f0430b1ed05e381ad9239baeb26f7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE5MzhkNWY2MDcxZjA0MzBiMWVkMDVlMzgxYWQ5MjM5YmFlYjI2Zjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T18:37:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T18:37:59Z"},"message":"Overlap executor skill reads with namespace discovery (#30225)\n\n## Why\n\nEnvironment skill discovery needs two independent pieces of information:\n\n- plugin namespaces from `plugin.json` files; and\n- skill metadata from each `SKILL.md` file.\n\nToday these happen in sequence. Codex waits for every plugin namespace\nlookup to finish before it starts reading any skill files. On a remote\nexecutor, that creates an avoidable network-latency barrier.\n\n```text\nbefore: walk -> namespace lookups -> skill reads -> build catalog\nafter:  walk -> namespace lookups ─┐\n             -> skill reads ───────┴-> build catalog\n```\n\n## What changes\n\n- Read and parse skill files without waiting for plugin namespace\ndiscovery.\n- Resolve root and nested plugin namespaces concurrently.\n- Join both results only when constructing the final qualified skill\nnames.\n- Keep the existing 64-skill concurrency bound, output ordering,\nwarnings, metadata behavior, and namespace rules.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe regression test makes plugin manifest lookup wait until a `SKILL.md`\nread has started. The old serialized pipeline would time out; the new\npipeline completes and still returns the correctly namespaced skill.\n\n`just test -p codex-core-skills` passes all 111 tests.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThis does not add an exec-server endpoint, batch filesystem calls, or\nreduce the number of files transferred. A frontmatter-only read or\nserver-side skill catalog can remain a separate follow-up if benchmarks\nshow that transferred bytes are the next bottleneck.","tree":{"sha":"8ffa5968521a7a83df350c041239cda3b36d37f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8ffa5968521a7a83df350c041239cda3b36d37f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a938d5f6071f0430b1ed05e381ad9239baeb26f7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPscHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA69MQADKXYpRHqQyxfue/1mBXtStS\n49UiFjkik5Lr0dplHTpQ1IfiSM2gbo+do/63+pAAD3pnT6W+iWEuRdhEpZeLsXnc\nTUA4gIfPFauTaedcZBLA+oX8VuMsFY/hHfjldD845QbweQY/GUVrXxOszeXb67FC\nxdpWStkjqPXzpvoaIGQTeCbYdfn5IsCBmjVQk5OQSmvezfpFI2SKbTDGBmcTueoA\n0Zuw2RtTzWrLZfoSvPvAKZ3wBtLQtLW3vQUwwbssDJtWrwvwsT/j9zIaSJz3Sp3D\nUdm4Pym1ZsFqtCo/b7fHV9qnGSo0fOP9J6aCj+hKtByHnlteXexsnl2eANg07uvi\nfGTewPTjb5yP3F591V/XWKLPfUIemMp+3qjG22qLUGdbTgYRqiCC2TjKaVKwU9mS\nHyzyg3V1Zo2stPc3XV4i7BlAA8bzjI2jAOe+Ior5eAh0o10CyQhhtFlPpsTHwX/+\n5VIiJz84NW+Qv0ydTbPimEC+FuzlLF0+jutoz2lMKuEkSi3SNamYAXkBRyrfQBn/\nGajxVAZQzWXwkHj4KeolTV1RVgjA+clWsOGUFjiAoEm5WovFEcwYyVjRaqEYquH5\nnC7rZOWip7+UxVDqjMDWxk6vpmNRiYt9HoGABtlGAXnlhJ+Z7nVj9IWxPmsFFsIl\ndBYWBcAnYTflYOEU8E+W\n=3BYg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8ffa5968521a7a83df350c041239cda3b36d37f9\nparent d9cf931d0eafa18f4fdfc7ab8c9c241b48df3216\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782499079 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782499079 +0000\n\nOverlap executor skill reads with namespace discovery (#30225)\n\n## Why\n\nEnvironment skill discovery needs two independent pieces of information:\n\n- plugin namespaces from `plugin.json` files; and\n- skill metadata from each `SKILL.md` file.\n\nToday these happen in sequence. Codex waits for every plugin namespace\nlookup to finish before it starts reading any skill files. On a remote\nexecutor, that creates an avoidable network-latency barrier.\n\n```text\nbefore: walk -> namespace lookups -> skill reads -> build catalog\nafter:  walk -> namespace lookups ─┐\n             -> skill reads ───────┴-> build catalog\n```\n\n## What changes\n\n- Read and parse skill files without waiting for plugin namespace\ndiscovery.\n- Resolve root and nested plugin namespaces concurrently.\n- Join both results only when constructing the final qualified skill\nnames.\n- Keep the existing 64-skill concurrency bound, output ordering,\nwarnings, metadata behavior, and namespace rules.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe regression test makes plugin manifest lookup wait until a `SKILL.md`\nread has started. The old serialized pipeline would time out; the new\npipeline completes and still returns the correctly namespaced skill.\n\n`just test -p codex-core-skills` passes all 111 tests.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThis does not add an exec-server endpoint, batch filesystem calls, or\nreduce the number of files transferred. A frontmatter-only read or\nserver-side skill catalog can remain a separate follow-up if benchmarks\nshow that transferred bytes are the next bottleneck.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T18:38:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a938d5f6071f0430b1ed05e381ad9239baeb26f7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a938d5f6071f0430b1ed05e381ad9239baeb26f7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a938d5f6071f0430b1ed05e381ad9239baeb26f7/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d9cf931d0eafa18f4fdfc7ab8c9c241b48df3216","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d9cf931d0eafa18f4fdfc7ab8c9c241b48df3216","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d9cf931d0eafa18f4fdfc7ab8c9c241b48df3216"}]},{"sha":"d9cf931d0eafa18f4fdfc7ab8c9c241b48df3216","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ5Y2Y5MzFkMGVhZmExOGY0ZmRmYzdhYjhjOWMyNDFiNDhkZjMyMTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"hefuc-oai","email":"hefuc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T18:37:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T18:37:40Z"},"message":"[codex] Add managed new-thread model settings (#29683)\n\n## Why\n\nAdmins need persistent defaults for the model, reasoning effort, and\nservice tier shown when the Desktop App creates a new thread. These are\ninitialization defaults rather than runtime constraints: the App should\nuse them to initialize its draft while still allowing a user to make an\nexplicit selection.\n\nThe app-server therefore needs to expose the managed values before\nthread creation without changing `thread/start` behavior for other\nclients.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Parse `model`, `model_reasoning_effort`, and `service_tier` from\n`[models.new_thread]` in `requirements.toml`.\n- Compose the `models` requirements through the existing\nrequirements-layer precedence rules.\n- Expose the resolved values through `configRequirements/read` as\n`requirements.models.newThread`.\n- Add the corresponding app-server protocol types and regenerate the\nJSON and TypeScript schema fixtures.\n- Document the new `configRequirements/read` fields in the app-server\nREADME.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR is data plumbing only. It does not apply these values during\n`thread/start` and does not change thread creation for existing\napp-server clients, resumed or forked sessions, internal or subagent\nsessions, `codex exec`, or the TUI. A companion Desktop App change owns\ndraft initialization, sends the effective settings for ordinary and\nprewarmed starts, and preserves explicit user changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Requirements deserialization coverage for `[models.new_thread]`\n- Requirements-layer precedence coverage\n- App-server API mapping coverage\n- `configRequirements/read` integration coverage\n- Regenerated app-server JSON and TypeScript schema fixtures","tree":{"sha":"9a8557d3a62cad8fc191f6442b3bdd3b40fd2953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9a8557d3a62cad8fc191f6442b3bdd3b40fd2953"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d9cf931d0eafa18f4fdfc7ab8c9c241b48df3216","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPsb0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALHwQAIWYwmUjvLLVVsuzWq7k+sP4\nhSlmlqm9JkO6oVBaG1kDLyGlQ/FbiC8GiEChfThlvhzqHgpI0nNgNlErQdQnniOW\nA6PeYY2RiDvBVGxsyXIiOkIvXVGpXajkf5e6h1gVChwBWbmflKwZSsjgQQDv+Xfk\nNCJQbAHWpBrDmmhuIb11Z0ZDO5+NxYye3maFfTSILhM87mXma93rV8N6ed3yYphM\nz6pjagdKPZZ5F07ETXBwTkPZnOSdOUWbGC1ir6iNTefwM4IitSexn0hSEMAztP7c\nMfxz0V2RVpzs3kEWnptzF3Io9oBmSTKUVHvGdz4fAcwauUalhwp2vz0X3UueKFHX\nOdbGZu1f/IiMc/8+mB94GEo/C1jkLjcp9fL1I49fcBIv56IPq5snRrG/4qHmhF8x\nh6PybU2rGEUSnqKdo/he2146lcD9sNnYnJ4/q7X9emXXOrCZaKKRZCdbMGWco4Lc\nIPbru6FfYJtf66BHHiYdXdVV91kxYCFC7PWxQ56T55HAOlAMfDG6GV6wAfpMjix9\nDZwi5H3+qnRi0OGGfF9b3V7A5qfSxfxvArXTo+//Qg8X7sGwdCVQv5A/qtqcBV6h\np784ttkhuYWG0c4psfrGUUeDYSSbW3uuMIpOqbYoTFDsxA3QqL7OtCs9nG0ZGmXL\nyvYI3Yix0JlCvgr4/AvG\n=kAU4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9a8557d3a62cad8fc191f6442b3bdd3b40fd2953\nparent f91334380e46cfd909c3642c1e05d3d8283c40ef\nauthor hefuc-oai <hefuc@openai.com> 1782499060 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782499060 +0000\n\n[codex] Add managed new-thread model settings (#29683)\n\n## Why\n\nAdmins need persistent defaults for the model, reasoning effort, and\nservice tier shown when the Desktop App creates a new thread. These are\ninitialization defaults rather than runtime constraints: the App should\nuse them to initialize its draft while still allowing a user to make an\nexplicit selection.\n\nThe app-server therefore needs to expose the managed values before\nthread creation without changing `thread/start` behavior for other\nclients.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Parse `model`, `model_reasoning_effort`, and `service_tier` from\n`[models.new_thread]` in `requirements.toml`.\n- Compose the `models` requirements through the existing\nrequirements-layer precedence rules.\n- Expose the resolved values through `configRequirements/read` as\n`requirements.models.newThread`.\n- Add the corresponding app-server protocol types and regenerate the\nJSON and TypeScript schema fixtures.\n- Document the new `configRequirements/read` fields in the app-server\nREADME.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR is data plumbing only. It does not apply these values during\n`thread/start` and does not change thread creation for existing\napp-server clients, resumed or forked sessions, internal or subagent\nsessions, `codex exec`, or the TUI. A companion Desktop App change owns\ndraft initialization, sends the effective settings for ordinary and\nprewarmed starts, and preserves explicit user changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Requirements deserialization coverage for `[models.new_thread]`\n- Requirements-layer precedence coverage\n- App-server API mapping coverage\n- `configRequirements/read` integration coverage\n- Regenerated app-server JSON and TypeScript schema fixtures","verified_at":"2026-06-26T18:37:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d9cf931d0eafa18f4fdfc7ab8c9c241b48df3216","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d9cf931d0eafa18f4fdfc7ab8c9c241b48df3216","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d9cf931d0eafa18f4fdfc7ab8c9c241b48df3216/comments","author":{"login":"hefuc-oai","id":289792942,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUXjrg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289792942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/hefuc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f91334380e46cfd909c3642c1e05d3d8283c40ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f91334380e46cfd909c3642c1e05d3d8283c40ef","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f91334380e