l":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"914c8eeb4e41442e04a7706ca1638491ceabf4a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/914c8eeb4e41442e04a7706ca1638491ceabf4a4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/914c8eeb4e41442e04a7706ca1638491ceabf4a4"}]},{"sha":"914c8eeb4e41442e04a7706ca1638491ceabf4a4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkxNGM4ZWViNGU0MTQ0MmUwNGE3NzA2Y2ExNjM4NDkxY2VhYmY0YTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T12:52:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T12:52:04Z"},"message":"[codex] narrow unused skills intro export (#29991)\n\n## Summary\n\n- stop publicly re-exporting the internally used\n`SKILLS_INTRO_WITH_ALIASES` constant\n- keep the constant and all skills rendering behavior unchanged\n- preserve every integration helper, API, fixture, assertion, and module\nused by tests\n\n## Scope guardrails\n\nThis revision keeps all remote/network-facing functionality and every\nline introduced by `jif <jif@openai.com>`.\n\nFollowing the test-preservation audit, it also restores the in-process\nRMCP test transport, the original `codex-mcp` fixture,\n`PluginLoadOutcome::effective_skill_roots` and its assertions, the\n`EffectiveSkillRoots` API family, the test-only apps renderer, and the\nTUI dead-code annotation. Those files now match the PR base exactly.\n\nNo test imports or directly references the remaining public skills\nexport being narrowed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- repository-wide test-reference audit: no test-used code remains\ndeleted or narrowed\n- deleted-line `git blame` audit: zero Jif-authored deletions\n- `cargo test -p codex-core-plugins -p codex-mcp -p codex-rmcp-client\n--lib`: 467 passed\n- `cargo test -p codex-core --lib apps::render`: 2 passed\n- `cargo test -p codex-core-skills --lib render::tests`: 19 passed\n- `cargo check -p codex-core-skills --all-targets`: passed\n- `just fix -p codex-core-skills`: passed\n- `just fmt`: passed\n- `git diff --check`: passed\n\nThe full local `codex-core-skills` suite passed 106/108 tests; two\nloader tests detected an ambient repository skills root outside the\npackage and failed their isolation assertions. The scoped renderer suite\nand all-target compile pass, and CI runs in an isolated environment.\n\nFinal code delta: 1 insertion, 2 deletions across 2 files.","tree":{"sha":"cb3c203c91152642e81e6c7db3e12b69c2e787bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cb3c203c91152642e81e6c7db3e12b69c2e787bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/914c8eeb4e41442e04a7706ca1638491ceabf4a4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPnX0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA78EQAJ9oeIcKiEDBXaEvyERFoXqx\niNaP7KaQhayinSU7xzDT0Bah0j64ofEM0KP4QoT3Gy8s9CYH4xU1plH3hnqYTOBf\n9rX9vvu4a9lg62Tmpviwu9VkUOz1WRrP01DbYyqNJOrhnlxV4G6eZzTX0B6Ym2/H\nWFqqreplTPdfn8E1ZPgE3Jy9n0kNCxOMDhd+X18fUz1ni/Kxm2c6x1croKh4k1U0\nYtV1p1BQoh1WvMkHzu8wSKxV2GXEQP8gJIitN4Fkw5g6PiZxbXu9sLQYzBQWZgJv\npLozvuDhP9etr+8W057956lRkfKtHiw3RJi/wG+RA/Gq+dg6C3a6xQRXim45mmT+\nPrjuj9zSsGSftT4bc9EHH+d5Zf+GbdKe+bi1f8ZYq5eh4QkB4ao17Uz16F7SaMBs\nUQtxpCPDBPVb+RIhuc5m+Knked9ZspT7jfllAFoEH+ak8DQ0uQTtv/pNFWKfA6LK\nR3gbXepPwlcwx5wPabmBDlKqksX+TWH7PW+iz+F2YB9HSACrHN2sRTWOmGko1oDw\nlrKlxpxEZOndqMDVxnkvZCdDDdJvtKzeeXvup8HwrpniWOLhIq8gYmbUomeglhW7\n2ov7FVmIugCbjYOqZ7i7hRpSgM4AL75qpwdLbDWDyD/bMhpKtgw50ymCPiqadJLg\nX1CtN7JBY1Cc3MpxApoO\n=bbXT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cb3c203c91152642e81e6c7db3e12b69c2e787bb\nparent 3c03bb4f182c91b07c12bcd4d79ac61df10dd084\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1782478324 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782478324 -0700\n\n[codex] narrow unused skills intro export (#29991)\n\n## Summary\n\n- stop publicly re-exporting the internally used\n`SKILLS_INTRO_WITH_ALIASES` constant\n- keep the constant and all skills rendering behavior unchanged\n- preserve every integration helper, API, fixture, assertion, and module\nused by tests\n\n## Scope guardrails\n\nThis revision keeps all remote/network-facing functionality and every\nline introduced by `jif <jif@openai.com>`.\n\nFollowing the test-preservation audit, it also restores the in-process\nRMCP test transport, the original `codex-mcp` fixture,\n`PluginLoadOutcome::effective_skill_roots` and its assertions, the\n`EffectiveSkillRoots` API family, the test-only apps renderer, and the\nTUI dead-code annotation. Those files now match the PR base exactly.\n\nNo test imports or directly references the remaining public skills\nexport being narrowed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- repository-wide test-reference audit: no test-used code remains\ndeleted or narrowed\n- deleted-line `git blame` audit: zero Jif-authored deletions\n- `cargo test -p codex-core-plugins -p codex-mcp -p codex-rmcp-client\n--lib`: 467 passed\n- `cargo test -p codex-core --lib apps::render`: 2 passed\n- `cargo test -p codex-core-skills --lib render::tests`: 19 passed\n- `cargo check -p codex-core-skills --all-targets`: passed\n- `just fix -p codex-core-skills`: passed\n- `just fmt`: passed\n- `git diff --check`: passed\n\nThe full local `codex-core-skills` suite passed 106/108 tests; two\nloader tests detected an ambient repository skills root outside the\npackage and failed their isolation assertions. The scoped renderer suite\nand all-target compile pass, and CI runs in an isolated environment.\n\nFinal code delta: 1 insertion, 2 deletions across 2 files.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T12:52:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/914c8eeb4e41442e04a7706ca1638491ceabf4a4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/914c8eeb4e41442e04a7706ca1638491ceabf4a4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/914c8eeb4e41442e04a7706ca1638491ceabf4a4/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3c03bb4f182c91b07c12bcd4d79ac61df10dd084","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3c03bb4f182c91b07c12bcd4d79ac61df10dd084","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3c03bb4f182c91b07c12bcd4d79ac61df10dd084"}]},{"sha":"3c03bb4f182c91b07c12bcd4d79ac61df10dd084","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNjMDNiYjRmMTgyYzkxYjA3YzEyYmNkNGQ3OWFjNjFkZjEwZGQwODQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T10:02:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T10:02:27Z"},"message":"Test selected capabilities across unavailable resume (#30215)\n\n## Why\n\nThe selected-capability integration test already covers initial\nattachment and cold resume, but it resumes while the selected executor\nis still reachable.\n\nThat leaves an important World State transition untested: a thread\nremembers its selected capability root, resumes while that environment\nis unavailable, and later sees the same stable environment return.\n\n## What this tests\n\nThis extends the existing end-to-end scenario:\n\n```text\nselected executor available\n        ↓\napp-server stops and the executor goes away\n        ↓\nthread resumes with the executor unavailable\n        ↓\nskills, selected MCP tools, and connector attribution are absent\n        ↓\nthe same environment ID is attached again\n        ↓\nskills, MCP tools, and connector attribution return\n```\n\nThe test also checks that the unavailable snapshot explicitly tells the\nmodel that no selected-environment skills are currently available. After\nreattachment, it invokes the selected skill again and verifies that a\nnew executor-owned MCP process starts.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is test-only. It keeps the existing assumption that an environment\nID refers to stable capability contents. It does not add package-file\ninvalidation or live transport reconnect behavior.","tree":{"sha":"a830ff0d8388932b155da7a4c204f9ec7640abdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a830ff0d8388932b155da7a4c204f9ec7640abdb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3c03bb4f182c91b07c12bcd4d79ac61df10dd084","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPk4zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgJUQADRhlLMD1REYnOEySVD6t9dC\nf+oZFWIrtapk/Hk3OQgj4gVetc1IaCyFaniwgZtSvA90l/jmX4ioS9SdC7vJVyFy\nmmlai2WzEYPhV4cxpFOGSQXYaEiD80QIXcXpXF9oMTEI4PpE/+ry7+Y0ConI1+NL\nvkrZIl5mGzpHNSeDdBellX8+hrwCW4RC5vS8/ZyAb1F7r0qE2ruDEFreP/ri3C4D\n+HlGgVZtCjlI12t/vm1XPG7qcy+lFhRkf3ucHHDPWbqhdpv0r3etvJq3LWg0iLa4\ni9Oup+uIkzmwZoHi5XQFPxahCl7KD7j/NCBqqXjixF4/H8Crnx8LGv9+qu32+h04\n7mFqWJqZpUgYIBiCrpkoqPG5/6ye/73Iw8PPyBj0qvwXNr4NHSjzg3+aX+UcLasf\nmg8ve0S8aJy92KoIdmr1/l3njB76/BVomfTvV5wu3rL32eDPP5XWwNCD8EMW6GQO\n0DQdltelN6BXSL3gndDwj9LX/N9zfURnhHaLN4Pb9EmieKA8q5wtVK40fOM3pNMN\nPsLxHYYDAyNSfymHOmAOSXc06QeKUYeuEXS+k5WJ9Pbj/Tg3jr+wNuGRApvJmjvm\nyhhH3Bw9/rNkwj5M5n2LA1Tnm8F0CWKaTf26q3gKJo6lvAuM5iDwMrTKbYSmbPbb\nVjXdxblGcW3KRYwxjjGz\n=B9+E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a830ff0d8388932b155da7a4c204f9ec7640abdb\nparent 6d2168f06ae275d5e1f73cabf935d2bcc8549998\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782468147 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782468147 +0100\n\nTest selected capabilities across unavailable resume (#30215)\n\n## Why\n\nThe selected-capability integration test already covers initial\nattachment and cold resume, but it resumes while the selected executor\nis still reachable.\n\nThat leaves an important World State transition untested: a thread\nremembers its selected capability root, resumes while that environment\nis unavailable, and later sees the same stable environment return.\n\n## What this tests\n\nThis extends the existing end-to-end scenario:\n\n```text\nselected executor available\n        ↓\napp-server stops and the executor goes away\n        ↓\nthread resumes with the executor unavailable\n        ↓\nskills, selected MCP tools, and connector attribution are absent\n        ↓\nthe same environment ID is attached again\n        ↓\nskills, MCP tools, and connector attribution return\n```\n\nThe test also checks that the unavailable snapshot explicitly tells the\nmodel that no selected-environment skills are currently available. After\nreattachment, it invokes the selected skill again and verifies that a\nnew executor-owned MCP process starts.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is test-only. It keeps the existing assumption that an environment\nID refers to stable capability contents. It does not add package-file\ninvalidation or live transport reconnect behavior.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T10:02:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3c03bb4f182c91b07c12bcd4d79ac61df10dd084","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3c03bb4f182c91b07c12bcd4d79ac61df10dd084","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3c03bb4f182c91b07c12bcd4d79ac61df10dd084/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6d2168f06ae275d5e1f73cabf935d2bcc8549998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d2168f06ae275d5e1f73cabf935d2bcc8549998","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d2168f06ae275d5e1f73cabf935d2bcc8549998"}]},{"sha":"6d2168f06ae275d5e1f73cabf935d2bcc8549998","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkMjE2OGYwNmFlMjc1ZDVlMWY3M2NhYmY5MzVkMmJjYzg1NDk5OTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T08:27:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T08:27:41Z"},"message":"Reuse MCP runtimes when selected availability changes nothing (#30148)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP runtime reuse was keyed by every ready selected-capability\nenvironment, even when an environment contributed no MCP servers or\nconnectors.\n\nFor example:\n\n1. a global stdio MCP is running;\n2. a selected remote environment contains only a skill;\n3. that environment becomes ready;\n4. the MCP and connector projection stays exactly the same;\n5. Codex nevertheless rebuilds the MCP manager and restarts the global\nstdio process.\n\nThat restart can interrupt active calls and discard process-local state\neven though nothing about MCP changed.\n\n## What changes\n\nWhen selected-environment availability changes, Codex now resolves the\ncandidate MCP and connector projection before deciding whether to\nreplace the runtime:\n\n- if the winning MCP servers or their ownership change, rebuild as\nbefore;\n- if the selected connector snapshot changes, rebuild as before;\n- if an enabled MCP is explicitly bound to an environment whose\navailability changed, rebuild as before;\n- otherwise, keep the exact live manager and processes, and update only\nthe availability input remembered by the snapshot.\n\n```text\nready selected environments:  [] -> [skills-env]\nresolved MCP servers:          {global_probe} -> {global_probe}\nresolved connectors:           {} -> {}\nresult:                         reuse manager; keep the same process\n```\n\nThe comparison uses the resolved winning servers and their sources, so\nplugin/config ownership remains part of the runtime identity.\n\n## Existing stack coverage\n\nThe integration PR directly below this one already covers both rebuild\nboundaries: a selected MCP becomes callable and a selected connector\ntool becomes model-visible when their environment becomes available. It\nalso verifies that an unchanged selected MCP runtime keeps its process.\n\nThis PR does not add another remote-attachment integration scenario for\nthe no-change optimization. `environment/add` returns before readiness,\nand app-server does not currently expose a deterministic readiness\nsignal for an environment that contributes only skills. Keeping a\nfixed-delay test would add flake risk; adding a new readiness API would\nbe outside this fix.\n\n## Scope and assumptions\n\n- This does not change skill discovery, World State rendering, or plugin\nmetadata caching.\n- This does not add file watching or hot reload behavior.\n- This does not change disconnect/reconnect handling.\n- Selected environment IDs and their capability contents retain the\nstack's existing stability assumption.\n- Delayed `required = true` executor MCP behavior remains out of scope.","tree":{"sha":"914b9467fd8cf2d83a918bb26a952cc324531a91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/914b9467fd8cf2d83a918bb26a952cc324531a91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6d2168f06ae275d5e1f73cabf935d2bcc8549998","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPjf9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc80QAE+TKq88K7+BawJfR2mPz76t\nnptGYeuEfr6lba8isAPgRRRGlDVGkpZIWSbKkLS1skhnpT248UUMUY46mn0GZUWx\neMpgmiTz6URJYO4qUPt00PH/VXEPsF+4LlwLVY+Y2D7kPGpJB5petBibKZX7Yzia\nYwfT6y9Wt1BPozcJwbyJB52HHHQUTgUal3pLkeKleI3iZ+S1pZxM46w7yhHmt8zV\nFoza1T3Y4ignj0HzHNB24hUFGE0/6f9pzSLmZiHurf+LgQt1U7beBWcqDmE/+lQl\nHfV5h9ur8ycm0UrYYZll4wYY19m6bnJcLGS6sO6aTShOPEffo7zKEMIRD4oXR6sd\nSWPsA1qKFr8CLCWAQ5JcT6xpx/r2iT4OI6Bty8XgSmWp7ypNedDw6ulG25ttsCj9\n/Gho2HKUjXbVKCl+wrLBNZt5P9XOy89GpGrJEZVbnmo48XJaTQqLqMrBCz2et/rC\nTIYSXR9+GG2MnyRMZq8EvKmk+4+wK8+vnE0jieNNae79roRwguTN5Syjba72DlmY\nVUromMVWJWsi7dP9PTpRr1M9Vu5Ewc/p+E6viLIWT+ysY/QUdO+JLZbSneJUbpjM\nI3zGO1IDkJxyURUi4TRNE25gdvFuF3jIz9H7sFxV9aDjD1YggGNjrobOgOp5R95A\nhWLOAezSJD9aapTGeGIj\n=rC8L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 914b9467fd8cf2d83a918bb26a952cc324531a91\nparent 451c0a437f2434a95c5e3893613f8afb192f4781\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782462461 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782462461 +0100\n\nReuse MCP runtimes when selected availability changes nothing (#30148)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP runtime reuse was keyed by every ready selected-capability\nenvironment, even when an environment contributed no MCP servers or\nconnectors.\n\nFor example:\n\n1. a global stdio MCP is running;\n2. a selected remote environment contains only a skill;\n3. that environment becomes ready;\n4. the MCP and connector projection stays exactly the same;\n5. Codex nevertheless rebuilds the MCP manager and restarts the global\nstdio process.\n\nThat restart can interrupt active calls and discard process-local state\neven though nothing about MCP changed.\n\n## What changes\n\nWhen selected-environment availability changes, Codex now resolves the\ncandidate MCP and connector projection before deciding whether to\nreplace the runtime:\n\n- if the winning MCP servers or their ownership change, rebuild as\nbefore;\n- if the selected connector snapshot changes, rebuild as before;\n- if an enabled MCP is explicitly bound to an environment whose\navailability changed, rebuild as before;\n- otherwise, keep the exact live manager and processes, and update only\nthe availability input remembered by the snapshot.\n\n```text\nready selected environments:  [] -> [skills-env]\nresolved MCP servers:          {global_probe} -> {global_probe}\nresolved connectors:           {} -> {}\nresult:                         reuse manager; keep the same process\n```\n\nThe comparison uses the resolved winning servers and their sources, so\nplugin/config ownership remains part of the runtime identity.\n\n## Existing stack coverage\n\nThe integration PR directly below this one already covers both rebuild\nboundaries: a selected MCP becomes callable and a selected connector\ntool becomes model-visible when their environment becomes available. It\nalso verifies that an unchanged selected MCP runtime keeps its process.\n\nThis PR does not add another remote-attachment integration scenario for\nthe no-change optimization. `environment/add` returns before readiness,\nand app-server does not currently expose a deterministic readiness\nsignal for an environment that contributes only skills. Keeping a\nfixed-delay test would add flake risk; adding a new readiness API would\nbe outside this fix.\n\n## Scope and assumptions\n\n- This does not change skill discovery, World State rendering, or plugin\nmetadata caching.\n- This does not add file watching or hot reload behavior.\n- This does not change disconnect/reconnect handling.\n- Selected environment IDs and their capability contents retain the\nstack's existing stability assumption.\n- Delayed `required = true` executor MCP behavior remains out of scope.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T08:27:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d2168f06ae275d5e1f73cabf935d2bcc8549998","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d2168f06ae275d5e1f73cabf935d2bcc8549998","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d2168f06ae275d5e1f73cabf935d2bcc8549998/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"451c0a437f2434a95c5e3893613f8afb192f4781","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/451c0a437f2434a95c5e3893613f8afb192f4781","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/451c0a437f2434a95c5e3893613f8afb192f4781"}]},{"sha":"451c0a437f2434a95c5e3893613f8afb192f4781","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ1MWMwYTQzN2YyNDM0YTk1YzVlMzg5MzYxM2Y4YWZiMTkyZjQ3ODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T07:47:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T07:47:27Z"},"message":"[codex] fix CreateThreadParams test initializer (#30198)\n\n## Summary\n\n- initialize `selected_capability_roots` in the new\n`attach_in_memory_thread_store` test helper\n- restore `codex-core` test compilation on `main`\n\n## Root cause\n\n[#30144](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/30144) added the helper\nfrom commit `0c3d0742`, whose parent was `c38b2e9b`. That branch was\nbased before [#29856](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29856) added\n`selected_capability_roots` as a required field on `CreateThreadParams`.\n\nThe PR's Rust and Bazel workflows both passed against the stale branch\nhead `0c3d0742`. When #30144 was squashed onto newer `main`, its\ninitializer was integrated alongside the required field from #29856,\nproducing `E0063` in `core/src/session/tests.rs`. Because those\nworkflows tested the branch head rather than the integrated merge\nresult, they did not see the version-skew failure before merge.\n\n## Impact\n\nAny job that compiles the `codex-core` library tests fails, which turned\nthe main-branch `rust-ci-full` and `Bazel` workflows red across\nplatforms and blocks unrelated focused core tests. This change only\ncompletes the test initializer; it does not alter production behavior or\nworkflow configuration.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nturn_complete_flushes_terminal_event_after_delivery` (1 passed, 2909\nskipped)\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"e9dfa8d8fb37aa7133b58dba49eb960f5d3e0f4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e9dfa8d8fb37aa7133b58dba49eb960f5d3e0f4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/451c0a437f2434a95c5e3893613f8afb192f4781","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPi6PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANssQABxs0X2RgvQdgekwKAhOv/S+\njcHgknR2FIz6Ve4jc0TTMxnqu+A6+QNjAs7vXPvwgZYmCX/j5kIP21W1UPxAXU31\nhOSW1H8dzbEG+8UBCZJ77NwiePeH83e600F6aBZniuhXiZewRbZ4WmJtdbhEqkOe\nOyaP1An+5G14y4deoy4suMUVP1k0WIyhs+yi1AfnshKZtmVJKYoGluHtvBE+04DA\nMIdE1K8iUwO/rIsHwswD5pT3DLvJoFnGS4GCirVrEVcQJEGlU/1JxJWoeLByAEGe\nFFGNlhB3XUwjXiNsRHSMumY5UnqXo3uwgzvHHgouuHoVZoqOxWP6sEU9Jm5uqHJW\njol3qN42HSr3ikXdYddmppvND1N9BqcrbeXw7W7QeW0kmh+W7LWGssVm9Pa4srw5\ndeUZ5xuYazSZLF7jerEoVEHSP+qkdgKEsQPES+fnPDNZ+YD9l6W5KbrgI/Rbp4AY\nnMEBkM0HQaFANxomlwY7LRBgTvQMMJIgFQhBITTNUKxarHPjEzWH9vm+lbtfBQgN\nJDfLjKrUsGNQUYUCrsKIPYNXdE4DTkAOrFoxkqj3lUrENbDAIQi6+8jEcnAnPcHk\nJaueW6A1exHis4gig17VaiP/9xR6BUGvdykXRoc0cTkRNkTFZpCU3I7QBYXgxIb8\nkV16hN+Xkt+i+IoZXnYs\n=Ply/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e9dfa8d8fb37aa7133b58dba49eb960f5d3e0f4c\nparent 7d8906b4785d9e2d6ebe8c75a163f97de4f7ca35\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782460047 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782460047 +0100\n\n[codex] fix CreateThreadParams test initializer (#30198)\n\n## Summary\n\n- initialize `selected_capability_roots` in the new\n`attach_in_memory_thread_store` test helper\n- restore `codex-core` test compilation on `main`\n\n## Root cause\n\n[#30144](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/30144) added the helper\nfrom commit `0c3d0742`, whose parent was `c38b2e9b`. That branch was\nbased before [#29856](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29856) added\n`selected_capability_roots` as a required field on `CreateThreadParams`.\n\nThe PR's Rust and Bazel workflows both passed against the stale branch\nhead `0c3d0742`. When #30144 was squashed onto newer `main`, its\ninitializer was integrated alongside the required field from #29856,\nproducing `E0063` in `core/src/session/tests.rs`. Because those\nworkflows tested the branch head rather than the integrated merge\nresult, they did not see the version-skew failure before merge.\n\n## Impact\n\nAny job that compiles the `codex-core` library tests fails, which turned\nthe main-branch `rust-ci-full` and `Bazel` workflows red across\nplatforms and blocks unrelated focused core tests. This change only\ncompletes the test initializer; it does not alter production behavior or\nworkflow configuration.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nturn_complete_flushes_terminal_event_after_delivery` (1 passed, 2909\nskipped)\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-26T07:47:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/451c0a437f2434a95c5e3893613f8afb192f4781","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/451c0a437f2434a95c5e3893613f8afb192f4781","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/451c0a437f2434a95c5e3893613f8afb192f4781/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7d8906b4785d9e2d6ebe8c75a163f97de4f7ca35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7d8906b4785d9e2d6ebe8c75a163f97de4f7ca35","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7d8906b4785d9e2d6ebe8c75a163f97de4f7ca35"}]},{"sha":"7d8906b4785d9e2d6ebe8c75a163f97de4f7ca35","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdkODkwNmI0Nzg1ZDllMmQ2ZWJlOGM3NWExNjNmOTdkZTRmN2NhMzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T07:23:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T07:23:33Z"},"message":"[codex] wire process-owned code mode host into core (#30142)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add the `code_mode_host` feature flag and select\n`ProcessOwnedCodeModeSessionProvider` in `CodeModeService` when enabled\n- initialize code-mode sessions lazily so a missing host reports a tool\nerror without failing thread startup\n- resolve `codex-code-mode-host` beside the running Codex binary by\ndefault while preserving `CODEX_CODE_MODE_HOST_PATH` as an override\n- add unit and end-to-end coverage for host resolution and graceful\nmissing-host behavior\n\n## Why\n\nThis wires the process-owned session client from #30112 into the core\nservice behind an opt-in rollout gate. Packaged Codex installations can\nplace the helper in the same `bin` directory as the main executable\nwithout relying on `PATH`, while development and custom installations\ncan continue to override the helper path.\n\n## Stack\n\n- Depends on #30112\n- Base branch: `cconger/process-owned-session-runtime-4-client`\n\n## Validation\n\nBuild `codex` and `codex-code-mode-host`\n`CODEX_CODE_MODE_HOST_PATH=\"$PWD/target/debug/codex-code-mode-host\"\n./target/debug/codex --enable code_mode_host`","tree":{"sha":"e9dfa8d8fb37aa7133b58dba49eb960f5d3e0f4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e9dfa8d8fb37aa7133b58dba49eb960f5d3e0f4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7d8906b4785d9e2d6ebe8c75a163f97de4f7ca35","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPij1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYdMQADyot6rhV6sXzQEOjvKkYro3\n5Ia48xqAIQnp5FFKiVxvPomisU6XilO+ESNjbY8clhrrxB4tzkw2caOHLRbTHMX/\nip6pI3F2BHnmbr+mMUASmp2vjJYQgCEKlvaYJomIgCr3ZCf18bIYeyVCube/Jlmp\nq/GRUKNtbMWEcctrjjpVn6pMQ2I9AyZ97I2RUO3TCYDYbmXhC4cBDh5EkU/qtojV\nXx4IEPVurtDzX2DwkZBUqT4OnhC9e/kHHlY6eG4P1oxUWKc5weklgeiMjvbX527p\nNt9D+5Id8dD9Cf4jzQDGFwNlELRIxH6WiDwK7nxIyKt1ZxDzSOF8XULoB5zcyLY0\nR12qn1mVv+fvIJ2nxemslSRHyLhDFXfPsDUWmrLvled5PLziboa4ufDcUtWvrBKQ\nMphR4dei81LtJv82W7+OHe9XMSNKVJNT0nmYi5ynfdcpcDaCIC9s9Pt4irKzSbBZ\nJXT3UmOnxF0gPUByuWX4b3APwkTHse5KHjWZ5OTpNNomINlxqVKfNI80gsUsVUhC\n4WMIhzg0O3kEsltVN6oxY6dDQa/7qtma9gPXOnmoUUMsQCUH2UsYKnYPlVil2LNg\ngNTEBGs2N+xCBfoWkdHnAQq2mjlYQ4upYNqJBUcMA8plipWPMGahSquzvf9YMQMH\nVz9vuTzaYB1pcDjjwYC4\n=Afu7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e9dfa8d8fb37aa7133b58dba49eb960f5d3e0f4c\nparent ab16046c88b2ea9e9af849ab6662129c6becb151\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782458613 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782458613 -0700\n\n[codex] wire process-owned code mode host into core (#30142)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add the `code_mode_host` feature flag and select\n`ProcessOwnedCodeModeSessionProvider` in `CodeModeService` when enabled\n- initialize code-mode sessions lazily so a missing host reports a tool\nerror without failing thread startup\n- resolve `codex-code-mode-host` beside the running Codex binary by\ndefault while preserving `CODEX_CODE_MODE_HOST_PATH` as an override\n- add unit and end-to-end coverage for host resolution and graceful\nmissing-host behavior\n\n## Why\n\nThis wires the process-owned session client from #30112 into the core\nservice behind an opt-in rollout gate. Packaged Codex installations can\nplace the helper in the same `bin` directory as the main executable\nwithout relying on `PATH`, while development and custom installations\ncan continue to override the helper path.\n\n## Stack\n\n- Depends on #30112\n- Base branch: `cconger/process-owned-session-runtime-4-client`\n\n## Validation\n\nBuild `codex` and `codex-code-mode-host`\n`CODEX_CODE_MODE_HOST_PATH=\"$PWD/target/debug/codex-code-mode-host\"\n./target/debug/codex --enable code_mode_host`","verified_at":"2026-06-26T07:23:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7d8906b4785d9e2d6ebe8c75a163f97de4f7ca35","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7d8906b4785d9e2d6ebe8c75a163f97de4f7ca35","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7d8906b4785d9e2d6ebe8c75a163f97de4f7ca35/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ab16046c88b2ea9e9af849ab6662129c6becb151","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab16046c88b2ea9e9af849ab6662129c6becb151","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ab16046c88b2ea9e9af849ab6662129c6becb151"}]},{"sha":"ab16046c88b2ea9e9af849ab6662129c6becb151","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFiMTYwNDZjODhiMmVhOWU5YWY4NDlhYjY2NjIxMjljNmJlY2IxNTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T06:46:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T06:46:17Z"},"message":"[codex] add process-owned code-mode session client (#30112)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add `ProcessOwnedCodeModeSessionProvider` and logical session\ngeneration/rebinding state\n- add the supervised child-process connection, reader/writer tasks, and\ndriver state machine\n- make dropped execute/wait/open callers cancellation-safe with explicit\nownership handoff and durable cleanup\n- validate cell/delegate lifecycle state and reject invalid protocol\ntransitions\n- add end-to-end stdio coverage for delegates, cancellation, frame\nlimits, child loss, stale generations, replacement, and long-lived\nsessions\n\n## Why\n\nThis final stage exposes the process-owned client only after the wire\nprotocol, host-safe runtime, and standalone host are independently in\nplace. Transport failure is fail-stop: the client closes local state,\ncancels callbacks, reaps the child, and lazily rebuilds a fresh host\ngeneration rather than transactionally recovering the old connection.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is **4 of 4** in the process-owned code-mode session stack.\n\n- Depends on #30111\n- Full stack: #30108 → #30110 → #30111 → this PR\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode -p codex-code-mode-host` — 86 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode`\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode-host`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `bazel test //codex-rs/code-mode:code-mode-unit-tests\n//codex-rs/code-mode-host:code-mode-host-unit-tests\n//codex-rs/code-mode-host:code-mode-host-stdio-test\n//codex-rs/code-mode-protocol:code-mode-protocol-unit-tests` — 4/4\npassed\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"fd9108a23c43ebaa8a1efba4d057c8e2d6525b2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fd9108a23c43ebaa8a1efba4d057c8e2d6525b2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ab16046c88b2ea9e9af849ab6662129c6becb151","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPiA5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6b4QAGxu11OEv8bDStM4m3k42qQm\nUfQp64sLBauCQCnMwc8yNp1zwt/SLGnMgCfKrzozfJWRrv8dLm4LHiPp0ffxosfm\n4OajVEaaG9tz+PnrXeqEwMnwX20Itdrl9kQEAlcQF7CK+2Xjq1MJMe+Rf5ygWHzv\nNL9QJRvBpou6ufYQSo3Q9iQy1MzSk9j3BZ4rqFv2uBSsf23/RU522qhV8hdc5G2L\neKNjhHP8XyxsbBr10o0KOJ045WNbP8uG0Z0QlpQ9kgGEzzGzkUlKhoCVu89Ulnku\nQWkq8shyobUMlNfeGHs0+KG+EPtbrkdnCIIaCybTZ8+CI3SwY/ZUZZMnkMS6UkQs\n/G72HFu0IjrRAwPXHsV0pIRt1WqnQNSr4v2WAy9E7fXDokAa4XKD/42lcYlKRckm\nbteBfMIg4Ld5ATJkF5yO5IIFZQckrtmGNNm4+7pDbqEKt3MXr4hmdbfx31X/6Eju\nhh51cnLe/dE49Ux9OvxkuQYEAo356Ynti3fn12FvEluMFluYhqbej1TQChUuB3Z+\nQYkCmqyY7cy03FP2CKajbFU6qB2mtPOTbwlCbEQZw7nYD1HVBZupHi9Me3uSzzzP\n5eHaqEk8G9SKEwhsYJ5JbUubAOW/Q782bj+N7e+BgyPHvDBoZ+ngKvp7HZuhVuvN\nEp85NS/mHRDC6++IPyNA\n=c0bx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fd9108a23c43ebaa8a1efba4d057c8e2d6525b2a\nparent b5866eebd631a62a1f3f29ac5e44752e38949c73\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782456377 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782456377 -0700\n\n[codex] add process-owned code-mode session client (#30112)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add `ProcessOwnedCodeModeSessionProvider` and logical session\ngeneration/rebinding state\n- add the supervised child-process connection, reader/writer tasks, and\ndriver state machine\n- make dropped execute/wait/open callers cancellation-safe with explicit\nownership handoff and durable cleanup\n- validate cell/delegate lifecycle state and reject invalid protocol\ntransitions\n- add end-to-end stdio coverage for delegates, cancellation, frame\nlimits, child loss, stale generations, replacement, and long-lived\nsessions\n\n## Why\n\nThis final stage exposes the process-owned client only after the wire\nprotocol, host-safe runtime, and standalone host are independently in\nplace. Transport failure is fail-stop: the client closes local state,\ncancels callbacks, reaps the child, and lazily rebuilds a fresh host\ngeneration rather than transactionally recovering the old connection.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is **4 of 4** in the process-owned code-mode session stack.\n\n- Depends on #30111\n- Full stack: #30108 → #30110 → #30111 → this PR\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode -p codex-code-mode-host` — 86 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode`\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode-host`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `bazel test //codex-rs/code-mode:code-mode-unit-tests\n//codex-rs/code-mode-host:code-mode-host-unit-tests\n//codex-rs/code-mode-host:code-mode-host-stdio-test\n//codex-rs/code-mode-protocol:code-mode-protocol-unit-tests` — 4/4\npassed\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-26T06:46:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab16046c88b2ea9e9af849ab6662129c6becb151","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ab16046c88b2ea9e9af849ab6662129c6becb151","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab16046c88b2ea9e9af849ab6662129c6becb151/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b5866eebd631a62a1f3f29ac5e44752e38949c73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b5866eebd631a62a1f3f29ac5e44752e38949c73","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b5866eebd631a62a1f3f29ac5e44752e38949c73"}]},{"sha":"b5866eebd631a62a1f3f29ac5e44752e38949c73","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI1ODY2ZWViZDYzMWE2MmExZjNmMjlhYzVlNDQ3NTJlMzg5NDljNzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"stevenlee-oai","email":"stevenlee@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T06:23:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T06:23:24Z"},"message":"Persist Cloudflare affinity cookies for MCP HTTP (#29516)\n\n[Codex Thread\n019ef1f9-36e2-7e91-9337-504f097b9dc1](https://codex-thread-link.openai.chatgpt-team.site/thread/019ef1f9-36e2-7e91-9337-504f097b9dc1)\n\n## Why\n\nHosted plugin-service Streamable HTTP MCP traffic uses\n`https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/ps/mcp` and depends on Cloudflare's\n`__cflb` cookie for load-balancer affinity. The local and exec-server\n`http/request` path built a fresh reqwest client for each request\nwithout installing Codex's existing shared ChatGPT Cloudflare cookie\nstore, so affinity could be lost between calls.\n\nThis is an affinity-hardening change motivated by an incident\ninvestigation. It does not establish the broader connector-cache\nincident RCA or claim to fix that incident in full.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Install the existing process-local, strictly allowlisted ChatGPT\nCloudflare cookie store on the reqwest client used by\n`ReqwestHttpClient`.\n- Fresh clients now share allowed Cloudflare infrastructure cookies\nwithin the process that originates the local or exec-server network\nrequest.\n- Keep the existing HTTPS ChatGPT-host and Cloudflare-cookie-name\nrestrictions. This does not introduce a general cookie jar or send\nChatGPT Cloudflare cookies to unrelated hosts.\n\n## Test coverage\n\n- `codex-client` unit coverage verifies that the existing strict store\naccepts and returns `__cflb` for HTTPS ChatGPT URLs.\n- The exec-server HTTPS integration test sends four independent\n`http/request` calls through a local TLS-intercepting proxy and verifies\nthat:\n- `Set-Cookie: __cflb=west` is sent on the next plugin-service request;\n  - a later `Set-Cookie: __cflb=central` replaces the stored value;\n  - non-Cloudflare session cookies are discarded;\n  - no stored ChatGPT Cloudflare cookie is sent to a non-ChatGPT host.\n- `just test -p codex-client` — 38 passed.\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server --test chatgpt_cloudflare_affinity` —\n1 passed.\n- `just bazel-lock-check` — passed.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No persistence of ChatGPT auth, account, session, residency, or\narbitrary cookies.\n- No cookie persistence for third-party MCP servers.\n- No special composition of caller-provided `Cookie` headers.\n- No plugin-service, connector-cache, Habitat/habicache, routing,\nredirect, or API-contract changes.\n- No broader incident RCA conclusions.","tree":{"sha":"8d02329c5c0300b68d4b75ec6bcddca8384dbfa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8d02329c5c0300b68d4b75ec6bcddca8384dbfa5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b5866eebd631a62a1f3f29ac5e44752e38949c73","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPhrcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE3QQAEHmaIfpbZ/Eu2lWpWlaxPyM\nPoK4OtxihGvOqYBp7MNC3KYOAT5lwlY9EbgdAS6dhJyo4Ez0oN1itixP8zYnvwkk\niN0bYLAeO8xPBBIRUT/ApoT2ada0T6dciF6hipwKix0/11HaHw5vwqHOA1ZGhnNH\nX9ocDuJwNU/gwS1FeWYRzG8SX+vu6FuCH8YPJp+HD+QLTip63BadlgP6W+13LzFw\nVvy++QOjt7PIer8Zt0H2J5Woa50AJwKRZoMqlVtG0lq+R0PoDdmWdlL2iWVJxOOD\n8ruuUYtw+0onrWWRarFl+avLPbPmSWy/4Iae3Kbmb/NzYuXpnBAAj3YUuAImAgDq\nTkfXOBrUn+dPjHiHR7fiOl8fJydqIQuUpLavPiwEhgMc2409QRVG8N35DgK9Yb/0\nI/25aq5WMazpNze+WybvKVvQtH3IRpRvPO7wMgiTpQmthDmqf7kraitn0FssLUP6\nObXKq+5uVfXCzhcVqZ33+YCSHsH3l5xGjz9r7XoLHDMkZyPLSkYoD4ZBWcIlzivt\nwQIKPrrd40+qZ2z8oiO5lvn5j2d/s2cTygxnnflqrFH+QFCJlLU+6+PRF+ogn9ag\nVZgYzfAsp5O/85uvTT2QqI1BV/efuewZLrIgQCD9p8FJ7w78RE8iJDwgpcw4DYmV\nZomy74jez5oj3LJPpKAK\n=583O\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8d02329c5c0300b68d4b75ec6bcddca8384dbfa5\nparent 92d2e1df7079b5bd549c92a17fa234706d0580b3\nauthor stevenlee-oai <stevenlee@openai.com> 1782455004 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782455004 -0400\n\nPersist Cloudflare affinity cookies for MCP HTTP (#29516)\n\n[Codex Thread\n019ef1f9-36e2-7e91-9337-504f097b9dc1](https://codex-thread-link.openai.chatgpt-team.site/thread/019ef1f9-36e2-7e91-9337-504f097b9dc1)\n\n## Why\n\nHosted plugin-service Streamable HTTP MCP traffic uses\n`https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/ps/mcp` and depends on Cloudflare's\n`__cflb` cookie for load-balancer affinity. The local and exec-server\n`http/request` path built a fresh reqwest client for each request\nwithout installing Codex's existing shared ChatGPT Cloudflare cookie\nstore, so affinity could be lost between calls.\n\nThis is an affinity-hardening change motivated by an incident\ninvestigation. It does not establish the broader connector-cache\nincident RCA or claim to fix that incident in full.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Install the existing process-local, strictly allowlisted ChatGPT\nCloudflare cookie store on the reqwest client used by\n`ReqwestHttpClient`.\n- Fresh clients now share allowed Cloudflare infrastructure cookies\nwithin the process that originates the local or exec-server network\nrequest.\n- Keep the existing HTTPS ChatGPT-host and Cloudflare-cookie-name\nrestrictions. This does not introduce a general cookie jar or send\nChatGPT Cloudflare cookies to unrelated hosts.\n\n## Test coverage\n\n- `codex-client` unit coverage verifies that the existing strict store\naccepts and returns `__cflb` for HTTPS ChatGPT URLs.\n- The exec-server HTTPS integration test sends four independent\n`http/request` calls through a local TLS-intercepting proxy and verifies\nthat:\n- `Set-Cookie: __cflb=west` is sent on the next plugin-service request;\n  - a later `Set-Cookie: __cflb=central` replaces the stored value;\n  - non-Cloudflare session cookies are discarded;\n  - no stored ChatGPT Cloudflare cookie is sent to a non-ChatGPT host.\n- `just test -p codex-client` — 38 passed.\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server --test chatgpt_cloudflare_affinity` —\n1 passed.\n- `just bazel-lock-check` — passed.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No persistence of ChatGPT auth, account, session, residency, or\narbitrary cookies.\n- No cookie persistence for third-party MCP servers.\n- No special composition of caller-provided `Cookie` headers.\n- No plugin-service, connector-cache, Habitat/habicache, routing,\nredirect, or API-contract changes.\n- No broader incident RCA conclusions.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T06:23:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b5866eebd631a62a1f3f29ac5e44752e38949c73","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b5866eebd631a62a1f3f29ac5e44752e38949c73","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b5866eebd631a62a1f3f29ac5e44752e38949c73/comments","author":{"login":"stevenlee-oai","id":213687449,"node_id":"U_kgDODLycmQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/213687449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/stevenlee-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"92d2e1df7079b5bd549c92a17fa234706d0580b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/92d2e1df7079b5bd549c92a17fa234706d0580b3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/92d2e1df7079b5bd549c92a17fa234706d0580b3"}]},{"sha":"92d2e1df7079b5bd549c92a17fa234706d0580b3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkyZDJlMWRmNzA3OWI1YmQ1NDljOTJhMTdmYTIzNDcwNmQwNTgwYjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"kbazzi","email":"kbazzi@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T04:31:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T04:31:12Z"},"message":"Retry failed Codex Apps MCP startup (#29920)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe built-in Codex Apps MCP client shares a future for the full startup\noperation: connect, complete `initialize`, fetch the initial tools, and\nreturn a usable client. Sharing deduplicates startup work, but it also\nmemoizes terminal errors.\n\nAfter a transient connection, handshake, or initial `tools/list`\nfailure, later tool builds observe the same failed future. The thread\ncannot reconnect after the backend recovers and continues serving its\nstartup-time cached tool snapshot, which may be empty or stale.\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen Apps MCP startup ends in an error, Codex starts bounded recovery\nwithout putting startup latency on tool-router construction:\n\n1. The current tool build immediately continues with the cached startup\nsnapshot.\n2. After the initial failure is reported, Codex starts one fresh full\nstartup attempt in the background.\n3. Concurrent tool builds share that in-flight attempt and also continue\nwith cached tools.\n4. On success, the recovered client becomes active, refreshes the Apps\ntools cache, emits a `Ready` startup status, and is reused by later\noperations.\n5. On failure, the cache remains unchanged and later tool builds may\nstart another background attempt after exponential cooldown: 1s, 2s, 4s,\n8s, 16s, then 30s maximum.\n\nEach recreated startup performs a fresh MCP `initialize` and uncached\n`tools/list`. The MCP client retains its existing bounded retries for\nretryable `initialize` and `tools/list` failures.\n\nThis avoids adding the Apps startup timeout to every request during a\nsustained outage.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is limited to the built-in Codex Apps MCP client:\n\n- no reconnects for user-configured MCP servers;\n- no cache deletion; and\n- no proactive refresh for a healthy client with stale tools.\n\n## Tests\n\nCoverage verifies:\n\n- tool builds return cached tools without waiting for a blocked\nreconnect;\n- concurrent tool builds start only one background reconnect;\n- failed reconnects preserve cached tools and respect exponential\ncooldown;\n- a recovered client is retained and reused; and\n- a long-lived thread exposes recovered app tools on a later follow-up.\n\nValidation:\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp` — 95 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlater_follow_up_uses_background_recovered_apps_after_mid_thread_startup_failures\n--no-capture` — passed\n- `just fix -p codex-mcp`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"e85a2280a3540634a741b9bcdf2d947c8d124a69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e85a2280a3540634a741b9bcdf2d947c8d124a69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/92d2e1df7079b5bd549c92a17fa234706d0580b3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPgCQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAayEQAB/NOvPWAqnNVXUo+0y82SwP\n0xp25pMk8bvp0mX3qsxzZh3JOeJIRhPlbHZNjZuVPPEjOh8h5VLCEi3fZwdIfdKq\nJ+kBk1AAWH+JET94ic7KU3BJJlwSvtP8/6w5fq81Xcvehh2CdPpCD/ZJeKP9l6n9\n7uIajIoZPuoDPnjmQp62Sh+wJLtXNjnXYr7O6HUEGa8xUbG1VLh18zwWO76xWQ2v\ndmvB/N06LEbD+q/dvU7ReYK2K3FwEQQTv9A/LctMmRS5S9Oo45dXRQta0m5ydPQY\na2k2rY5A2ytwzP9cCwicaPrSZiARGyBlTDlAjzy7Yv/KoXi5F+YCzceWzX3lD8ij\nw+RhiChAyNCY3RmXz75hfY0PgUctFNlGu9lowQ+hcd78gK7bZPpdXcCOjGnOkNky\nmr+qHiF8LiFwwAVH1fi//uivuHDCL5MCsBdX7/MAZKRD6q7wn47fRYWxtguVS2ZD\nA5UgsSbfykCXkxaGnPN/QWD31gQacvDMG5WYm9LXZ47Bta4MqYnBW8gUpAfwlm5I\nSyXzZ1JJNa5lr5J3Jub7iKpWu+06zA279/l4hrUpQgll0ARx1zT+B3HpPcnci+M1\nszlj1drZ7JruO/V7B8Yvujco+C7oBtzm0ZPW437GUy4OqLGSGKtCSbfvfKrz45BA\nhZZYcrxn+N0wqCZmPcoO\n=8rIF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e85a2280a3540634a741b9bcdf2d947c8d124a69\nparent f5f812389ee49ab4c9ef1237781ea1013e733fdc\nauthor kbazzi <kbazzi@openai.com> 1782448272 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782448272 -0700\n\nRetry failed Codex Apps MCP startup (#29920)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe built-in Codex Apps MCP client shares a future for the full startup\noperation: connect, complete `initialize`, fetch the initial tools, and\nreturn a usable client. Sharing deduplicates startup work, but it also\nmemoizes terminal errors.\n\nAfter a transient connection, handshake, or initial `tools/list`\nfailure, later tool builds observe the same failed future. The thread\ncannot reconnect after the backend recovers and continues serving its\nstartup-time cached tool snapshot, which may be empty or stale.\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen Apps MCP startup ends in an error, Codex starts bounded recovery\nwithout putting startup latency on tool-router construction:\n\n1. The current tool build immediately continues with the cached startup\nsnapshot.\n2. After the initial failure is reported, Codex starts one fresh full\nstartup attempt in the background.\n3. Concurrent tool builds share that in-flight attempt and also continue\nwith cached tools.\n4. On success, the recovered client becomes active, refreshes the Apps\ntools cache, emits a `Ready` startup status, and is reused by later\noperations.\n5. On failure, the cache remains unchanged and later tool builds may\nstart another background attempt after exponential cooldown: 1s, 2s, 4s,\n8s, 16s, then 30s maximum.\n\nEach recreated startup performs a fresh MCP `initialize` and uncached\n`tools/list`. The MCP client retains its existing bounded retries for\nretryable `initialize` and `tools/list` failures.\n\nThis avoids adding the Apps startup timeout to every request during a\nsustained outage.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is limited to the built-in Codex Apps MCP client:\n\n- no reconnects for user-configured MCP servers;\n- no cache deletion; and\n- no proactive refresh for a healthy client with stale tools.\n\n## Tests\n\nCoverage verifies:\n\n- tool builds return cached tools without waiting for a blocked\nreconnect;\n- concurrent tool builds start only one background reconnect;\n- failed reconnects preserve cached tools and respect exponential\ncooldown;\n- a recovered client is retained and reused; and\n- a long-lived thread exposes recovered app tools on a later follow-up.\n\nValidation:\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp` — 95 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlater_follow_up_uses_background_recovered_apps_after_mid_thread_startup_failures\n--no-capture` — passed\n- `just fix -p codex-mcp`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-26T04:31:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/92d2e1df7079b5bd549c92a17fa234706d0580b3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/92d2e1df7079b5bd549c92a17fa234706d0580b3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/92d2e1df7079b5bd549c92a17fa234706d0580b3/comments","author":{"login":"kbazzi","id":289796993,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUXzgQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289796993?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi","html_url":"https://github.com/kbazzi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f5f812389ee49ab4c9ef1237781ea1013e733fdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f5f812389ee49ab4c9ef1237781ea1013e733fdc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f5f812389ee49ab4c9ef1237781ea1013e733fdc"}]},{"sha":"f5f812389ee49ab4c9ef1237781ea1013e733fdc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY1ZjgxMjM4OWVlNDlhYjRjOWVmMTIzNzc4MWVhMTAxM2U3MzNmZGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tom","email":"wiltzius@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T04:01:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T04:01:11Z"},"message":"[codex] fix terminal rollout event durability (#30144)\n\nCurrently session code does not flush the thread store after appending\nthe `TurnComplete` / `TurnAborted` events.\n\nThis isn't a problem in practice for local storage because append_items\nitself effectively blocks, but any thread stores that buffer in\nappend_items and only commit on flush effectively never get these events\npersisted.\n\nThe fix adds explicit rollout flushes at the terminal emitters after\nnormal completion and interruption.\n\nAdded test cases that assert the number of flushes when completing or\naborting turns. These are admittedly a little brittle and I'm open to\nbetter ideas on how to add automated testing.","tree":{"sha":"02f6ec08f04d33174fe2aec5493820342a8ac86f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/02f6ec08f04d33174fe2aec5493820342a8ac86f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f5f812389ee49ab4c9ef1237781ea1013e733fdc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPfmHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0f8QADeeGAOzK2dFtNvBsJOIe21H\nqyT1sFwikpaTFAOFB0xjTRQzerCGB7ysWFESDVKxFbcmDCISlpCD1L8fCVSO6x4L\n6FtI3izKqq6qfG6GETA5pa2boKlNzURrqIgpydJnkoEx2lopoMKTW7OlwmKhFYLP\nd1gksOJY9iJ6Rvp2G6TQyBvr22BOkuELKOZ6mx0CUpW8rKbXrvPmqBfN1UVdk2zC\nUZ5ku7vr4WZTDd1EIhpSFHsVsvSuonoNnlyDY6yk92EeE7v9V9o+egAG5UKqSNA3\ngwcN2DPyvWGWw8zEkCLrRaNLbJPRGVfnBByDtA8E8sdRED5kZHKjoFG0akbLPUCg\nLcycwQtdosymizEUrQ9CYwxcw5sw92jOYl2+v5AAD8SDcGr/QOIaRGawPNxTRfWr\niUqM77Ipg9bnEOoynhKjEIaX3LsEL4Mcj5PyrXgcLTJfkhT8PwBUHnvzsv79jAJ+\nrDL8tNNPuKlq4Xi2PXbSdXgSasFhyxKvIhfx2oIboZ10KYh5mp+ILfT4FybSChwk\nS7bBt7yTft18FlDtSQ79Js4ZM8gOMxf+Juc1DuaH2NpNNa6pIWQSonpVGoFPflIV\nFllg6jl2EWXK6844q++ALprUg70I9dvJ3RGilvNGyjy6TXMOusSqycArXTIbDhnX\nUAhIFlTBI5dzsiKwZLiF\n=k0DQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 02f6ec08f04d33174fe2aec5493820342a8ac86f\nparent 25f50de6ed95627e1ffe7f11ca30d3d62c6e20e6\nauthor Tom <wiltzius@openai.com> 1782446471 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782446471 -0700\n\n[codex] fix terminal rollout event durability (#30144)\n\nCurrently session code does not flush the thread store after appending\nthe `TurnComplete` / `TurnAborted` events.\n\nThis isn't a problem in practice for local storage because append_items\nitself effectively blocks, but any thread stores that buffer in\nappend_items and only commit on flush effectively never get these events\npersisted.\n\nThe fix adds explicit rollout flushes at the terminal emitters after\nnormal completion and interruption.\n\nAdded test cases that assert the number of flushes when completing or\naborting turns. These are admittedly a little brittle and I'm open to\nbetter ideas on how to add automated testing.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T04:01:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f5f812389ee49ab4c9ef1237781ea1013e733fdc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f5f812389ee49ab4c9ef1237781ea1013e733fdc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f5f812389ee49ab4c9ef1237781ea1013e733fdc/comments","author":{"login":"wiltzius-openai","id":176426546,"node_id":"U_kgDOCoQOMg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176426546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/wiltzius-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"25f50de6ed95627e1ffe7f11ca30d3d62c6e20e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/25f50de6ed95627e1ffe7f11ca30d3d62c6e20e6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/25f50de6ed95627e1ffe7f11ca30d3d62c6e20e6"}]},{"sha":"25f50de6ed95627e1ffe7f11ca30d3d62c6e20e6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI1ZjUwZGU2ZWQ5NTYyN2UxZmZlN2YxMWNhMzBkM2Q2MmM2ZTIwZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T02:11:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T02:11:55Z"},"message":"Test selected capabilities across availability and resume (#30157)\n\n## Why\n\nThis stack crosses World State, executor skills, selected plugin\nmetadata, MCP processes, connectors, dynamic environments, and resume.\nThis PR adds two end-to-end scenarios that validate those pieces\ntogether.\n\nBoth tests enable `deferred_executor`, so they exercise the real\ndelayed-environment path.\n\n## Scenario 1: availability across turns and resume\n\n```text\n1. Start a thread with one selected plugin root bound to E1.\n2. E1 is unavailable.\n   - executor skill is absent\n   - selected MCP is absent\n   - connector has no selected-plugin attribution\n3. Start E1 and register the same stable environment ID.\n4. Start a new turn.\n   - the executor skill appears through World State\n   - its body beats a colliding host skill\n   - the selected MCP tool is advertised and executes inside E1\n   - the connector is attributed to the selected plugin\n5. Start another turn without changing E1.\n   - the MCP PID stays the same, proving runtime reuse\n6. Restart app-server and resume the thread.\n   - durable selected-root intent is restored\n   - skills, MCP, and connector attribution are restored\n   - a new MCP PID proves ephemeral process state was rebuilt\n```\n\n## Scenario 2: availability changes inside one turn\n\n```text\n1. Start a turn while E1 is unavailable.\n2. The first model sample sees no executor skill, MCP, or selected connector.\n3. The turn pauses on request_user_input.\n4. Start E1 and register it while that same turn is still active.\n5. Continue the turn.\n6. The very next model sample sees:\n   - the executor skill catalog\n   - the selected MCP tool\n   - selected-plugin connector attribution\n7. The model calls the MCP, and its output proves execution happened inside E1.\n```\n\nThis second scenario specifically protects the aeon-style behavior:\ncapability state is captured again for every sampling step, not only at\nthe next user turn.\n\n## Scope\n\nThese are integration tests only. They do not add a combinatorial matrix\nfor unsupported plugin-file mutation, environment generations, transport\ndisconnects, or delayed `required = true` executor MCPs.","tree":{"sha":"2cac0299359e3726749b4496ef9f73ae56738703","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2cac0299359e3726749b4496ef9f73ae56738703"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/25f50de6ed95627e1ffe7f11ca30d3d62c6e20e6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPd/rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH6YQAGftTidqrXgDyQLMUlgEHm+P\nqgZ29+ohD5dM0QBaOo6IYljRJNJAgJj5Fth9q6IWnMLqcMOgWkh5OWrFQMKaGzop\n+/pCXA7yMoDelLZ+FlJq4V/+0rnHsCsbPvDsGEns+6xKonxwWoYsouxkS6CrTIgf\n4A+gX2+0mCoFRVG/C3sUYqGNIpK04veeogyFK9bvdaTGqqnBJttC9Q7C49w6dMSs\n/3A4vozCrKbh7usft16vj7cY7ojrZF8/UVw/Qa9qOF+2j0iw049j6TCVa3uX9pn4\nC2RI/dberLM8T6xB0kOLwMH8ue4dGHulZyAQZdo1GOHP8J7vazl6IxUK6El5Uszi\nJUvvSs9n2DlHLFI+kfyGX3OeGrFM90yE+WZ/V+DpbAbzqDbz2LW7e9jJyOlzL1o0\nkOOHS9KZF1dyCFOcBa2GzSfpvNUQ7AO+cOYRa+7o8SN9Z2AXZprRa8dufvw8/nlp\nCrP3qSF/I/c9q9hx0wW6S/M4aAew/bUaNhsJ9SOGkd+5Fp3he8pk6lU5/yMELOVw\nBz9qJFLWmoJHLfKtJd48uQiMCR/foZfLHFnjmw3hB9Bs5jZZcP8j6DonEOKyMyvE\nV467TChSmECXUwrsEGb8bbwKuc87V1TAFmlcRtD/xOAw1rTHDbj8vjnuLnc5TRP3\ntFjRemzBCazPyX/2F6iS\n=WtCn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2cac0299359e3726749b4496ef9f73ae56738703\nparent 0d4351c1b80cae3a40a2d0d64d4e87ca1d5c4afa\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782439915 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782439915 +0100\n\nTest selected capabilities across availability and resume (#30157)\n\n## Why\n\nThis stack crosses World State, executor skills, selected plugin\nmetadata, MCP processes, connectors, dynamic environments, and resume.\nThis PR adds two end-to-end scenarios that validate those pieces\ntogether.\n\nBoth tests enable `deferred_executor`, so they exercise the real\ndelayed-environment path.\n\n## Scenario 1: availability across turns and resume\n\n```text\n1. Start a thread with one selected plugin root bound to E1.\n2. E1 is unavailable.\n   - executor skill is absent\n   - selected MCP is absent\n   - connector has no selected-plugin attribution\n3. Start E1 and register the same stable environment ID.\n4. Start a new turn.\n   - the executor skill appears through World State\n   - its body beats a colliding host skill\n   - the selected MCP tool is advertised and executes inside E1\n   - the connector is attributed to the selected plugin\n5. Start another turn without changing E1.\n   - the MCP PID stays the same, proving runtime reuse\n6. Restart app-server and resume the thread.\n   - durable selected-root intent is restored\n   - skills, MCP, and connector attribution are restored\n   - a new MCP PID proves ephemeral process state was rebuilt\n```\n\n## Scenario 2: availability changes inside one turn\n\n```text\n1. Start a turn while E1 is unavailable.\n2. The first model sample sees no executor skill, MCP, or selected connector.\n3. The turn pauses on request_user_input.\n4. Start E1 and register it while that same turn is still active.\n5. Continue the turn.\n6. The very next model sample sees:\n   - the executor skill catalog\n   - the selected MCP tool\n   - selected-plugin connector attribution\n7. The model calls the MCP, and its output proves execution happened inside E1.\n```\n\nThis second scenario specifically protects the aeon-style behavior:\ncapability state is captured again for every sampling step, not only at\nthe next user turn.\n\n## Scope\n\nThese are integration tests only. They do not add a combinatorial matrix\nfor unsupported plugin-file mutation, environment generations, transport\ndisconnects, or delayed `required = true` executor MCPs.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T02:11:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/25f50de6ed95627e1ffe7f11ca30d3d62c6e20e6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/25f50de6ed95627e1ffe7f11ca30d3d62c6e20e6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/25f50de6ed95627e1ffe7f11ca30d3d62c6e20e6/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0d4351c1b80cae3a40a2d0d64d4e87ca1d5c4afa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0d4351c1b80cae3a40a2d0d64d4e87ca1d5c4afa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0d4351c1b80cae3a40a2d0d64d4e87ca1d5c4afa"}]},{"sha":"0d4351c1b80cae3a40a2d0d64d4e87ca1d5c4afa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBkNDM1MWMxYjgwY2FlM2E0MGEyZDBkNjRkNGU4N2NhMWQ1YzRhZmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:34:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:34:35Z"},"message":"[codex] allow CCA image generation and web search extensions (#29909)\n\n## Summary\n\n- allow the standalone image-generation and web-search extensions for\nthe actor-authorized provider shape used by CCA\n- preserve builtin `image_generation` and `web_search` for older models\nand existing flows\n- keep ordinary non-OpenAI providers excluded from both extensions\n- remove only the image extension local managed-AuthManager requirement\nthat CCA cannot satisfy\n- share actor-authorization detection through `ModelProviderInfo`\n- keep Core tests focused on routing behavior and cover header-shape\nedge cases in `model-provider-info`\n- add a Responses Lite regression that verifies both\n`image_gen.imagegen` and `web.run`\n\n## Why\n\nCCA uses a provider named `local` with `requires_openai_auth: false` and\na non-empty `x-openai-actor-authorization` header. Core accepts that\nprovider shape, but both extension provider-name gates rejected it;\nimage generation additionally required a Codex-managed login.\n\nThe standalone paths must coexist with existing builtin tools. New\nResponses Lite models can receive `image_gen.imagegen` and `web.run`,\nwhile older models continue using builtin tools.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis enables both standalone extensions for CCA once installed\ndownstream, without removing or changing builtin-tool compatibility for\nolder models.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponses_lite_exposes_standalone_tools_for_actor_authorized_provider`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponses_lite_uses_standalone_web_search_and_image_generation`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nhosted_tools_follow_provider_auth_model_and_config_gates`\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-model-provider-info`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"9e55fdd45edddabe6ca5516a639f80ce2b2fce2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9e55fdd45edddabe6ca5516a639f80ce2b2fce2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0d4351c1b80cae3a40a2d0d64d4e87ca1d5c4afa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPdcrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmW0QAI6CRRaG9gYcuT06lAA6Xlr3\nV5tkjh5TimU/PAXC2K8GkU7PQrUk2dDpaqeGdgX8HInazuP3nW224vPcCZhgEXuL\n0EZRGGpdrDnIYgrFnh0i33CIxy12Y+mf0vgewJzhEbEDOjD2675aZRsYmcQwbuGY\nP4pEs0dwOWkPqHUIJKbElK/EF0RIxNUL8mtZcdrtSAQ+zPh8GO2Y2FQAqMUm1LoQ\nQD9vMq1VTaM/x/YmF1FVY5yTM+uIx/XWSStEETAm5KxIz7v+HfHkcZolqqzeEcRW\ngF3oqsrsiCTMz4pCKV49uqAu6Cion3C2lTDvn1PMN54+vjED/Z4JtXCeRhBqlDys\ns+PLjcBVZr1wBk1PQSgMeT/9q/Jz93VJlJpH1B3bR6uhsNRbL9+Ad6skD22eV7RV\nxeAz3hfGQzLYXIYdwLxFxhl+z6T0KscmDIlskyGtlcQIg8rWcbIOQYVJxhttJtlt\nEz5KNSQERxLncZ/aoDFb3QjpH1vk6h1VyVvo19C+Gq6d7Yxf9j8jnjo0ea5mvvSn\nTvq6X9lvvPjsC5Sf5CitFeEGY77ybcgeFXmEpKQWQUlrBFkCUjAyMG4l0HlkMaC3\ngOTMnSd8Orzhz7Cp9fw6TImLhC0jU+CEcLeBcVgygA+ZdohU5ZDRTpvOVVoBSxim\nxbN0oR+9LFyIjaSpGSfx\n=5YC0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9e55fdd45edddabe6ca5516a639f80ce2b2fce2f\nparent ec300bc7bd7355833f579a603df067d59c1963cb\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1782437675 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782437675 -0700\n\n[codex] allow CCA image generation and web search extensions (#29909)\n\n## Summary\n\n- allow the standalone image-generation and web-search extensions for\nthe actor-authorized provider shape used by CCA\n- preserve builtin `image_generation` and `web_search` for older models\nand existing flows\n- keep ordinary non-OpenAI providers excluded from both extensions\n- remove only the image extension local managed-AuthManager requirement\nthat CCA cannot satisfy\n- share actor-authorization detection through `ModelProviderInfo`\n- keep Core tests focused on routing behavior and cover header-shape\nedge cases in `model-provider-info`\n- add a Responses Lite regression that verifies both\n`image_gen.imagegen` and `web.run`\n\n## Why\n\nCCA uses a provider named `local` with `requires_openai_auth: false` and\na non-empty `x-openai-actor-authorization` header. Core accepts that\nprovider shape, but both extension provider-name gates rejected it;\nimage generation additionally required a Codex-managed login.\n\nThe standalone paths must coexist with existing builtin tools. New\nResponses Lite models can receive `image_gen.imagegen` and `web.run`,\nwhile older models continue using builtin tools.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis enables both standalone extensions for CCA once installed\ndownstream, without removing or changing builtin-tool compatibility for\nolder models.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponses_lite_exposes_standalone_tools_for_actor_authorized_provider`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponses_lite_uses_standalone_web_search_and_image_generation`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nhosted_tools_follow_provider_auth_model_and_config_gates`\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-model-provider-info`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-26T01:34:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0d4351c1b80cae3a40a2d0d64d4e87ca1d5c4afa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0d4351c1b80cae3a40a2d0d64d4e87ca1d5c4afa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0d4351c1b80cae3a40a2d0d64d4e87ca1d5c4afa/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ec300bc7bd7355833f579a603df067d59c1963cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ec300bc7bd7355833f579a603df067d59c1963cb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ec300bc7bd7355833f579a603df067d59c1963cb"}]},{"sha":"ec300bc7bd7355833f579a603df067d59c1963cb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGVjMzAwYmM3YmQ3MzU1ODMzZjU3OWE2MDNkZjA2N2Q1OWMxOTYzY2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Martin Au-Yeung","email":"martinauyeung@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:31:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:31:10Z"},"message":"Expose MCP app identity in app context (#29934)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP tool-call events need to expose trusted app identity and action\nmetadata directly so v2 clients do not have to infer it from tool names\nor resource URIs.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add optional `appName`, `templateId`, and `actionName` fields to MCP\ntool-call `appContext`.\n- Populate `appName` and `templateId` from trusted Codex Apps metadata,\nand derive `actionName` from the trusted app resource metadata.\n- Preserve all three fields through core events, legacy protocol events,\npersisted thread history, resume redaction, and app-server v2 responses.\n- Document the public `appContext` fields in\n`codex-rs/app-server/README.md`.\n- Regenerate app-server JSON and TypeScript schemas and add coverage for\nserialization, persistence, redaction, and metadata propagation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol mcp_tool_call`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nmcp_tool_call_item_metadata_only_trusts_codex_apps_identity\nmcp_tool_call_item_includes_app_identity`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Martin Au-Yeung <280153141+martinauyeung-oai@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"05c912d23bb3df18ad50c031615d909a66edf466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/05c912d23bb3df18ad50c031615d909a66edf466"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ec300bc7bd7355833f579a603df067d59c1963cb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPdZeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATLkQABhafANZBFAD0bXvqYWKc1qK\nVoD6PPD+3RblY0as/E8kKob41qq8WgeuFbXzOCOA5DHI4151e/i2Z7wOY5mkKuo/\nErLt1MZi+gPdhB/NDQb+cdhETtjTv/2T2i+RZ2sFYqjgXXkj1/5g5WfZL4hzKaUx\n2h1sc8fBccAkfSWFdj//pkHv8T1Ak7UrXdl8KksvFc5vvpvYBwnct//oX7fD5+lW\ndm9Ani3tf8FYOd4muZvAH+D2z86zSBIUNb+dyHMUsZ0gghrulxMCasKgcppkymMJ\ntd2htoqAzlQba1gvpjtrIjd777NBwtHwpdruPEytr5QzbT1xIJLay6zPFDxagG+7\n2OG61ED2C8SdgG739RP7x1yFDVWM+vOIU18RJq465k3FVyrvH2ZvRF88vwEMsefq\na9xvL7ZqC2XCts/LIZpyPGaDx5JIUaLJIkzYgKMXg6v2gpCFVV3hrk7lbtsqKjBv\n3MHvZGhu8VtCJ3G+oqp8hzzuLJjkprhUaM/UfzGTWiWM6W21Hq+R1aOAEoeFoGrR\nK38puTa9dQPRLEboQsINkpPRpzs9AA6xY/IHwKRdji9R/ZXorMghQp4oq/c1Th6k\no3RQ87CdArj3JhITBHcHr8x7Efc8rsCS0nBsSTgmrEG4WXhyfhypndkdfcOCnlW4\nE5JSawSMNLnzOWQdoD5Q\n=nMLr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 05c912d23bb3df18ad50c031615d909a66edf466\nparent fb8598df3ff05366a295c407c91f3d9316a1630c\nauthor Martin Au-Yeung <martinauyeung@openai.com> 1782437470 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782437470 -0700\n\nExpose MCP app identity in app context (#29934)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP tool-call events need to expose trusted app identity and action\nmetadata directly so v2 clients do not have to infer it from tool names\nor resource URIs.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add optional `appName`, `templateId`, and `actionName` fields to MCP\ntool-call `appContext`.\n- Populate `appName` and `templateId` from trusted Codex Apps metadata,\nand derive `actionName` from the trusted app resource metadata.\n- Preserve all three fields through core events, legacy protocol events,\npersisted thread history, resume redaction, and app-server v2 responses.\n- Document the public `appContext` fields in\n`codex-rs/app-server/README.md`.\n- Regenerate app-server JSON and TypeScript schemas and add coverage for\nserialization, persistence, redaction, and metadata propagation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol mcp_tool_call`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nmcp_tool_call_item_metadata_only_trusts_codex_apps_identity\nmcp_tool_call_item_includes_app_identity`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Martin Au-Yeung <280153141+martinauyeung-oai@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-26T01:31:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ec300bc7bd7355833f579a603df067d59c1963cb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ec300bc7bd7355833f579a603df067d59c1963cb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ec300bc7bd7355833f579a603df067d59c1963cb/comments","author":{"login":"martinauyeung-oai","id":280153141,"node_id":"U_kgDOELLMNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/280153141?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/martinauyeung-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fb8598df3ff05366a295c407c91f3d9316a1630c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fb8598df3ff05366a295c407c91f3d9316a1630c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fb8598df3ff05366a295c407c91f3d9316a1630c"}]},{"sha":"fb8598df3ff05366a295c407c91f3d9316a1630c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZiODU5OGRmM2ZmMDUzNjZhMjk1YzQwN2M5MWYzZDkzMTZhMTYzMGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:28:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:28:14Z"},"message":"Keep MCP elicitation routable across runtime refreshes (#30127)\n\n## Why\n\nAn MCP tool call can still be waiting for an elicitation response when\nan environment update replaces the thread's MCP runtime.\n\nBefore this change:\n\n```text\nruntime A starts a tool call and asks the user\nenvironment becomes ready, so runtime B is published\nclient answers the prompt through runtime B\nruntime B cannot find runtime A's pending responder\n```\n\nThe response is lost and the original tool call stays blocked.\n\n## What changed\n\nAll MCP runtimes for one thread now share a small elicitation router:\n\n```text\nruntime A ---\\\n               shared router: response token -> exact pending responder\nruntime B ---/\n```\n\nWhen Codex surfaces an MCP elicitation, it assigns a unique opaque\nresponse token. The router records which pending request owns that\ntoken. A replacement runtime reuses the same router, so the latest\nruntime can deliver a response to a request started by the previous\nruntime.\n\nThe Codex-owned token also prevents two runtime connections that reuse\nthe same MCP server request ID from receiving each other's responses.\n\nThis does not retain or search old MCP managers. Only the pending\nresponder map is shared.\n\n## Covered scenario\n\nThe integration test exercises the complete failure mode:\n\n1. A thread starts while its selected environment is still unavailable.\n2. A configured MCP server starts a tool call and asks the client for\ninput.\n3. The environment becomes ready, causing Codex to publish a replacement\nMCP runtime.\n4. The client answers the original prompt after the replacement.\n5. The original tool call receives that answer and completes.\n\nA focused routing test also creates two runtimes with the same server\nrequest ID and verifies that each response reaches the exact request\nthat emitted its token.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR changes only elicitation response routing across MCP runtime\nreplacement. It does not change when runtimes are rebuilt, which\nenvironments contribute MCP configuration, or how environment\navailability is detected.","tree":{"sha":"d014288cf6edee5321fd78a1ea4e05366b2aa691","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d014288cf6edee5321fd78a1ea4e05366b2aa691"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fb8598df3ff05366a295c407c91f3d9316a1630c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPdWuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAae4QAKb5pSGg2po02wzXMUo45KFl\nb7fztcUvuPnK8NNpgfykh+3NCNoV4vK2Uyztn8m0gjY7tKlpg8yDr+iGE7a9MAhW\nTY99vo9Z0LJVBml0Lw4hVkGyyXmnouhI9lmYe+19j54Wn7OM87eQUy61JMMIMO3d\nd7kswXkH/fwATepCZyHVp5QKLAfLTTL3SDckj+Kk/Xo5JW6cy775x9gX1QMPvVU0\nspDweP6lnJnHk4SETbwzuKuvO9JRM+avGEpxHlaavheZB5VNjLsEUSy/Hi8iw1kP\n6AgAL0+THvSe06Pj2vB06qWjmnwh8+4/x5hBlOeyuH7mZwWDpo5NPfswggfcL7iU\nArG3WB/eE28ARJeGwwFk2xPnmEvuSvhhCCVmCq7YyvzEBzQRN+PaS4z4VnmgNmwQ\na9XLf2SjCDsmR07bzjoIcLYpscqEQbXo1v4lu+Y9k2WGum723FkewPAfa2QYHNi3\nyfeHEAd78qVC+XSqtWmObPwBK1Y2MennITkaAYBglanIwoBfxTDUOFmOc9esAc1n\n0Q++pYKOljDnVTf7e67xCmvxSnoDDoBVwTpqIf7AOityF+9bGNIOKd73ZmSRhMrX\noqaCSZeJz8ENHfAmy1NV8JzVASSRHOLmDeq27KFzfQzF3XDlfOPXBKBlfciUNWmk\nATUO8SpfxX6y2wt4wq4A\n=vlh2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d014288cf6edee5321fd78a1ea4e05366b2aa691\nparent 723b23efd0c06289e878b294b29f6d7ed98a66e8\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782437294 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782437294 +0000\n\nKeep MCP elicitation routable across runtime refreshes (#30127)\n\n## Why\n\nAn MCP tool call can still be waiting for an elicitation response when\nan environment update replaces the thread's MCP runtime.\n\nBefore this change:\n\n```text\nruntime A starts a tool call and asks the user\nenvironment becomes ready, so runtime B is published\nclient answers the prompt through runtime B\nruntime B cannot find runtime A's pending responder\n```\n\nThe response is lost and the original tool call stays blocked.\n\n## What changed\n\nAll MCP runtimes for one thread now share a small elicitation router:\n\n```text\nruntime A ---\\\n               shared router: response token -> exact pending responder\nruntime B ---/\n```\n\nWhen Codex surfaces an MCP elicitation, it assigns a unique opaque\nresponse token. The router records which pending request owns that\ntoken. A replacement runtime reuses the same router, so the latest\nruntime can deliver a response to a request started by the previous\nruntime.\n\nThe Codex-owned token also prevents two runtime connections that reuse\nthe same MCP server request ID from receiving each other's responses.\n\nThis does not retain or search old MCP managers. Only the pending\nresponder map is shared.\n\n## Covered scenario\n\nThe integration test exercises the complete failure mode:\n\n1. A thread starts while its selected environment is still unavailable.\n2. A configured MCP server starts a tool call and asks the client for\ninput.\n3. The environment becomes ready, causing Codex to publish a replacement\nMCP runtime.\n4. The client answers the original prompt after the replacement.\n5. The original tool call receives that answer and completes.\n\nA focused routing test also creates two runtimes with the same server\nrequest ID and verifies that each response reaches the exact request\nthat emitted its token.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR changes only elicitation response routing across MCP runtime\nreplacement. It does not change when runtimes are rebuilt, which\nenvironments contribute MCP configuration, or how environment\navailability is detected.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T01:28:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fb8598df3ff05366a295c407c91f3d9316a1630c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fb8598df3ff05366a295c407c91f3d9316a1630c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fb8598df3ff05366a295c407c91f3d9316a1630c/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"723b23efd0c06289e878b294b29f6d7ed98a66e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/723b23efd0c06289e878b294b29f6d7ed98a66e8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/723b23efd0c06289e878b294b29f6d7ed98a66e8"}]},{"sha":"723b23efd0c06289e878b294b29f6d7ed98a66e8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDcyM2IyM2VmZDBjMDYyODllODc4YjI5NGIyOWY2ZDdlZDk4YTY2ZTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:18:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:18:00Z"},"message":"Reinject missing World State fragments on resume (#30152)\n\n## Why\n\nWorld State restores its structured snapshot on resume so unchanged\nsections do not have to be rendered again. That is safe only when the\nmodel-visible fragment represented by the snapshot is still present in\nretained history.\n\nFor selected executor skills, the failing selected-capability scenario\nexposed this state:\n\n```text\npersisted World State: selected skill catalog is known\nretained model history: selected skill catalog message is missing\nnext diff: unchanged, so emit nothing\n```\n\nThe model resumes without being told about the selected skill catalog.\n\n## What changed\n\nWorld State contributions may now optionally describe the concrete\nmodel-visible fragment that must remain in retained history.\n\nWhen a persisted snapshot is present:\n\n```text\nmatching retained fragment exists -> trust snapshot, emit nothing\nmatching retained fragment missing -> treat section as absent, render current state once\n```\n\nThe skills extension uses this for non-empty selected-environment\ncatalogs by matching its exact rendered catalog body. Empty or hidden\ncatalogs do not require a fragment.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis does not clear or rebuild the whole World State baseline. It does\nnot change skill discovery, cache invalidation, environment\navailability, or MCP runtime behavior. It only keeps a persisted section\nsnapshot and its retained model context consistent across resume/history\nreconstruction.\n\n## Coverage\n\nA focused World State regression test verifies both sides:\n\n- a missing retained fragment is rendered again\n- a matching retained fragment avoids duplicate injection","tree":{"sha":"dfcc588c2a90c0a79dce8df8f8aff9f23991cdf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/dfcc588c2a90c0a79dce8df8f8aff9f23991cdf8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/723b23efd0c06289e878b294b29f6d7ed98a66e8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPdNICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA60QQAFW1/uIZoUae0YP5KJgkxosg\n+jnlhjIUOjijrSBHKaJv9pbc/AF3tGD3uO5Cxxo+BLMLgyKirGBLLhxZN+Isv3jt\n1AK+B+j0l4dqJkQWN43SjCw0pqpWLEvMg8JAVZzUSBanyjlhPhJM+O+lMHMiOxuF\n2kf3o2KCWdDXzT6N54rkV1z1SC70liNrJPgZncNyhf6N7Kl5BHMD08f9odAQrWOd\nLfZFExfPjq/2O60c+oKazFVX+EXJvwvATEsrYZAvpzAS4BwqQBxVa6usNy4SS9pI\n1EHTJ6qOWPcAdfXo1KK0K3ZrwtWVo4ltVUQbR56/wFQH1fwTeSsNKMHJ9U3+kWfv\nsXqgmiklyX1bAaFryJMevMmiUB4Ts4Ioa8PEU/moKOVDIN8sZsQhf7GX2zrn64se\nyGZ1Uu8YtvmRApDp2xpA5zdvrQuzN5KedHZHiUtmBL5uF45Y1t7z4zaDb6CFFemH\nRzONhO9JUl+TWiiG+7v/Fu01xv/vSeJy9QgQpN1XDBS5dVxNJFHB3Q69ApR+tuwe\neIEBeEmZzbqRTxl8xzQkEQ3C/JPTlWVtz9fPbyrJhPQTcht0XPxsRV+M86iAlsFg\nP7/Yo/5EcffvaetAfxOUdFyjcL/HHZFevMWLjCBZ+F0Z0TrFcBq7RAaNzAOPbect\nyEHjgtqF1PAjB12I2JQG\n=XTOi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dfcc588c2a90c0a79dce8df8f8aff9f23991cdf8\nparent 841f30598c05eebb62139bdd75abef1b7b61d5f7\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782436680 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782436680 +0100\n\nReinject missing World State fragments on resume (#30152)\n\n## Why\n\nWorld State restores its structured snapshot on resume so unchanged\nsections do not have to be rendered again. That is safe only when the\nmodel-visible fragment represented by the snapshot is still present in\nretained history.\n\nFor selected executor skills, the failing selected-capability scenario\nexposed this state:\n\n```text\npersisted World State: selected skill catalog is known\nretained model history: selected skill catalog message is missing\nnext diff: unchanged, so emit nothing\n```\n\nThe model resumes without being told about the selected skill catalog.\n\n## What changed\n\nWorld State contributions may now optionally describe the concrete\nmodel-visible fragment that must remain in retained history.\n\nWhen a persisted snapshot is present:\n\n```text\nmatching retained fragment exists -> trust snapshot, emit nothing\nmatching retained fragment missing -> treat section as absent, render current state once\n```\n\nThe skills extension uses this for non-empty selected-environment\ncatalogs by matching its exact rendered catalog body. Empty or hidden\ncatalogs do not require a fragment.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis does not clear or rebuild the whole World State baseline. It does\nnot change skill discovery, cache invalidation, environment\navailability, or MCP runtime behavior. It only keeps a persisted section\nsnapshot and its retained model context consistent across resume/history\nreconstruction.\n\n## Coverage\n\nA focused World State regression test verifies both sides:\n\n- a missing retained fragment is rendered again\n- a matching retained fragment avoids duplicate injection","verified_at":"2026-06-26T01:18:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/723b23efd0c06289e878b294b29f6d7ed98a66e8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/723b23efd0c06289e878b294b29f6d7ed98a66e8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/723b23efd0c06289e878b294b29f6d7ed98a66e8/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"841f30598c05eebb62139bdd75abef1b7b61d5f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/841f30598c05eebb62139bdd75abef1b7b61d5f7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/841f30598c05eebb62139bdd75abef1b7b61d5f7"}]},{"sha":"841f30598c05eebb62139bdd75abef1b7b61d5f7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg0MWYzMDU5OGMwNWVlYmI2MjEzOWJkZDc1YWJlZjFiN2I2MWQ1Zjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"alexsong-oai","email":"alexsong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:15:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:15:48Z"},"message":"[codex] Attribute app-server analytics by thread originator (#29935)\n\n## Why\n\nDesktop Work threads and regular Codex threads can share the same\napp-server connection. App-server analytics currently copy\n`product_client_id` from connection metadata for every thread-scoped\nevent, so Work thread activity is attributed to the Desktop connection\ninstead of the thread's resolved originator. This prevents analytics\nfrom distinguishing the two products on a shared connection.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Publish the resolved originator after a thread is materialized,\ncovering new, resumed, forked, and subagent threads.\n- Store that originator in the analytics reducer's existing per-thread\nstate.\n- Override only `app_server_client.product_client_id` for thread, turn,\ntool, review, goal, guardian, and compaction events while preserving the\nconnection's client name, version, and transport metadata.\n- Fall back to the connection-wide product client ID when a thread has\nno originator override.\n- Preserve persisted originators in thread initialization analytics for\nresume and fork flows.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-analytics\nthread_originator_overrides_shared_connection_across_thread_events\nsubagent_events_keep_thread_originator_with_explicit_turn_connection`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nturn_start_tracks_thread_originator_in_analytics\nthread_start_tracks_thread_initialized_analytics\nthread_fork_tracks_thread_initialized_analytics\nthread_resume_tracks_thread_initialized_analytics`\n- `just test -p codex-core thread_manager`","tree":{"sha":"bd55e37fa90970d6e2af30ba1e620887542d8067","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bd55e37fa90970d6e2af30ba1e620887542d8067"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/841f30598c05eebb62139bdd75abef1b7b61d5f7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPdLECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3SUQACJdVlVxuPP3dcH9YAT2A7QX\n2B3ihhWaNe2T0TWMtcDW22euzaid6HXYhJBz9fqlg4OZRPNToC4Pn8AkbWYBnn4d\n7t40CadUkw99q3aUkg/cOfgmX0/LVi7KqYOs5GDejgv8IREXnOlQuI/nazcFy5dx\nSws13OkRtkR9+0aLu7uh3tJm1cROO3s0n0W9OYgZqTNfawDNqs7+/aEDut0p6XDz\nsRQgnDf/79IkrdRqA8wUopUvezgzK+kia7a1568JcFUCkCGUsuyGZDAeNkWYY1Ry\n22TmfZOFpt+hvKsNy0fCCTdgKyziH/wowl/+drm5W6qQid7zoX51RQ/no1S+otNH\niHnUcEECiZdJszun+3q9qjQpTGW9j2W/Gxj29wje8K7KEkh8ZM75W4v5IhRfH1k8\n1gYJJEoKJmePCb6LHYgWvg/V2wzqdLf3nIYe6uS/c/qk3OCE9wjJgUWfDLeh5fSf\n1rv65Gor5xjWnFaaMjbNllTqfj9xQTZS7XjtxfhlA5iq3vxxvxSPXGnLUVDsXdik\nFy/0BlbmCAdaDlv55zBcymGUPjlvI3fKpxIJBVTb5uK7dxFuuqpmmQ01lH3tXwdX\nwDITX3wD2KruFg5Qf7glcnBOuIw+T3v9fU4jhMD1AE9iNWQqAPQOjc40VWsoAmEi\nKQMlQFXDFBt5hVdTThRD\n=3P/s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bd55e37fa90970d6e2af30ba1e620887542d8067\nparent da78d5fdc5d8b30a80b402100d8b25ed8031f8c4\nauthor alexsong-oai <alexsong@openai.com> 1782436548 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782436548 -0700\n\n[codex] Attribute app-server analytics by thread originator (#29935)\n\n## Why\n\nDesktop Work threads and regular Codex threads can share the same\napp-server connection. App-server analytics currently copy\n`product_client_id` from connection metadata for every thread-scoped\nevent, so Work thread activity is attributed to the Desktop connection\ninstead of the thread's resolved originator. This prevents analytics\nfrom distinguishing the two products on a shared connection.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Publish the resolved originator after a thread is materialized,\ncovering new, resumed, forked, and subagent threads.\n- Store that originator in the analytics reducer's existing per-thread\nstate.\n- Override only `app_server_client.product_client_id` for thread, turn,\ntool, review, goal, guardian, and compaction events while preserving the\nconnection's client name, version, and transport metadata.\n- Fall back to the connection-wide product client ID when a thread has\nno originator override.\n- Preserve persisted originators in thread initialization analytics for\nresume and fork flows.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-analytics\nthread_originator_overrides_shared_connection_across_thread_events\nsubagent_events_keep_thread_originator_with_explicit_turn_connection`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nturn_start_tracks_thread_originator_in_analytics\nthread_start_tracks_thread_initialized_analytics\nthread_fork_tracks_thread_initialized_analytics\nthread_resume_tracks_thread_initialized_analytics`\n- `just test -p codex-core thread_manager`","verified_at":"2026-06-26T01:15:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/841f30598c05eebb62139bdd75abef1b7b61d5f7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/841f30598c05eebb62139bdd75abef1b7b61d5f7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/841f30598c05eebb62139bdd75abef1b7b61d5f7/comments","author":{"login":"alexsong-oai","id":256201575,"node_id":"U_kgDOD0VTZw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256201575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/alexsong-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"da78d5fdc5d8b30a80b402100d8b25ed8031f8c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/da78d5fdc5d8b30a80b402100d8b25ed8031f8c4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/da78d5fdc5d8b30a80b402100d8b25ed8031f8c4"}]},{"sha":"da78d5fdc5d8b30a80b402100d8b25ed8031f8c4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRhNzhkNWZkYzVkOGIzMGE4MGI0MDIxMDBkOGIyNWVkODAzMWY4YzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:00:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T01:00:39Z"},"message":"[codex] implement standalone code-mode process host (#30111)\n\n## Summary\n\n- implement the standalone `codex-code-mode-host` stdio service\n- route sessions, cells, delegate requests, responses, and cancellation\nthrough a bounded host peer\n- supervise request, writer, cell-forwarding, actor, and V8 failure\nboundaries\n- bound request/session tombstones and fail-stop the connection on\ninvalid protocol state\n- add host-only duplex protocol tests and local Cargo/Bazel run recipes\n\n## Why\n\nThis stage makes the host process independently runnable and reviewable\nbefore exposing any remote client in Codex. Transport or runtime failure\ncloses the connection and relies on process replacement rather than\ntransactional recovery.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is **3 of 4** in the process-owned code-mode session stack.\n\n- Depends on #30110\n- The final client PR targets this branch\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode-host` — 7 host-only tests passed\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode-host`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"2542888bf79cc161e04ba1d17738106470693c94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2542888bf79cc161e04ba1d17738106470693c94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/da78d5fdc5d8b30a80b402100d8b25ed8031f8c4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPc83CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwiAQAAGvz4MayrAagRsmUaNIZtfj\nxKq4/S8QBFVqwZYOD/bzSDpV6Lz55yd5GvTO5hDPgFzjxlixkNH6eQeWma+qZg/B\ntcG2/h4xhpfaJCAbPQFjnPe27IwHSnTxnN5N9pzwa6yhOcJe0VOjZLEHdFdVHCEp\nJuqaFbqXF/kDOpmeFUmot8ngZtBna701ZuaZY1Zi7KcKMY3qNr9tlLMHHGo97ybb\nXV5RjEMaAAJtwzVYSa3PBTBhp+ltQbTNmgyPkU2bQdzaHoLCKPtzU8RrswMNHst0\nn1LXiLoVRqzusg1vbjlBITobbb/wFNy5Z0K2pho9Hkb4N/QfShRygTe3xos3xlzG\nnBFT7EuWqfi7TDtHwVe56qWQnl3ynoWqkl5CQTkUS7LzBsERdLNM2VCsYPyRQmqK\nPU7JV+il1bVzaTG0iBmrzq2Gh24JkNhulzUWyjk2g4tRp9m+aokoXcEeQk7jPHBY\nD3ve4YcUtQRR3pPBrE+++nya9EwalvDosRVj2yyYULiTrBoYk8fJFHpMs6BJRJL5\n+s3iCOheLFba295CHN+meYfkvBb5hiZUpUk4iYA2Pb52nZIMkIEJnjx6ANum0tbQ\nX1zlo3kOhg193hfbAiuAg5Y0ikeq73R+AqM2K0lLQZ9sNJZzmrcr/WOsA45ohNxI\nDfKS/6ubrrMllIfmA5rb\n=B+zF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2542888bf79cc161e04ba1d17738106470693c94\nparent 8ebf71ec257fcb95d72a71c7d3bedbbe9a861e45\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782435639 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782435639 -0700\n\n[codex] implement standalone code-mode process host (#30111)\n\n## Summary\n\n- implement the standalone `codex-code-mode-host` stdio service\n- route sessions, cells, delegate requests, responses, and cancellation\nthrough a bounded host peer\n- supervise request, writer, cell-forwarding, actor, and V8 failure\nboundaries\n- bound request/session tombstones and fail-stop the connection on\ninvalid protocol state\n- add host-only duplex protocol tests and local Cargo/Bazel run recipes\n\n## Why\n\nThis stage makes the host process independently runnable and reviewable\nbefore exposing any remote client in Codex. Transport or runtime failure\ncloses the connection and relies on process replacement rather than\ntransactional recovery.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is **3 of 4** in the process-owned code-mode session stack.\n\n- Depends on #30110\n- The final client PR targets this branch\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode-host` — 7 host-only tests passed\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode-host`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-26T01:00:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/da78d5fdc5d8b30a80b402100d8b25ed8031f8c4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/da78d5fdc5d8b30a80b402100d8b25ed8031f8c4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/da78d5fdc5d8b30a80b402100d8b25ed8031f8c4/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8ebf71ec257fcb95d72a71c7d3bedbbe9a861e45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ebf71ec257fcb95d72a71c7d3bedbbe9a861e45","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8ebf71ec257fcb95d72a71c7d3bedbbe9a861e45"}]},{"sha":"8ebf71ec257fcb95d72a71c7d3bedbbe9a861e45","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhlYmY3MWVjMjU3ZmNiOTVkNzJhNzFjN2QzYmVkYmJlOWE4NjFlNDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T00:47:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T00:47:00Z"},"message":"Reuse walk inventory for environment skill metadata (#30145)\n\n## Why\n\nEnvironment skill discovery already asks the executor to run one\n`fs/walk`. That response contains every regular file path found under\nthe selected root, including any `agents/openai.yaml` files.\n\nToday Core keeps the discovered `SKILL.md` paths but discards the rest\nof that file inventory. It then sends one `fs/getMetadata` request per\nskill just to ask whether `agents/openai.yaml` exists. A root with 66\nskills and no metadata therefore pays for 66 unnecessary network round\ntrips.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Keep the `fs/walk` file and directory inventory for the duration of\nthe scan.\n- Associate each discovered `SKILL.md` with metadata that is known\npresent, known absent, or still requires a fallback probe.\n- Read a known `agents/openai.yaml` directly instead of statting it\nfirst.\n- Skip the metadata request entirely when a complete walk shows that the\nskill has no `agents` directory.\n- Read a known `SKILL.md` and `agents/openai.yaml` concurrently.\n- Keep parsing and validation in `core-skills`.\n\nThe inventory is scan-local. This does not add another cache or change\ncache lifetime.\n\n## Network impact\n\nFor a complete scan of 66 valid skills with no `agents/openai.yaml`, and\none root `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`:\n\n| Operation | Current | After this PR |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `fs/walk` | 1 | 1 |\n| Read `SKILL.md` | 66 | 66 |\n| Stat `agents/openai.yaml` | 66 | 0 |\n| Read `agents/openai.yaml` | 0 | 0 |\n| Stat plugin manifest | 1 | 1 |\n| Read plugin manifest | 1 | 1 |\n| **Total executor RPCs** | **135** | **69** |\n\nThis removes exactly 66 request/response exchanges from the common cold\nscan. Warm scans remain at zero discovery RPCs because the thread-level\nexecutor catalog cache is unchanged.\n\nWhen metadata exists, each file still requires one read. This PR removes\nonly the preceding existence check; it does not batch file contents into\na new RPC.\n\n## Correctness fallbacks\n\nAbsence is trusted only when the walk is complete and the metadata\ndirectory was not present. Core keeps the existing `getMetadata`\nfallback when:\n\n- the walk was truncated;\n- the walk reported an error; or\n- an `agents` directory was observed but `openai.yaml` was not, which\npreserves support for file symlinks and traversal boundaries.\n\n## Deliberate scope\n\nThis PR changes only the environment skill loader and its existing\nfilesystem-call regression coverage. It does not:\n\n- change `fs/walk` or any exec-server protocol;\n- add `readFiles` or a skills-list endpoint;\n- change thread caching;\n- change local skill discovery;\n- change exec-server request concurrency; or\n- optimize plugin-manifest lookup.\n\nThe plugin-manifest stat is intentionally left in place, which is why\nthis PR reaches 69 calls rather than the broader 68-call estimate. That\nlookup has separate alternate-path, ancestor, and symlink semantics and\nshould not be mixed into this change.","tree":{"sha":"7488d1711a307c21decfa6a16053e48bb92ac8ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7488d1711a307c21decfa6a16053e48bb92ac8ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8ebf71ec257fcb95d72a71c7d3bedbbe9a861e45","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPcwECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHXoQAIt8vfgwIpbgrml/TyEBLbFa\nujhLOrdhl627ZceihdaTBhQQB8WYXFho40xCOC0MJGccyYz7ZAK6x4EjhNQns2V4\njlZnBqxOZp7w0ypNPXNLLsQIsqyrUcV7cn5a9aCWmBxuSCPWMupcMZa173Hc0a8/\n7xO1kwuvBof0QtvRtljao/vI5y14Qhe4UADJeHSlPPNxKdUJb0IIzIBoadeufLx7\npmFG9Vl5TRCz7RbjUQmPzHA8Y40e5c1gt8IQpIaVmBi4WiyxtE1wwrUErOb50wZB\nnTbrWdnqDskOPI5MAk9ttFLrfI56hg0POirFBhHTepnHLBVgxbstSymnk3k22jXz\nKGKgkRFrqmItppUOJ+TMFPZedcNrQazT5gFLL4t3x57VmZVK4fnD4Ab1V42lYaiC\n2OcioSjP4IGsaVS6NqpBbtDAYCey/A7aWQyuG35+UI08OFEVjLLcvQMLGA/HluJM\nDEWB137PGRtd5qNs5GBSFjmpY4za2+xRCGmacaGT0vwvq11cbksiDGZXxYN3QLrJ\n9Pbk3BvMZbh9nX2I3RtdI3Ukq4j8WdDY+SHI+Gy7HetP4yIk2W9R8C0uJDCMTQ1A\ntDSpj/YC9vuxJXk+fTXiaGVRzNPbfAC59/SMWK3+8ggr1sHptEPFhpilhEvmfBTy\nbnD8woyOpO6kiwsRGz9D\n=o15g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7488d1711a307c21decfa6a16053e48bb92ac8ca\nparent 3095ea9c3d155bfc89197d2628eb818a55c2755d\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782434820 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782434820 +0100\n\nReuse walk inventory for environment skill metadata (#30145)\n\n## Why\n\nEnvironment skill discovery already asks the executor to run one\n`fs/walk`. That response contains every regular file path found under\nthe selected root, including any `agents/openai.yaml` files.\n\nToday Core keeps the discovered `SKILL.md` paths but discards the rest\nof that file inventory. It then sends one `fs/getMetadata` request per\nskill just to ask whether `agents/openai.yaml` exists. A root with 66\nskills and no metadata therefore pays for 66 unnecessary network round\ntrips.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Keep the `fs/walk` file and directory inventory for the duration of\nthe scan.\n- Associate each discovered `SKILL.md` with metadata that is known\npresent, known absent, or still requires a fallback probe.\n- Read a known `agents/openai.yaml` directly instead of statting it\nfirst.\n- Skip the metadata request entirely when a complete walk shows that the\nskill has no `agents` directory.\n- Read a known `SKILL.md` and `agents/openai.yaml` concurrently.\n- Keep parsing and validation in `core-skills`.\n\nThe inventory is scan-local. This does not add another cache or change\ncache lifetime.\n\n## Network impact\n\nFor a complete scan of 66 valid skills with no `agents/openai.yaml`, and\none root `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`:\n\n| Operation | Current | After this PR |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `fs/walk` | 1 | 1 |\n| Read `SKILL.md` | 66 | 66 |\n| Stat `agents/openai.yaml` | 66 | 0 |\n| Read `agents/openai.yaml` | 0 | 0 |\n| Stat plugin manifest | 1 | 1 |\n| Read plugin manifest | 1 | 1 |\n| **Total executor RPCs** | **135** | **69** |\n\nThis removes exactly 66 request/response exchanges from the common cold\nscan. Warm scans remain at zero discovery RPCs because the thread-level\nexecutor catalog cache is unchanged.\n\nWhen metadata exists, each file still requires one read. This PR removes\nonly the preceding existence check; it does not batch file contents into\na new RPC.\n\n## Correctness fallbacks\n\nAbsence is trusted only when the walk is complete and the metadata\ndirectory was not present. Core keeps the existing `getMetadata`\nfallback when:\n\n- the walk was truncated;\n- the walk reported an error; or\n- an `agents` directory was observed but `openai.yaml` was not, which\npreserves support for file symlinks and traversal boundaries.\n\n## Deliberate scope\n\nThis PR changes only the environment skill loader and its existing\nfilesystem-call regression coverage. It does not:\n\n- change `fs/walk` or any exec-server protocol;\n- add `readFiles` or a skills-list endpoint;\n- change thread caching;\n- change local skill discovery;\n- change exec-server request concurrency; or\n- optimize plugin-manifest lookup.\n\nThe plugin-manifest stat is intentionally left in place, which is why\nthis PR reaches 69 calls rather than the broader 68-call estimate. That\nlookup has separate alternate-path, ancestor, and symlink semantics and\nshould not be mixed into this change.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T00:47:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ebf71ec257fcb95d72a71c7d3bedbbe9a861e45","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8ebf71ec257fcb95d72a71c7d3bedbbe9a861e45","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ebf71ec257fcb95d72a71c7d3bedbbe9a861e45/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3095ea9c3d155bfc89197d2628eb818a55c2755d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3095ea9c3d155bfc89197d2628eb818a55c2755d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3095ea9c3d155bfc89197d2628eb818a55c2755d"}]},{"sha":"3095ea9c3d155bfc89197d2628eb818a55c2755d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMwOTVlYTljM2QxNTViZmM4OTE5N2QyNjI4ZWI4MThhNTVjMjc1NWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T00:36:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T00:36:44Z"},"message":"Project selected plugin runtime by environment availability (#30093)\n\n## Why\n\nSelected plugin metadata is stable, but MCP processes are live runtime\nstate. They need different lifetimes:\n\n- the MCP extension caches manifest, MCP, and connector declarations for\neach stable selected root;\n- each model step projects that cached metadata through the roots that\nresolved as ready for that exact step;\n- the MCP manager is rebuilt only when that availability projection\nchanges.\n\nThis matches executor skills: both features consume the same resolved\nstep roots instead of inferring readiness from the turn's selected\nenvironments.\n\n## Behavior\n\n```text\nE1 not ready for this step\n  -> no E1 MCP servers or connectors\n  -> cached plugin metadata stays in ext/mcp\n\nE1 becomes ready\n  -> reuse cached metadata\n  -> publish one MCP runtime containing E1 capabilities\n\nsame ready roots on the next step\n  -> reuse the exact runtime; no rediscovery and no MCP restart\n\nresume\n  -> create new extension thread state and a new MCP runtime\n```\n\nAll model-facing consumers use the same step snapshot:\n\n```text\nresolved selected roots\n        |\n        v\nextension MCP/connector projection\n        |\n        v\n{ MCP config, connector snapshot, MCP manager }\n        |\n        +-> advertise model tools\n        +-> build app/connector tools\n        +-> execute MCP calls\n```\n\n## Cache contract\n\nThe existing MCP extension owns a cache keyed by the full\n`SelectedCapabilityRoot`:\n\n```rust\nlet state = thread_store.get_or_init(SelectedExecutorPluginMcpState::default);\n```\n\nThe cache lives with extension thread state. Environment availability\nfilters projection but does not invalidate metadata. Resume creates new\nthread state. There is no file watcher or executor generation because\ncontents behind a stable environment/root are assumed stable.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Keeps executor plugin discovery and cached metadata in `ext/mcp`.\n- Caches MCP and connector declarations together per selected root.\n- Uses the step's already-resolved capability roots, including lazy\nenvironments that are not turn environments.\n- Reuses the current MCP runtime when the ready-root projection is\nunchanged.\n- Uses the same step MCP manager and connector snapshot for\nmodel-visible tools and execution.\n- Resolves direct thread-scoped MCP requests from the current\nselected-root projection.\n\n## Deliberately out of scope\n\n- `app/list` remains based on the latest global host-plugin state; this\nPR does not make its response or notifications thread-specific.\n- `required = true` startup semantics do not apply to delayed executor\nMCP activation.\n- No filesystem/content invalidation.\n- No transport-disconnect watcher.\n- No executor generations or environment replacement semantics.\n- No client sharing across complete manager replacements.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. Extension-owned World State sections.\n2. Project executor skills through World State.\n3. Pin one MCP runtime to each model step.\n4. **This PR:** project selected MCP and connector state from\nextension-owned metadata.\n5. Integration coverage for selected capability availability and resume.\n\n## Verification\n\n-\n`selected_plugin_servers_use_managed_requirements_for_the_selected_root_id`\n- The stacked integration PR covers unavailable to ready activation,\nunchanged-runtime reuse, skills, MCP tools, connector attribution, and\ncold resume.","tree":{"sha":"cb6c003f9b58c25a58a1e016d0a8575205141086","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cb6c003f9b58c25a58a1e016d0a8575205141086"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3095ea9c3d155bfc89197d2628eb818a55c2755d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPcmcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA98cQACjVsVujUs1AUJH5iuHJNZUw\nhiQKSwcLBYKIzwWGqD/BwzCJ6I1DRv//a8Yw+ypA1RNZ5D2SxgGhan1aUth2iFWm\nmM/v7VuLeCoDUhObT9zwQL91/RLcb0IUY5I8lmfUsRfvDzbfGTB3KxuBmGcUCiAH\nb/rZ18hO+E6pT6FYIfpckDI4wtYXBi91JJNWeY+YkMBsAwylpKx5xcoGuv9AOdYd\ny/IWBIDtRjDsHQ0HJA+pbLe/oAMbFoLFRzli5lsl7vBQINjTRULNwVn32UDt29u5\nt7zUwljW+hwO79emioCYKXyeuci7YRLjMRFZAIlqAVefG/QWaS6HwVKP8rd8dO1G\nvxd5LtDDRy0WU0HhTHsgALy9SApYPclRcctLkaefX5Yc6vS8vUEMTerTStqbMBLG\nya9VILpij7TJLVMd7aq38yTquZoVOq7KO+EpLS4o2oOSWM2whUP4OZvI59nmobq6\nfS4x4OgwAOSHpT2fwvAn4pdojskTVzl8Uq6Y2wfW/fVGZZGX3m7Q7qXLUccDLfoR\n7tiXRS259eWlEPAqr6A3etjbfYT+ISKwuzuF3Q1X+x0yH2/Q8OzNCRcysPlYSIIz\nQFEzrB3FnMKfov9oqeAg3KwB48OSxL4QU+5RA8szIqzSFU6hWEdKGZVxN2s1viPJ\nIypMZVw1P5AE4IU+WPGL\n=9mkB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cb6c003f9b58c25a58a1e016d0a8575205141086\nparent 5044062704af7667e460cc401221a081054ef3ab\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782434204 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782434204 +0100\n\nProject selected plugin runtime by environment availability (#30093)\n\n## Why\n\nSelected plugin metadata is stable, but MCP processes are live runtime\nstate. They need different lifetimes:\n\n- the MCP extension caches manifest, MCP, and connector declarations for\neach stable selected root;\n- each model step projects that cached metadata through the roots that\nresolved as ready for that exact step;\n- the MCP manager is rebuilt only when that availability projection\nchanges.\n\nThis matches executor skills: both features consume the same resolved\nstep roots instead of inferring readiness from the turn's selected\nenvironments.\n\n## Behavior\n\n```text\nE1 not ready for this step\n  -> no E1 MCP servers or connectors\n  -> cached plugin metadata stays in ext/mcp\n\nE1 becomes ready\n  -> reuse cached metadata\n  -> publish one MCP runtime containing E1 capabilities\n\nsame ready roots on the next step\n  -> reuse the exact runtime; no rediscovery and no MCP restart\n\nresume\n  -> create new extension thread state and a new MCP runtime\n```\n\nAll model-facing consumers use the same step snapshot:\n\n```text\nresolved selected roots\n        |\n        v\nextension MCP/connector projection\n        |\n        v\n{ MCP config, connector snapshot, MCP manager }\n        |\n        +-> advertise model tools\n        +-> build app/connector tools\n        +-> execute MCP calls\n```\n\n## Cache contract\n\nThe existing MCP extension owns a cache keyed by the full\n`SelectedCapabilityRoot`:\n\n```rust\nlet state = thread_store.get_or_init(SelectedExecutorPluginMcpState::default);\n```\n\nThe cache lives with extension thread state. Environment availability\nfilters projection but does not invalidate metadata. Resume creates new\nthread state. There is no file watcher or executor generation because\ncontents behind a stable environment/root are assumed stable.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Keeps executor plugin discovery and cached metadata in `ext/mcp`.\n- Caches MCP and connector declarations together per selected root.\n- Uses the step's already-resolved capability roots, including lazy\nenvironments that are not turn environments.\n- Reuses the current MCP runtime when the ready-root projection is\nunchanged.\n- Uses the same step MCP manager and connector snapshot for\nmodel-visible tools and execution.\n- Resolves direct thread-scoped MCP requests from the current\nselected-root projection.\n\n## Deliberately out of scope\n\n- `app/list` remains based on the latest global host-plugin state; this\nPR does not make its response or notifications thread-specific.\n- `required = true` startup semantics do not apply to delayed executor\nMCP activation.\n- No filesystem/content invalidation.\n- No transport-disconnect watcher.\n- No executor generations or environment replacement semantics.\n- No client sharing across complete manager replacements.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. Extension-owned World State sections.\n2. Project executor skills through World State.\n3. Pin one MCP runtime to each model step.\n4. **This PR:** project selected MCP and connector state from\nextension-owned metadata.\n5. Integration coverage for selected capability availability and resume.\n\n## Verification\n\n-\n`selected_plugin_servers_use_managed_requirements_for_the_selected_root_id`\n- The stacked integration PR covers unavailable to ready activation,\nunchanged-runtime reuse, skills, MCP tools, connector attribution, and\ncold resume.","verified_at":"2026-06-26T00:36:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3095ea9c3d155bfc89197d2628eb818a55c2755d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3095ea9c3d155bfc89197d2628eb818a55c2755d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3095ea9c3d155bfc89197d2628eb818a55c2755d/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5044062704af7667e460cc401221a081054ef3ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5044062704af7667e460cc401221a081054ef3ab","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5044062704af7667e460cc401221a081054ef3ab"}]},{"sha":"5044062704af7667e460cc401221a081054ef3ab","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUwNDQwNjI3MDRhZjc2NjdlNDYwY2M0MDEyMjFhMDgxMDU0ZWYzYWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-26T00:01:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-26T00:01:43Z"},"message":"ci: narrow Windows test skips (#30134)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Windows cross-build skip used the broad `powershell` substring,\nwhich hid unrelated Windows tests. Narrowing it exposed the same ConPTY\nCtrl-C timeout that is breaking `main`; that test is not reliable in\neither cross-built or native Windows Bazel CI yet.\n\n## What changed\n\n- scope the cross-build PowerShell carve-out to the dedicated\nparser-process test module\n- exclude the exact ConPTY Ctrl-C test from Bazel CI while leaving local\nWindows runs enabled\n- repeat the exact exclusion in the cross-build config because it\nreplaces the base skip list\n\n## Manual validation\n\n- `just test-github-scripts`\n- queried the PTY test target under both `ci-windows` and\n`ci-windows-cross`\n- verified the matcher excludes parser-process and ConPTY tests without\nexcluding unrelated PowerShell tests\n- [Windows shard\n4/4](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/28204844286/job/83553063859)\nreproduced the `main` ConPTY timeout before the exact CI-only exclusion\nwas applied","tree":{"sha":"8886165cbcaee594379a1d3ff247fe35e0fd9264","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8886165cbcaee594379a1d3ff247fe35e0fd9264"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5044062704af7667e460cc401221a081054ef3ab","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPcFnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzvUQABksx4LPQQ+6jTuhFRjZwD8W\nYnuaNyIn++NTZq75ZdUuXyg10GsgiX2h5YV9AHd0aVwI4pafYNHIQfAl6kxop2PO\nQ66gE4yOcRI2oeLgMUj2eXLfRYP3TfNNmGxoTtqTjpk19dGtzWzJlsEkDQFNUbKN\nQGsVkv4KNbO+qW0mhSMW92U7gTFFJDNUYhYIfrQFuAMB09ylZjNN4CObFam0C44q\nOYq4Iw7HrNK02ONMqBNqCdNWy/HVSQsM3PdcTbF/rFD0JvdZNX/5Eu9UCRJwgy8G\nbvDDM5SpN4oSYvMtXFPdOtszCw4o+dsUoP3SMce3yytqo2ofcuDi49z1JSXL8MPQ\nl7qGToF6JAxJTMeDBa9gWpK23Htznh6w7IL9phznbpDO0aqk5/PBZCzOHV8IUua4\nH/Pkchi4KCNPJl2KG9zqu96jxP+KA7vqn3fB6258LvFSD/fkkjT0xu6iSo6QBqeb\nCMuCptebZGUJhWLEO9m5BAx82UJ1E1uZzUz0R8yZ6MF5s80vpU1UzwLGtK6XxsUd\nlTwz3x8odB1l0y6d7dpWTPx/Eerp8vA22boGe84sJf/+9ClHhdkUs5xfeeeTWnuS\nG9VGZie2fwm5TWsGU0aa2d4VO66TXmy8JcUSyo8mwJ9tSyK32n5c/aDPQhb063gi\n5g/J5URQRAXoApniDEDg\n=P8iK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8886165cbcaee594379a1d3ff247fe35e0fd9264\nparent ee9e0f6387b91cd14008ea59a8e4315b2a2fdacb\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782432103 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782432103 -0700\n\nci: narrow Windows test skips (#30134)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Windows cross-build skip used the broad `powershell` substring,\nwhich hid unrelated Windows tests. Narrowing it exposed the same ConPTY\nCtrl-C timeout that is breaking `main`; that test is not reliable in\neither cross-built or native Windows Bazel CI yet.\n\n## What changed\n\n- scope the cross-build PowerShell carve-out to the dedicated\nparser-process test module\n- exclude the exact ConPTY Ctrl-C test from Bazel CI while leaving local\nWindows runs enabled\n- repeat the exact exclusion in the cross-build config because it\nreplaces the base skip list\n\n## Manual validation\n\n- `just test-github-scripts`\n- queried the PTY test target under both `ci-windows` and\n`ci-windows-cross`\n- verified the matcher excludes parser-process and ConPTY tests without\nexcluding unrelated PowerShell tests\n- [Windows shard\n4/4](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/28204844286/job/83553063859)\nreproduced the `main` ConPTY timeout before the exact CI-only exclusion\nwas applied","verified_at":"2026-06-26T00:01:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5044062704af7667e460cc401221a081054ef3ab","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5044062704af7667e460cc401221a081054ef3ab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5044062704af7667e460cc401221a081054ef3ab/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ee9e0f6387b91cd14008ea59a8e4315b2a2fdacb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ee9e0f6387b91cd14008ea59a8e4315b2a2fdacb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ee9e0f6387b91cd14008ea59a8e4315b2a2fdacb"}]},{"sha":"ee9e0f6387b91cd14008ea59a8e4315b2a2fdacb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGVlOWUwZjYzODdiOTFjZDE0MDA4ZWE1OWE4ZTQzMTViMmEyZmRhY2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T23:53:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T23:53:07Z"},"message":"Pin MCP runtimes to model steps (#30101)\n\n## Why\n\nAn MCP refresh can replace the session's current manager while a model\nstep is still running. The step must execute calls through the same\nmanager whose tools it advertised.\n\n## Boundary\n\n```text\ncurrent session MCP runtime\n          |\n          | capture once for this model step\n          v\nStepContext.mcp\n  - exact MCP config\n  - exact connection manager\n  - exact runtime environment context\n```\n\n```rust\npub struct McpRuntimeSnapshot {\n    config: Arc<McpConfig>,\n    manager: Arc<McpConnectionManager>,\n    runtime_context: McpRuntimeContext,\n}\n```\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nstep A captures runtime A and advertises A's tools\nrefresh publishes runtime B\nstep A tool call -> runtime A\nnext step        -> runtime B\n```\n\nCapturing the snapshot is only an `Arc` clone. It does not restart MCPs\nor make an RPC.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Captures one MCP runtime in `StepContext`.\n- Uses it for tool planning, tool calls, resources, approvals, connector\nattribution, and elicitation.\n- Publishes replacement runtimes atomically.\n- Lets an old runtime live only while an in-flight step or request still\nholds its `Arc`.\n\nMost of this diff is mechanical routing from the session-global manager\nto `step_context.mcp`; it does not introduce selected-plugin discovery\nyet.\n\n## What does not change\n\n- No plugin or extension migration.\n- No new MCP cache policy.\n- No environment file watching.\n- No client sharing between separate managers.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. Extension-owned World State sections.\n2. Project executor skills through World State.\n3. **This PR:** pin one MCP runtime to each model step.\n4. Project selected MCP/app/connector metadata by environment\navailability.\n5. One end-to-end integration scenario.","tree":{"sha":"60c5226e6a0eade7367a0469db98b4c40a93cfb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/60c5226e6a0eade7367a0469db98b4c40a93cfb3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ee9e0f6387b91cd14008ea59a8e4315b2a2fdacb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPb9jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq78QAF5uXckAP4fhq7SxU0n4S3lD\nd0Ovsg3KXM7zCzRF4JV/rW1I6bXVxKmvGIDRiLEqscVljw4MszJwciFeHxMa6f3f\nLzt+++PdAtX1uzqraEBW8je/eVikF9A596WYx//XxcAEpa6UfXPwjgdq2tTDD7GE\nbnFZc4V+mRh2tt/LKa785CtuM7Lds6ezPlC9xIlMQgX5WxMKlc5xqDbLOYfkv2n4\nQj2BDa8+xoTQy0LKaoZjLZVQypNs4/2LjhMNrjQ9Ucr3Z3/WmUmU1LYTcyjzxUtG\ntlka7lxCBcJFGtT9fTpt5top1zf5GHev4OzIGwx6o+0pwgMGsoDXoUQYblh8abMU\n9u1Qn9ZBnkRzra53NJqMCtvJmvdcdq9DqmOmtEvH0/OSsedf5iQP8z66g0WNnP8C\nD2O7Pt6aJoHn1y+4EI9SkY1D21cxZLLxWybhdm7Ng1Jr8f+nvWEBPkVDuCl2hbrr\nY7kefcsFlxQ/cHNuWBdPjJ2laUMkEv8WGY/NeQCSvydzfSRZKBHGprbvUVQbh0OF\nkngojKLRWuueagzb669igBTcBG9nJe2fER1TajEnHfgVznesV++HykMyHdq65pmc\nrOqEjkd+cqU2iLmvxzJGzOcQvPdphgMIfD4Xoewp4QajBLq+WgB9ogrq4+eZj820\nGl+GBpgWx7O3/zrRAwf3\n=ovxF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 60c5226e6a0eade7367a0469db98b4c40a93cfb3\nparent 8ce931ab763541736bd08d0507b4777543532762\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782431587 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782431587 +0100\n\nPin MCP runtimes to model steps (#30101)\n\n## Why\n\nAn MCP refresh can replace the session's current manager while a model\nstep is still running. The step must execute calls through the same\nmanager whose tools it advertised.\n\n## Boundary\n\n```text\ncurrent session MCP runtime\n          |\n          | capture once for this model step\n          v\nStepContext.mcp\n  - exact MCP config\n  - exact connection manager\n  - exact runtime environment context\n```\n\n```rust\npub struct McpRuntimeSnapshot {\n    config: Arc<McpConfig>,\n    manager: Arc<McpConnectionManager>,\n    runtime_context: McpRuntimeContext,\n}\n```\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nstep A captures runtime A and advertises A's tools\nrefresh publishes runtime B\nstep A tool call -> runtime A\nnext step        -> runtime B\n```\n\nCapturing the snapshot is only an `Arc` clone. It does not restart MCPs\nor make an RPC.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Captures one MCP runtime in `StepContext`.\n- Uses it for tool planning, tool calls, resources, approvals, connector\nattribution, and elicitation.\n- Publishes replacement runtimes atomically.\n- Lets an old runtime live only while an in-flight step or request still\nholds its `Arc`.\n\nMost of this diff is mechanical routing from the session-global manager\nto `step_context.mcp`; it does not introduce selected-plugin discovery\nyet.\n\n## What does not change\n\n- No plugin or extension migration.\n- No new MCP cache policy.\n- No environment file watching.\n- No client sharing between separate managers.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. Extension-owned World State sections.\n2. Project executor skills through World State.\n3. **This PR:** pin one MCP runtime to each model step.\n4. Project selected MCP/app/connector metadata by environment\navailability.\n5. One end-to-end integration scenario.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T23:53:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ee9e0f6387b91cd14008ea59a8e4315b2a2fdacb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ee9e0f6387b91cd14008ea59a8e4315b2a2fdacb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ee9e0f6387b91cd14008ea59a8e4315b2a2fdacb/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8ce931ab763541736bd08d0507b4777543532762","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ce931ab763541736bd08d0507b4777543532762","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8ce931ab763541736bd08d0507b4777543532762"}]},{"sha":"8ce931ab763541736bd08d0507b4777543532762","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhjZTkzMWFiNzYzNTQxNzM2YmQwOGQwNTA3YjQ3Nzc1NDM1MzI3NjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tom","email":"wiltzius@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T23:22:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T23:22:22Z"},"message":"[codex] Propagate traces through exec-server HTTP (#30117)\n\nFixes distributed trace continuity across exec-server JSON-RPC HTTP\negress by adding an executor client span and injecting its W3C context\nthrough a reusable `codex-otel` helper.\n\nThis preserves the caller trace across core/tool → executor →\nprovider/MCP instead of dropping parentage at raw reqwest.\n\nNote that this doesn't include the websocket path, which is needed to\nreally get the full story but at least we cover the basic http path with\nthis change.","tree":{"sha":"9be567196136f08146615c347041513e72efdf3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9be567196136f08146615c347041513e72efdf3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8ce931ab763541736bd08d0507b4777543532762","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPbguCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAupsQACO2UeyRCWTlwlJ795CcChhO\nu3TsQBujix2MKCHtoPOSKZgk70xsI4w2wy/1Vu37hlRy7dh++Hjy6STOzqC2QhTC\nAAVOwka0iIoXeMTi43GHAWj9yFUMMh6KT6+lcEYMkTIsyTtKiT7mhdgDT8q/96Pz\ny3NX8hMennaWnO6icGzL3gxK33otpnB9k2MIt7QYoEFUSyPOEzYbr69fFacue8IV\nCPqNP9xSlb6Pd5QzBHpd1+P0gU3K9QcY1HkBL3XS8j3DOsLteluj0vQ7fT+BAMt7\n2mcn3w4S9Jp3Mam9bsbtLjVgnWGGANxykh9+Dy3nAIn64zhluAPfFul/sH+wvMiy\n107c6JK8KZo/NMNI9jcr6hlhCGoeC6wC4KNzItK8iREfE9V26qeHvC6q0wn/GEAK\nX4RTq3+jj4EtpJnm3qNN5D/ifC/u+Aynxu5gH5UqIuq+RU90Txyb0ctIFzy5VlRH\naecmhJzxLBGTVr1pqCx/8jDF5liii3qG5ybhrf3Hb53umegg4INIwMwqS7V6Bz9/\n8BznMEFxVfz+cxaTe07buV5fcPqfdS2U6JIwD4HjYaPPmfbq9p0ug4281Byx3LBo\nYimJ7UDKywA58RZl8EXGbAnnyQ9YU00vh3ZP+aRJP5wGXFHFtZU0UFKW60/oQl0N\nGpKT0hWynFJXRXk0Z0t/\n=7Sbp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9be567196136f08146615c347041513e72efdf3f\nparent 5eebeb816905f44fd847124ea610922795362cbc\nauthor Tom <wiltzius@openai.com> 1782429742 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782429742 +0000\n\n[codex] Propagate traces through exec-server HTTP (#30117)\n\nFixes distributed trace continuity across exec-server JSON-RPC HTTP\negress by adding an executor client span and injecting its W3C context\nthrough a reusable `codex-otel` helper.\n\nThis preserves the caller trace across core/tool → executor →\nprovider/MCP instead of dropping parentage at raw reqwest.\n\nNote that this doesn't include the websocket path, which is needed to\nreally get the full story but at least we cover the basic http path with\nthis change.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T23:22:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ce931ab763541736bd08d0507b4777543532762","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8ce931ab763541736bd08d0507b4777543532762","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ce931ab763541736bd08d0507b4777543532762/comments","author":{"login":"wiltzius-openai","id":176426546,"node_id":"U_kgDOCoQOMg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176426546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/wiltzius-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5eebeb816905f44fd847124ea610922795362cbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5eebeb816905f44fd847124ea610922795362cbc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5eebeb816905f44fd847124ea610922795362cbc"}]},{"sha":"5eebeb816905f44fd847124ea610922795362cbc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVlZWJlYjgxNjkwNWY0NGZkODQ3MTI0ZWE2MTA5MjI3OTUzNjJjYmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T23:13:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T23:13:43Z"},"message":"Project executor skills through World State (#30088)\n\n## Why\n\nA selected executor environment can be unavailable in one model step and\nready in the next. The model should see its skills only while that\nenvironment is ready, without rescanning stable files on every sample.\n\nThe product assumption is simple:\n\n- an environment ID names one stable logical environment;\n- the selected root contents do not change during the thread.\n\n## Behavior\n\n```text\nE1 unavailable -> do not show E1 skills\nE1 ready       -> discover once, cache, show through World State\nE1 unavailable -> hide skills, keep cache\nE1 ready again -> reuse cache, show skills again\nresume         -> create a new thread cache and discover again\n```\n\nThe cache key is the full `SelectedCapabilityRoot`. Availability does\nnot invalidate it; dropping the extension's thread state does.\n\nThe step supplies the ready selected roots directly. They do not have to\nbe turn environments:\n\n```text\nturn environment: laptop\nselected root:    worker:/plugins/lint-fix\n\nworker ready -> lint-fix skills are visible\n```\n\n## What changes\n\n- Keeps executor skill catalogs in the existing skills extension.\n- Passes the roots resolved as ready for the step into World State\ncontributors.\n- Loads each ready selected root at most once per thread.\n- Contributes the executor catalog as the `skills` World State section.\n- Uses the exact step catalog for explicit skill selection and body\nreads.\n- Leaves host and orchestrator skill behavior where it already lives.\n\nTaking a step snapshot itself does not add an RPC. Executor filesystem\ncalls happen only on the first discovery of a stable root for that\nthread.\n\n## What does not change\n\n- No filesystem watcher or content-based invalidation.\n- No retry/generation framework.\n- No skill runtime migration into core.\n- No general rewrite of the skills extension.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. Extension-owned World State sections.\n2. **This PR:** project cached executor skills through World State.\n3. Pin one MCP runtime to each model step.\n4. Project selected MCP/app/connector metadata by environment\navailability.\n5. One end-to-end integration scenario.","tree":{"sha":"771959f01f4e25e64a71e2234e934d49f8d19e85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/771959f01f4e25e64a71e2234e934d49f8d19e85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5eebeb816905f44fd847124ea610922795362cbc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPbYnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAepMQAIWjjF9a1obRlSFM18c4xqcm\n+XyzTA+j9ZtWBo/Y9fXbaZI7N5j/Bba/qTbrmlwy7DbetwdToIYjXFwVIKjcHgNj\nRKBCH5a/K2Kqg4onIPd6kDhwyQ2SX25UsJxpEsndLjhCio2ZFgkRcbUv5N9JNfvh\nQ4H0CBSYYOwf3j2JQCp94mrG8Fm0U6kJ6To8+ldAnIOT8brDrJn6BY7Kpdw7w2cU\n/sxHIGJbD75On2zqB5YM1YPM6XL3fMMHFDZD5TcOC1rJQauWL8O4iuZW3ZQ5Rg59\nlSgZ4yeL2vyXiuFzCKxxsV6nLJ3aKjubkcys1Up1kjCemeHhZOWQhTGxe5MPxBHe\nsY3OWcs0qyaLGrVHX/zfwD5Sjb/ZIeYTwfxrL3DkRTNnF0nTAKR5vwMagsaoX8Fs\nHIjtMHiiHqUF3FwyGr75/OX/P62Y5bzbt3iM8RrW8aGAwmWXDvz1m5GM6kpK+yNL\nHf71wFIQ0jFF+Uu6RXb8E3GxmBgHZufsiZFQcl4CjRvVEEj5KpcaFwVC0V/2Wbmg\nVgBJuhkeEl/EsCJX9kgFjZ4V3tB+7jmMUNqTOqJaDNQIZGUnhwESb5aRQbU/sF6a\nKCd2kaymdMbr/7B3Zzx62JzwgDPlji85Bp8BZv08Q42E7jVDtoGl9sWnQHVS3sQt\nJPFhlhTF3lVYe/crPphb\n=rcAc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 771959f01f4e25e64a71e2234e934d49f8d19e85\nparent 6c21297bba7da6ef9c14362406eec59aba5cbfce\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782429223 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782429223 +0100\n\nProject executor skills through World State (#30088)\n\n## Why\n\nA selected executor environment can be unavailable in one model step and\nready in the next. The model should see its skills only while that\nenvironment is ready, without rescanning stable files on every sample.\n\nThe product assumption is simple:\n\n- an environment ID names one stable logical environment;\n- the selected root contents do not change during the thread.\n\n## Behavior\n\n```text\nE1 unavailable -> do not show E1 skills\nE1 ready       -> discover once, cache, show through World State\nE1 unavailable -> hide skills, keep cache\nE1 ready again -> reuse cache, show skills again\nresume         -> create a new thread cache and discover again\n```\n\nThe cache key is the full `SelectedCapabilityRoot`. Availability does\nnot invalidate it; dropping the extension's thread state does.\n\nThe step supplies the ready selected roots directly. They do not have to\nbe turn environments:\n\n```text\nturn environment: laptop\nselected root:    worker:/plugins/lint-fix\n\nworker ready -> lint-fix skills are visible\n```\n\n## What changes\n\n- Keeps executor skill catalogs in the existing skills extension.\n- Passes the roots resolved as ready for the step into World State\ncontributors.\n- Loads each ready selected root at most once per thread.\n- Contributes the executor catalog as the `skills` World State section.\n- Uses the exact step catalog for explicit skill selection and body\nreads.\n- Leaves host and orchestrator skill behavior where it already lives.\n\nTaking a step snapshot itself does not add an RPC. Executor filesystem\ncalls happen only on the first discovery of a stable root for that\nthread.\n\n## What does not change\n\n- No filesystem watcher or content-based invalidation.\n- No retry/generation framework.\n- No skill runtime migration into core.\n- No general rewrite of the skills extension.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. Extension-owned World State sections.\n2. **This PR:** project cached executor skills through World State.\n3. Pin one MCP runtime to each model step.\n4. Project selected MCP/app/connector metadata by environment\navailability.\n5. One end-to-end integration scenario.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T23:13:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5eebeb816905f44fd847124ea610922795362cbc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5eebeb816905f44fd847124ea610922795362cbc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5eebeb816905f44fd847124ea610922795362cbc/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6c21297bba7da6ef9c14362406eec59aba5cbfce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6c21297bba7da6ef9c14362406eec59aba5cbfce","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6c21297bba7da6ef9c14362406eec59aba5cbfce"}]},{"sha":"6c21297bba7da6ef9c14362406eec59aba5cbfce","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZjMjEyOTdiYmE3ZGE2ZWY5YzE0MzYyNDA2ZWVjNTlhYmE1Y2JmY2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T22:33:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T22:33:58Z"},"message":"[codex] add code-mode host failure supervision hooks (#30110)\n\n## Why\n\nA process host should be discarded and rebuilt after critical actor or\nV8 failure, while the existing in-process production path must keep its\ncurrent cell-error semantics. This change establishes that failure\nboundary without adding the host process or remote client.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add optional task-failure supervision to the transport-neutral\ncode-mode session runtime\n- report Tokio cell-actor failures and V8 runtime-thread panics to a\nhost-provided fail-stop handler\n- preserve the existing handler-less in-process behavior\n- make host-owned cell ID allocation fail before numeric wraparound\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe V8 panic signal surfaced here should also be consumed by the\n`InProcessCodeModeSession` manager in a future change so it can fail the\naffected cell. This PR intentionally leaves the handler-less in-process\nbehavior unchanged while putting the required panic tracking in place.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is **2 of 4** in the process-owned code-mode session stack.\n\n- #30108 is merged into `main`\n- The next PR targets this branch\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode` — 53 passed\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-code-mode`\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode`","tree":{"sha":"3703ac9068682b188c117fd31f6100702c4be387","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3703ac9068682b188c117fd31f6100702c4be387"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6c21297bba7da6ef9c14362406eec59aba5cbfce","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPazWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmIgQAEpE9RZYlek9r926wrJkSFlv\nlLfVyTq+pUEAI/Nvu4maNfLokVJMqmXs9r3epLhZhW/+A7ZZzn1bmPt57yJJrKLe\n/cxSEEXwvnqJ9XRIJadav+Wev7x37t+SD1YQ/sFfTQEpcl7u1THaTr4PfUg+1Xs/\nvhoJxpvqxLNizVV2GuoyTkKNXNgKeL70SuLUvgvAgS5dq0AeQvWdD6PlMig3r7dj\nEKDqqrr4+z3xriPjDLL+bkRqJoYMMwuqo4Ypc7QhSFrOxOgFlUqbrPqTWIgSOJ6M\n0P2aIYO9Ov1/4jzKPhnnTh8WoRHEAaosNvu8paMeJu0S91Y1nPsERwYb6nbgaygY\nGgGV31aIhSSpTDSS8BjBA2KT1DubSgKrC0F6NnWUX1FsfHn+c8BmcSaC8VQGqOu+\ntnXYCPMKBC4GMEjKVwgIcrmLjBBrHxV+aOI1CbUyTfuHPp7hcIhdppRnQSBI5+fk\niMHtgCamSSYaiThN84F/JbLgTybUloQvpreV6amdCVb5D7w7XVqdkT3EvF4y/VN/\n6bfZVcJ2+d8Gvs4PVUJQgytHOjK28z0D2oxmtDbhZqucp6GJDk+fW0SKxguyNhvV\nlJcupXtj9fg4tc4KzytIz2W9xeBBdesQyPs5q4ct2Jh8Vuc5rg7iTjNB8NxL73S7\n8+PrVtuVXIC5P30Pnz0C\n=S56G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3703ac9068682b188c117fd31f6100702c4be387\nparent e2746fd7e90d4f6095da62d70f50194cc21d2d3e\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782426838 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782426838 -0700\n\n[codex] add code-mode host failure supervision hooks (#30110)\n\n## Why\n\nA process host should be discarded and rebuilt after critical actor or\nV8 failure, while the existing in-process production path must keep its\ncurrent cell-error semantics. This change establishes that failure\nboundary without adding the host process or remote client.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add optional task-failure supervision to the transport-neutral\ncode-mode session runtime\n- report Tokio cell-actor failures and V8 runtime-thread panics to a\nhost-provided fail-stop handler\n- preserve the existing handler-less in-process behavior\n- make host-owned cell ID allocation fail before numeric wraparound\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe V8 panic signal surfaced here should also be consumed by the\n`InProcessCodeModeSession` manager in a future change so it can fail the\naffected cell. This PR intentionally leaves the handler-less in-process\nbehavior unchanged while putting the required panic tracking in place.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is **2 of 4** in the process-owned code-mode session stack.\n\n- #30108 is merged into `main`\n- The next PR targets this branch\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode` — 53 passed\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-code-mode`\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T22:33:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6c21297bba7da6ef9c14362406eec59aba5cbfce","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6c21297bba7da6ef9c14362406eec59aba5cbfce","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6c21297bba7da6ef9c14362406eec59aba5cbfce/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e2746fd7e90d4f6095da62d70f50194cc21d2d3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e2746fd7e90d4f6095da62d70f50194cc21d2d3e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e2746fd7e90d4f6095da62d70f50194cc21d2d3e"}]},{"sha":"e2746fd7e90d4f6095da62d70f50194cc21d2d3e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUyNzQ2ZmQ3ZTkwZDRmNjA5NWRhNjJkNzBmNTAxOTRjYzIxZDJkM2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"chiam-oai","email":"chiam@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T22:30:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T22:30:26Z"},"message":"Recognize Work web and mobile thread originators (#29988)\n\n## Summary\n\n- recognize `codex_work_web` and `codex_work_mobile` as supported\n`thread/start.serviceName` values\n- use the recognized value as the thread-scoped originator, with the\nsame persistence and request propagation added for `codex_work_desktop`\n- cover precedence over persisted and inherited originators\n\nThis is the Codex consumer for the service names introduced by\n[openai/openai#1073178](https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1073178).\n\n## Rollout / Compatibility\n\nThe producer is ChatGPT's app-server integration in\nopenai/openai#1073178. This PR is the Codex app-server consumer that\nconverts those service names into the outgoing per-thread `originator`.\n\nUntil this change is deployed, the new service names are ignored and\nCodex continues using its fallback originator. Deploy this mapper and\nthe matching codex-backend compatibility change in\n[openai/openai#1073594](https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1073594)\nwhile the existing Flora egress overwrite remains in place. Remove that\noverwrite in\n[openai/openai#1073197](https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1073197)\nonly after both consumers are deployed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\neffective_originator_prefers_thread_scoped_sources_before_env_originator`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"610a04d4121b3a30f8800296e0f35cc28b2fb721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/610a04d4121b3a30f8800296e0f35cc28b2fb721"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e2746fd7e90d4f6095da62d70f50194cc21d2d3e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPawCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMVkQAJRk20VtrNhHQWic7mhmw9QP\nAy8AuKupP1egXVzO+0ulpuy/7L7yE8nY6+vUIHYWAU0H9FDT0nEUU05ZbW8g0v+Z\nWotm28wo2wUy9vAR2x58U89c5xW/hlU/d15qwXL8ucwLzatvysWb+y1kMJiudHPG\nqLZXOSW6XUT0DBVhpr18qEvFJ4CCSFHjENFE6Znjafs9tKftNc0e5/DKd1JEP5xB\nIyWTFsXEyO4YHR5h7b9TKuaqWzQAt4znGGGzROmcC0x1OFdoyjT3DbUCPwrKS1tp\ndgryUnBN4+UgzyQMzzIORb4fKbjwtLMVIajiPZAEbzQRgbHCf5HlBoJH6gW7HZfw\nrrQQhTAjMtyuv1z01FggKOzVKXASMORRPKWe5MEpSX1IxePD/AXd3s0kShcvHfr6\nrEngLY/XM6qi5xunj/IAStorUkYwGmbrxQcn1gSbqT6Ldde1Be3ip1xl8TebOtfZ\nHh23Ur8pg+C+r/jqX+WAUT/dfLovA3yI+Oadm0jE9h5M5b9R8PJM/7jTVpjqtW5s\n8O2/T8RySUx0FKKgHLrgp5+QFDx2/xn/vqeiaiBXsd7kUOJp1StFzz+z9pOYEEAP\nk18BLO6Z8TYil8CD/jFK/mwv3nDr01WcbL8otrDV5RfkCSAVvrL5x69BIxlwSCPd\nCadwn0KtsVeWvbusHLaT\n=Oky9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 610a04d4121b3a30f8800296e0f35cc28b2fb721\nparent a6d20ed29701bd8f291e94526154dcac90367d92\nauthor chiam-oai <chiam@openai.com> 1782426626 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782426626 -0700\n\nRecognize Work web and mobile thread originators (#29988)\n\n## Summary\n\n- recognize `codex_work_web` and `codex_work_mobile` as supported\n`thread/start.serviceName` values\n- use the recognized value as the thread-scoped originator, with the\nsame persistence and request propagation added for `codex_work_desktop`\n- cover precedence over persisted and inherited originators\n\nThis is the Codex consumer for the service names introduced by\n[openai/openai#1073178](https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1073178).\n\n## Rollout / Compatibility\n\nThe producer is ChatGPT's app-server integration in\nopenai/openai#1073178. This PR is the Codex app-server consumer that\nconverts those service names into the outgoing per-thread `originator`.\n\nUntil this change is deployed, the new service names are ignored and\nCodex continues using its fallback originator. Deploy this mapper and\nthe matching codex-backend compatibility change in\n[openai/openai#1073594](https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1073594)\nwhile the existing Flora egress overwrite remains in place. Remove that\noverwrite in\n[openai/openai#1073197](https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1073197)\nonly after both consumers are deployed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\neffective_originator_prefers_thread_scoped_sources_before_env_originator`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T22:30:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e2746fd7e90d4f6095da62d70f50194cc21d2d3e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e2746fd7e90d4f6095da62d70f50194cc21d2d3e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e2746fd7e90d4f6095da62d70f50194cc21d2d3e/comments","author":{"login":"chiam-oai","id":263771211,"node_id":"U_kgDOD7jUSw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263771211?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/chiam-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chiam-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a6d20ed29701bd8f291e94526154dcac90367d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a6d20ed29701bd8f291e94526154dcac90367d92","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a6d20ed29701bd8f291e94526154dcac90367d92"}]},{"sha":"a6d20ed29701bd8f291e94526154dcac90367d92","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE2ZDIwZWQyOTcwMWJkOGYyOTFlOTQ1MjYxNTRkY2FjOTAzNjdkOTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"felixxia-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:50:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:50:36Z"},"message":"[codex] Surface MCP reauthentication-required startup failures (#29877)\n\n## Summary\n\n- distinguish expired, non-refreshable stored MCP OAuth credentials from\nfirst-time missing credentials\n- carry a typed `failureReason: \"reauthenticationRequired\"` on the\nexisting `mcpServer/startupStatus/updated` notification only when user\naction is required\n- keep the public MCP auth-status API unchanged and regenerate the\napp-server protocol schemas and documentation\n\n## Why\n\nAn MCP server with an expired access token and no usable refresh token\ncurrently fails startup without giving clients a reliable, typed\nrecovery signal.\n\nThe existing startup-status notification is the natural place to carry\nthis state. Its nullable `failureReason` keeps the recovery reason\nattached to the failed startup transition without adding a one-off\nnotification. Internally, Codex distinguishes first-time login from\nreauthentication and emits the reason only when the startup error itself\nrequires authentication.\n\n## User impact\n\nApp clients can prompt an existing user to reconnect an MCP server when\nautomatic recovery is impossible by handling a failed\n`mcpServer/startupStatus/updated` notification whose `failureReason` is\n`reauthenticationRequired`. Starting, ready, cancelled, unrelated\nfailures, and first-time setup carry no reauthentication reason.\n\n## Companion app PR\n\n- openai/openai#1069582\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` — 248 passed; schema fixture\ntests passed\n- `cargo check -p codex-app-server -p codex-tui`\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client -p codex-mcp` — 184 passed, 2 skipped\n- `just test -p codex-protocol -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-mcp` — 579 passed\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"250834b6b8a3fb2b617c1f5c97c22d0088d0a9da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/250834b6b8a3fb2b617c1f5c97c22d0088d0a9da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a6d20ed29701bd8f291e94526154dcac90367d92","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPaKsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKYIQAIy319ruArnFThllO7LBIj3f\n2bMPmZxoN9UVhvBUWNjLoiptEYJFDTCUnkVW9ctKQLXJvOhYMk3rh+FyqT52dRBj\nURLVodE3n0UssWjOIKRmpGQzssHIHWazjP86cTUKSHQZ0vVqIoqY3Ppv40V92zVF\nCZoSbVGZ0T5urB+P5K+Wi8F0kw+RvLVVDK2qzWK6bvfv0pX46dcmXCrBzHoM1V49\n9xVJiWgTNcmcDvgNz2BmwzJkdH8IjK4ANzjs4Kb50WvHXDAyk34nwFBhFUcERzkT\nx4Zp113IBDHMkie3EGlwgVaSZMkP0+OzRmjziu8Eya0J6KId9sjHYJnE3931ejWq\namXO+F/JSREPx2ImHPz2NOL/b559lOWD/F6Wn50dMlqDqEgar4U4hxPQ8s7rvyiu\nUHtFC4dKrUf54Maej700/Ji6wz053ol5KJed7nFR/t8K5gZrCC3kq2AVfdor4D4f\nVTKqKDhrbRsO9ZoZKfRpvGzR2btNrqfWWxDazc9tn/Ot7FGswrqfs13GAg5e2IPu\nBBn4AkpbRKPZf0aCM1fGzZxb2zhDGvP6kA52HC0/s1s14Lxm28d62AMmrnIxSU1b\nS3BdJ9Yj4liHE867z71MiK/9+4QE8qkkGBl9Px/UAivr7UtYDHSLFlSCcKqvQJmS\nDCTAz/mRrxnwVCBO2DDR\n=L8vw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 250834b6b8a3fb2b617c1f5c97c22d0088d0a9da\nparent b80fbb70cd2f6e6ae32cca8c2eba923bf3c0055e\nauthor felixxia-oai <felixxia@openai.com> 1782424236 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782424236 +0000\n\n[codex] Surface MCP reauthentication-required startup failures (#29877)\n\n## Summary\n\n- distinguish expired, non-refreshable stored MCP OAuth credentials from\nfirst-time missing credentials\n- carry a typed `failureReason: \"reauthenticationRequired\"` on the\nexisting `mcpServer/startupStatus/updated` notification only when user\naction is required\n- keep the public MCP auth-status API unchanged and regenerate the\napp-server protocol schemas and documentation\n\n## Why\n\nAn MCP server with an expired access token and no usable refresh token\ncurrently fails startup without giving clients a reliable, typed\nrecovery signal.\n\nThe existing startup-status notification is the natural place to carry\nthis state. Its nullable `failureReason` keeps the recovery reason\nattached to the failed startup transition without adding a one-off\nnotification. Internally, Codex distinguishes first-time login from\nreauthentication and emits the reason only when the startup error itself\nrequires authentication.\n\n## User impact\n\nApp clients can prompt an existing user to reconnect an MCP server when\nautomatic recovery is impossible by handling a failed\n`mcpServer/startupStatus/updated` notification whose `failureReason` is\n`reauthenticationRequired`. Starting, ready, cancelled, unrelated\nfailures, and first-time setup carry no reauthentication reason.\n\n## Companion app PR\n\n- openai/openai#1069582\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` — 248 passed; schema fixture\ntests passed\n- `cargo check -p codex-app-server -p codex-tui`\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client -p codex-mcp` — 184 passed, 2 skipped\n- `just test -p codex-protocol -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-mcp` — 579 passed\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T21:50:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a6d20ed29701bd8f291e94526154dcac90367d92","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a6d20ed29701bd8f291e94526154dcac90367d92","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a6d20ed29701bd8f291e94526154dcac90367d92/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b80fbb70cd2f6e6ae32cca8c2eba923bf3c0055e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b80fbb70cd2f6e6ae32cca8c2eba923bf3c0055e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b80fbb70cd2f6e6ae32cca8c2eba923bf3c0055e"}]},{"sha":"b80fbb70cd2f6e6ae32cca8c2eba923bf3c0055e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI4MGZiYjcwY2QyZjZlNmFlMzJjY2E4YzJlYmE5MjNiZjNjMDA1NWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:44:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:44:35Z"},"message":"fix(app-server): suppress TUI rollback warning (#30124)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI uses `thread/rollback` internally for user-facing flows such as\nprompt cancellation/backtracking. After `thread/rollback` was marked\ndeprecated, those internal calls started surfacing `deprecationNotice`\nmessages in the TUI, even though the user did not explicitly call the\ndeprecated app-server API.\n\nThe endpoint should remain deprecated for external app-server clients,\nbut the built-in `codex-tui` client should not show this\nimplementation-detail warning during normal interaction.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Pass the initialized app-server client name into the `thread/rollback`\nrequest processor.\n- Suppress the `thread/rollback` deprecation notice only for\n`codex-tui`.\n- Preserve the existing `deprecationNotice` behavior for non-TUI\nclients.\n- Add regression coverage for the `codex-tui` suppression path.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start Codex TUI from this branch.\n2. Type text into the composer and press `Esc` to cancel/backtrack.\n3. Confirm the TUI restores/cancels the prompt without showing\n`thread/rollback is deprecated and will be removed soon`.\n4. Also verify an external app-server client that calls\n`thread/rollback` still receives `deprecationNotice`.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server thread_rollback`\n- `just argument-comment-lint`","tree":{"sha":"e3c77bc51e0a765c5c7fce4715f24d2a9ea882f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e3c77bc51e0a765c5c7fce4715f24d2a9ea882f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b80fbb70cd2f6e6ae32cca8c2eba923bf3c0055e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPaFDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgZkQAIVdVcAEIzTMH/42o5Kmw7Rf\nhugHKEaCxv603Iquc07xRxWDSCRXZQkRQRfRT6kHKawXqlipLrQYVVdqnJDUU6gY\nZkV6Y5okn8Uce4ZMo5NRcmyaT6FQLgxR9KA9lsB0yoz1piBwlwsY92KyLWkvW9zk\ntdrzZ56Ck69hu1TkwWyKT4XVMTp5YHdmw0LvZ19R+13ujaeSZOCdSlInba3vIeAX\njL8p8itzpCE+JEpwNBvOsGectQFY30iw7GnXVpS2rz8yTxBUX417ppHs6QjRQN7W\nKq6Cb6cs6xp//wi3fyE97w709RcRb3dXUhlIfTipmkAoVELnjybFbkboSSJA61yN\n+8P5APBu8KqRlDHiwk92/e9hEgo1/xbo9jvH4C5HGmuSXyLLsoesEuO4YNRfysmi\nZ/ySF/1BB2MY3Al0VlUZ5FNAfcmD2V6eC34cKCvjQr5t50J68eReP9VAZGkwRd1X\nK6zBNTBNXwdnq4FAqudohJrJ48wYKzaAy1hZ6Ns+SwxucxGfTA4mqseYYuTPOcY3\n+muqqkaYT0y3s2O+dCAzvt4kKjd03ksdsVXoyBwK2jKdgV2es+urU/ox69CNu7VJ\ng9qA8g+xm3/53pxbqfqAWJilWUlyg1Smce4pPIH7TtWt24TUBG4F2g/o5LGE6mtn\nhTXg0N7Gn/pt2weZax1Q\n=qXMP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e3c77bc51e0a765c5c7fce4715f24d2a9ea882f2\nparent c9e6d9783dfe99a819f00318f753b6f5cbcc38e8\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1782423875 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782423875 -0300\n\nfix(app-server): suppress TUI rollback warning (#30124)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI uses `thread/rollback` internally for user-facing flows such as\nprompt cancellation/backtracking. After `thread/rollback` was marked\ndeprecated, those internal calls started surfacing `deprecationNotice`\nmessages in the TUI, even though the user did not explicitly call the\ndeprecated app-server API.\n\nThe endpoint should remain deprecated for external app-server clients,\nbut the built-in `codex-tui` client should not show this\nimplementation-detail warning during normal interaction.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Pass the initialized app-server client name into the `thread/rollback`\nrequest processor.\n- Suppress the `thread/rollback` deprecation notice only for\n`codex-tui`.\n- Preserve the existing `deprecationNotice` behavior for non-TUI\nclients.\n- Add regression coverage for the `codex-tui` suppression path.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start Codex TUI from this branch.\n2. Type text into the composer and press `Esc` to cancel/backtrack.\n3. Confirm the TUI restores/cancels the prompt without showing\n`thread/rollback is deprecated and will be removed soon`.\n4. Also verify an external app-server client that calls\n`thread/rollback` still receives `deprecationNotice`.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server thread_rollback`\n- `just argument-comment-lint`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T21:44:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b80fbb70cd2f6e6ae32cca8c2eba923bf3c0055e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b80fbb70cd2f6e6ae32cca8c2eba923bf3c0055e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b80fbb70cd2f6e6ae32cca8c2eba923bf3c0055e/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c9e6d9783dfe99a819f00318f753b6f5cbcc38e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c9e6d9783dfe99a819f00318f753b6f5cbcc38e8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c9e6d9783dfe99a819f00318f753b6f5cbcc38e8"}]},{"sha":"c9e6d9783dfe99a819f00318f753b6f5cbcc38e8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM5ZTZkOTc4M2RmZTk5YTgxOWYwMDMxOGY3NTNiNmY1Y2JjYzM4ZTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:23:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:23:51Z"},"message":"Let extensions contribute World State sections (#30100)\n\n## Why\n\n#29856 already owns the durable thread intent and exact environment\nbinding. This PR adds only the small missing extension boundary: an\nextension can contribute one named World State section, while core still\nowns persistence, diffing, and model-visible fragment types.\n\nThis lets skills stay in the skills extension instead of moving their\nruntime into core.\n\n## Shape\n\n```text\nextension-owned state\n        |\n        | contribute section id + JSON snapshot + renderer\n        v\ncore World State\n        |\n        | compare with the previous snapshot\n        v\nno message, or one incremental model-visible update\n```\n\nThe extension API is deliberately small:\n\n```rust\nfn contribute_world_state(...) -> Vec<WorldStateSectionContribution>\n```\n\nCore adapts the rendered result to `ContextualUserFragment`, records the\nsnapshot, and keeps the existing compaction/resume behavior.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Adds extension-owned World State section contributions.\n- Calls those contributors from the existing per-step World State\nbuilder.\n- Restores durable selected capability roots into extension thread state\non resume.\n- Keeps the actual model-context fragment and rollout machinery in core.\n\n## What does not change\n\n- No skill or MCP implementation moves out of its extension.\n- No new file watcher, generation, or RPC.\n- No generic migration of existing World State sections.\n- No change to the stable environment-ID assumption from #29856.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nstep 1 snapshot: skills = []\nstep 2 snapshot: skills = [executor-demo:deploy]\n\ncore asks the skills extension to render only that change.\n```\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **This PR:** let extensions contribute World State sections.\n2. Project executor skills through the skills extension.\n3. Pin one MCP runtime to each model step.\n4. Project selected MCP/app/connector metadata by environment\navailability.\n5. One end-to-end integration scenario.","tree":{"sha":"547873ecac68194a377ea02a9454ca3527b99e89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/547873ecac68194a377ea02a9454ca3527b99e89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c9e6d9783dfe99a819f00318f753b6f5cbcc38e8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPZxnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb+gQAAobzpn9ovtKC+yFO+SfwFcD\nUSzO6vOJ71kB4+M+oc6m+U9s+LiMmLKEa4kpjjXxmfp8wtvbDBNjzwv5Xj8Mhkz5\nEgMVxm6vTU/1bebQISAiSFgWzv40SseEZd63e50x8oNmKtpFfsfr/10kzVyLtupS\n0FEGmJsntbiZSUYuOU2S0MmNggeh/BaDwJ5oXRcLYg9PQIw9lAAEl89bYrkYJ4/H\nGpEUntCXhjBhBRtOdBaHD+coYQDFUL9gXozUFPF8QPxJ3fEnzVuzvHi6Z3vn26xo\nos8O4Gvkwh+NRVi/ql07SIUpOtag9MmVChQqhayrISE9hD6Ltq6O/T3KXU9vzZWr\nwsyLmEA+jT3/bDGKjys04ptp13bqml+sFYnOP+hmjwTr73RLdSHXcFBd9iiwfDBP\nstSbZJq7w+zhqV/Zq+9bsEVbgdjhygjcUpISk79s2/jSPl851GIqEbqZmRj928qP\na86Y/8yZNxDI5+uhu6opLpnc/lg8shGD/+ACra1h/fqr7vgm5aEqhUtvdE8VUfx3\nPn8qpgVGUWhe4CcLklaaM2WSRzy71vvLfig7wpceadiHayjQOW7Q3wxVtBb7z4U/\n6+HqFRei44HcbSWl6OGXVodYW4KYe/TVrJrRbUReG0OIx7GmHrTHHNGqDE08nhYh\nWHgMkjxqAYBHMbHVKlVW\n=DAoq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 547873ecac68194a377ea02a9454ca3527b99e89\nparent db541f45536f18741b50c74b05904a2c5f628c96\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782422631 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782422631 +0100\n\nLet extensions contribute World State sections (#30100)\n\n## Why\n\n#29856 already owns the durable thread intent and exact environment\nbinding. This PR adds only the small missing extension boundary: an\nextension can contribute one named World State section, while core still\nowns persistence, diffing, and model-visible fragment types.\n\nThis lets skills stay in the skills extension instead of moving their\nruntime into core.\n\n## Shape\n\n```text\nextension-owned state\n        |\n        | contribute section id + JSON snapshot + renderer\n        v\ncore World State\n        |\n        | compare with the previous snapshot\n        v\nno message, or one incremental model-visible update\n```\n\nThe extension API is deliberately small:\n\n```rust\nfn contribute_world_state(...) -> Vec<WorldStateSectionContribution>\n```\n\nCore adapts the rendered result to `ContextualUserFragment`, records the\nsnapshot, and keeps the existing compaction/resume behavior.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Adds extension-owned World State section contributions.\n- Calls those contributors from the existing per-step World State\nbuilder.\n- Restores durable selected capability roots into extension thread state\non resume.\n- Keeps the actual model-context fragment and rollout machinery in core.\n\n## What does not change\n\n- No skill or MCP implementation moves out of its extension.\n- No new file watcher, generation, or RPC.\n- No generic migration of existing World State sections.\n- No change to the stable environment-ID assumption from #29856.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nstep 1 snapshot: skills = []\nstep 2 snapshot: skills = [executor-demo:deploy]\n\ncore asks the skills extension to render only that change.\n```\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **This PR:** let extensions contribute World State sections.\n2. Project executor skills through the skills extension.\n3. Pin one MCP runtime to each model step.\n4. Project selected MCP/app/connector metadata by environment\navailability.\n5. One end-to-end integration scenario.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T21:23:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c9e6d9783dfe99a819f00318f753b6f5cbcc38e8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c9e6d9783dfe99a819f00318f753b6f5cbcc38e8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c9e6d9783dfe99a819f00318f753b6f5cbcc38e8/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"db541f45536f18741b50c74b05904a2c5f628c96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db541f45536f18741b50c74b05904a2c5f628c96","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/db541f45536f18741b50c74b05904a2c5f628c96"}]},{"sha":"db541f45536f18741b50c74b05904a2c5f628c96","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRiNTQxZjQ1NTM2ZjE4NzQxYjUwYzc0YjA1OTA0YTJjNWY2MjhjOTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"felixxia-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:15:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:15:50Z"},"message":"[codex] Add managed MCP server matchers (#29648)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR extends the existing managed `mcp_servers` identity requirement\nso that one name-qualified rule can use either:\n\n- the released exact command or URL identity;\n- an exact stdio executable with an exact-length, ordered argument\nmatcher list; or\n- a direct MCP URL matcher.\n\nMatcher-based rules stay under the released `identity` key and use the\nsame `McpServerRequirement` abstraction and `mcp_servers.<server_name>`\nnamespace.\n\n## Behavior\n\nPolicy activation and name qualification are unchanged:\n\n- If `mcp_servers` is absent, ordinary configured MCP servers remain\nunrestricted.\n- If `mcp_servers` is present, a server needs a matching same-name\nrequirement.\n- `mcp_servers = {}` continues to deny every configured MCP server.\n- Existing exact identity requirements keep their released semantics.\n\nPlugin-bundled MCP servers use the same requirement shapes under\n`plugins.<plugin_name>.mcp_servers.<server_name>`. Top-level non-empty\nrules continue to govern only ordinary configured servers; plugin rules\nremain explicitly plugin-scoped. The existing globally empty\n`mcp_servers = {}` plugin kill switch is preserved.\n\nRequirements layers continue to use the existing regular TOML merge\nbehavior. Atomic replacement of named MCP requirements is intentionally\nout of scope here and is tracked independently in #30118.\n\n## Requirement contract\n\nThe released exact identity contract remains valid:\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.docs.identity]\ncommand = \"codex-mcp\"\n\n[mcp_servers.remote.identity]\nurl = \"https://example.com/mcp\"\n```\n\nCommand identities continue to check only `command`; they do not inspect\narguments, `cwd`, `env`, or `env_vars`.\n\nA command matcher uses an exact executable plus an exact-length, ordered\nargument list. Each argument position supports `exact`, `prefix`, or\nfull-value `regex` matching:\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.internal_mcp_proxy.identity]\ncommand = { executable = \"company-cli\", args = [\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"mcp\" },\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"proxy\" },\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"--server\" },\n  { match = \"regex\", expression = '^https://[A-Za-z0-9-]+\\.mcp\\.internal\\.example\\.com(?::443)?(?:/.*)?$' },\n] }\n```\n\nDirect streamable HTTP MCP definitions can use the same value matcher\ntypes through `identity.url`:\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.internal_http.identity]\nurl = {\n  match = \"regex\",\n  expression = '^https://[A-Za-z0-9-]+\\.mcp\\.internal\\.example\\.com(?:/.*)?$',\n}\n```\n\nPlugin-bundled MCP matchers use the same contract inside the\nplugin-qualified allowlist:\n\n```toml\n[plugins.\"sample@test\".mcp_servers.internal_mcp_proxy.identity]\ncommand = { executable = \"company-cli\", args = [\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"mcp\" },\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"proxy\" },\n] }\n```\n\nRegexes are validated while managed requirements are loaded, and regex\nmatching must cover the complete value. Command matchers constrain only\nthe executable and arguments.\n\n## Why\n\nEnterprise administrators need to allow MCP servers by executable and\npositional-argument shape, including fixed arguments plus constrained\nvalues such as internal MCP URLs passed to a proxy.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-config` (198 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-core mcp_servers_by_matchers --lib` (2 passed)","tree":{"sha":"1e2672529e08e77eb726ac294b4944f80d7e096f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1e2672529e08e77eb726ac294b4944f80d7e096f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/db541f45536f18741b50c74b05904a2c5f628c96","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPZqGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0NMQACEMx4g/Vi75KoO69heRo1xX\nTPISMZT/oQyu2EcKl/VcRWU0j4ruyujoDt47F04FZqX+549rkPGI5srpnNFPSeG7\nXEugNJb7n6YLGoyCiD4cR3zLbCq3/zmyiESMp1zDlwkEV8/pQ8/qszN7Rdqv1VPU\nASpIS3n3k/R9j95B8ASFPBBD7H8QeyGkQKWbKHSKIbP5XaJxcdsGRBes43n2VACf\nzI3CBvl2VLiA/1XLT/tRbZxaWGIdxq7RfdJ/l6w4tayN8V+RC/oVu86Dd7dxPYJk\nHi362kPJ7olG0e0n73v9K50quzmhg6D9ZvywtKlbRFGfJrKwfcJ657SnbdEwKrom\nmQhHY7NMbMU4xVCA1Q3niiwGcjJvX3VuJFsN2m/H7AYh9869xujAtDjI6W6TgXni\nU77IJP/u67Mr6ZrpDGtlAJOAuoRH8ME1FSIPhUWJ+eaIcU5aEDFJz+iD/W+l+aEx\nqyXZ5YM4d9/ZBkJG2xrliGbvgqD+J+h1UVrKgaYfWEZX+PRunwMA1TsaGxWbVLpo\nQTePy9N1aDASsCJfY3U2bHOd8UCeoI+VfojIufGV4ibtY7kWLt+6CBnXOHlERYHI\nA+pHEffr524wteWDnkZDW1WTbWME/jEGybZvgkoRAzzksEi+5EOBDCWjffyJBZ5p\n4TV+tS06dQCBY/BCdY2e\n=7pf9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1e2672529e08e77eb726ac294b4944f80d7e096f\nparent e23e7cbe4634bf1eed1584414e6bbb8a2be349f6\nauthor felixxia-oai <felixxia@openai.com> 1782422150 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782422150 +0100\n\n[codex] Add managed MCP server matchers (#29648)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR extends the existing managed `mcp_servers` identity requirement\nso that one name-qualified rule can use either:\n\n- the released exact command or URL identity;\n- an exact stdio executable with an exact-length, ordered argument\nmatcher list; or\n- a direct MCP URL matcher.\n\nMatcher-based rules stay under the released `identity` key and use the\nsame `McpServerRequirement` abstraction and `mcp_servers.<server_name>`\nnamespace.\n\n## Behavior\n\nPolicy activation and name qualification are unchanged:\n\n- If `mcp_servers` is absent, ordinary configured MCP servers remain\nunrestricted.\n- If `mcp_servers` is present, a server needs a matching same-name\nrequirement.\n- `mcp_servers = {}` continues to deny every configured MCP server.\n- Existing exact identity requirements keep their released semantics.\n\nPlugin-bundled MCP servers use the same requirement shapes under\n`plugins.<plugin_name>.mcp_servers.<server_name>`. Top-level non-empty\nrules continue to govern only ordinary configured servers; plugin rules\nremain explicitly plugin-scoped. The existing globally empty\n`mcp_servers = {}` plugin kill switch is preserved.\n\nRequirements layers continue to use the existing regular TOML merge\nbehavior. Atomic replacement of named MCP requirements is intentionally\nout of scope here and is tracked independently in #30118.\n\n## Requirement contract\n\nThe released exact identity contract remains valid:\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.docs.identity]\ncommand = \"codex-mcp\"\n\n[mcp_servers.remote.identity]\nurl = \"https://example.com/mcp\"\n```\n\nCommand identities continue to check only `command`; they do not inspect\narguments, `cwd`, `env`, or `env_vars`.\n\nA command matcher uses an exact executable plus an exact-length, ordered\nargument list. Each argument position supports `exact`, `prefix`, or\nfull-value `regex` matching:\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.internal_mcp_proxy.identity]\ncommand = { executable = \"company-cli\", args = [\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"mcp\" },\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"proxy\" },\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"--server\" },\n  { match = \"regex\", expression = '^https://[A-Za-z0-9-]+\\.mcp\\.internal\\.example\\.com(?::443)?(?:/.*)?$' },\n] }\n```\n\nDirect streamable HTTP MCP definitions can use the same value matcher\ntypes through `identity.url`:\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.internal_http.identity]\nurl = {\n  match = \"regex\",\n  expression = '^https://[A-Za-z0-9-]+\\.mcp\\.internal\\.example\\.com(?:/.*)?$',\n}\n```\n\nPlugin-bundled MCP matchers use the same contract inside the\nplugin-qualified allowlist:\n\n```toml\n[plugins.\"sample@test\".mcp_servers.internal_mcp_proxy.identity]\ncommand = { executable = \"company-cli\", args = [\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"mcp\" },\n  { match = \"exact\", value = \"proxy\" },\n] }\n```\n\nRegexes are validated while managed requirements are loaded, and regex\nmatching must cover the complete value. Command matchers constrain only\nthe executable and arguments.\n\n## Why\n\nEnterprise administrators need to allow MCP servers by executable and\npositional-argument shape, including fixed arguments plus constrained\nvalues such as internal MCP URLs passed to a proxy.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-config` (198 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-core mcp_servers_by_matchers --lib` (2 passed)","verified_at":"2026-06-25T21:15:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db541f45536f18741b50c74b05904a2c5f628c96","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/db541f45536f18741b50c74b05904a2c5f628c96","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db541f45536f18741b50c74b05904a2c5f628c96/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e23e7cbe4634bf1eed1584414e6bbb8a2be349f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e23e7cbe4634bf1eed1584414e6bbb8a2be349f6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e23e7cbe4634bf1eed1584414e6bbb8a2be349f6"}]},{"sha":"e23e7cbe4634bf1eed1584414e6bbb8a2be349f6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUyM2U3Y2JlNDYzNGJmMWVlZDE1ODQ0MTRlNmJiYjhhMmJlMzQ5ZjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:05:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T21:05:49Z"},"message":"release: consume standalone zsh artifacts (#30116)\n\n## Why\n\nOnce #30114 publishes zsh independently, regular Rust releases should\nreuse that protected, versioned artifact set instead of rebuilding\nidentical zsh binaries for every Codex version. Keeping the zsh release\ntag explicit in the workflow also makes future artifact upgrades\ndeliberate and easy to review.\n\nThis PR assumes the first standalone artifact release will be published\nas `codex-zsh-v0.1.0` before this change lands.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `CODEX_ZSH_RELEASE_TAG` near the top of\n`.github/workflows/rust-release.yml`, initially pinned to\n`codex-zsh-v0.1.0`.\n- Download the standalone release’s generated `codex-zsh` DotSlash\nmanifest before assembling Linux and macOS Codex packages.\n- Added a `--zsh-manifest` package-builder override so release packaging\nfetches the matching target archive and verifies the size and SHA-256\ndigest recorded in that manifest.\n- Removed the reusable zsh build job from regular Rust releases.\n- Stopped copying zsh archives into each Rust release and stopped\nregenerating a zsh DotSlash manifest there.\n\nWindows packaging remains unchanged because the patched zsh resource is\nonly shipped for supported Unix targets.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added package-helper coverage that supplies a standalone manifest\noverride and verifies the extracted zsh bytes.\n- Ran the `scripts/codex_package` unit test suite.\n- Validated `.github/scripts/build-codex-package-archive.sh` with `bash\n-n`.","tree":{"sha":"7729ff01fe5292ac5a28ba224093fc26f2f22ebb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7729ff01fe5292ac5a28ba224093fc26f2f22ebb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e23e7cbe4634bf1eed1584414e6bbb8a2be349f6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPZgtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA74wQAD4q7R72GvuryRq6P+zet0QF\n+HQxlimRLIoxdYWdSARpRfMSxoM9DyVcOckGCNVhpekWR8Rz2HzTcPOQebwjIpZf\nCPRNBzyd0U1klTtxV4OM6w5QW1Dj9WgbMjpN02vPIcYP+gyISSCLhSSb1kpIhPWp\nZrwpczfvlrILF2mV8upViaPlJ1SmmlgHXCRjtQF+UAwc4whCHj+YYnRDX1Dy/HIV\nNiYY+i2ca2Vy8VqLsRO1zzUYNJWMp+Po2mppMOP5KPU0KaJWwC/Yr/etEgc5m6b0\nhw8HEsxdAPekM7GLd1EL3PEGvNHiopuRKNLR8zCEWoErOQur5FuKINrfhGtxlu+o\n6PY7yvraka7+7ZMmSRG6g28e+jXJ2I83r3r71DYbYN+JLkx3qYudjxJuZFtILHGJ\nl/Gw8eyv1GoOpsCylNBFscsXhGC5OwZxK+e8Gamz5QZEp6YjC3WFFJY1mksNvlcs\nD7J0gOBan2YwhhfxIHPGzxi+Ll1oSEGEpvPHx1r6agMySVjhdOUVBeS2fFQuu1ab\nClwBChMa+H5t6HDlU8f0RITvw/JqdrDKTCXSb0r29U0yCzomnbxKtyHhtcpPDMmg\nd4pFYKqjG/Wiesn2a3uOaxDLRXULnN6rFN30xxuCnMupkyQgKycH37c2bn4lThjo\n3svVOwDAVyVULuT7zZqV\n=C6cT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7729ff01fe5292ac5a28ba224093fc26f2f22ebb\nparent 891f1f4c8584a082fc4658cabd48f1a8b01354e0\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782421549 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782421549 -0700\n\nrelease: consume standalone zsh artifacts (#30116)\n\n## Why\n\nOnce #30114 publishes zsh independently, regular Rust releases should\nreuse that protected, versioned artifact set instead of rebuilding\nidentical zsh binaries for every Codex version. Keeping the zsh release\ntag explicit in the workflow also makes future artifact upgrades\ndeliberate and easy to review.\n\nThis PR assumes the first standalone artifact release will be published\nas `codex-zsh-v0.1.0` before this change lands.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `CODEX_ZSH_RELEASE_TAG` near the top of\n`.github/workflows/rust-release.yml`, initially pinned to\n`codex-zsh-v0.1.0`.\n- Download the standalone release’s generated `codex-zsh` DotSlash\nmanifest before assembling Linux and macOS Codex packages.\n- Added a `--zsh-manifest` package-builder override so release packaging\nfetches the matching target archive and verifies the size and SHA-256\ndigest recorded in that manifest.\n- Removed the reusable zsh build job from regular Rust releases.\n- Stopped copying zsh archives into each Rust release and stopped\nregenerating a zsh DotSlash manifest there.\n\nWindows packaging remains unchanged because the patched zsh resource is\nonly shipped for supported Unix targets.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added package-helper coverage that supplies a standalone manifest\noverride and verifies the extracted zsh bytes.\n- Ran the `scripts/codex_package` unit test suite.\n- Validated `.github/scripts/build-codex-package-archive.sh` with `bash\n-n`.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T21:05:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e23e7cbe4634bf1eed1584414e6bbb8a2be349f6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e23e7cbe4634bf1eed1584414e6bbb8a2be349f6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e23e7cbe4634bf1eed1584414e6bbb8a2be349f6/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"891f1f4c8584a082fc4658cabd48f1a8b01354e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/891f1f4c8584a082fc4658cabd48f1a8b01354e0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/891f1f4c8584a082fc4658cabd48f1a8b01354e0"}]},{"sha":"891f1f4c8584a082fc4658cabd48f1a8b01354e0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg5MWYxZjRjODU4NGEwODJmYzQ2NThjYWJkNDhmMWE4YjAxMzU0ZTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:56:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:56:08Z"},"message":"release: publish standalone zsh artifacts (#30114)\n\n## Why\n\nThe patched zsh artifacts rarely change, but\n`.github/workflows/rust-release-zsh.yml` currently runs as part of every\nRust release. Rebuilding the same four binaries for each Codex version\nwastes release capacity and ties an independently versioned runtime\ndependency to the main release cadence.\n\nThis establishes the producer side of a build-once flow. The existing\nRust release workflow remains unchanged until the first standalone\nartifact release has been published and the checked-in DotSlash\nmanifests can be updated with its URLs and checksums.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Run the zsh release workflow for protected `codex-zsh-vX.Y.Z` tags\ninstead of as a reusable workflow.\n- Validate the semantic release tag before starting the platform builds.\n- Publish the four zsh archives to a GitHub prerelease so the release\nnever becomes the repository latest release.\n- Publish the generated `codex-zsh` DotSlash manifest alongside the\narchives.\n- Document how to publish the next artifact version after changing the\npinned zsh commit or patch.\n\n## Tag protection\n\nAn active repository tag ruleset named `codex-zsh-v*.*.*` targets\n`refs/tags/codex-zsh-v*.*.*`. It restricts tag creation, updates,\ndeletion, and non-fast-forward changes; requires linear history; and\nlimits bypass to the configured repository role.\n\nThis was verified with:\n\n```shell\ngh api repos/openai/codex/rulesets/18140982\n```\n\nThe response reported `\"enforcement\":\"active\"`, the expected tag\ncondition, and the `creation`, `update`, `deletion`, `non_fast_forward`,\nand `required_linear_history` rules.\n\n## Rollout\n\nAfter this lands, publish the first `codex-zsh-vX.Y.Z` release. A\nfollow-up can then update the checked-in DotSlash manifests and remove\nthe zsh rebuild from `.github/workflows/rust-release.yml`.\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/30114).\n* #30116\n* __->__ #30114","tree":{"sha":"0918bcfa6b2f99bfcfed0ec33d85e1cbdd0837bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0918bcfa6b2f99bfcfed0ec33d85e1cbdd0837bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/891f1f4c8584a082fc4658cabd48f1a8b01354e0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPZXoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN/gQAGrZ7VSfAMPiD8hfwSf6uIJQ\n5BZu6wIpwGMX4uWJdEmCgjw/VYxwih0w0bMAqoe6h2ME/w9iVj+87KE6YrikEIbY\nhig4b3/gfAIBc29pzNeF7ryXs/d+2Kj86G9oe3INykoRBEP2WCNsdfEo9XPZSSSL\nil0tEIpFIVX2JHSQ1ehRROx5odr0u7npaQl3t6G0IB51KHirfuYs0CboAbgHDz3+\nTufeO0N5awmC+ByEsVMgNfN8w7ek+h+EmOKyo7BbTTByHrHxDvqvJ2QVlxnedElH\n0hHlzQnMhl+m7XTd+e+9IQBBJUmsHPpPHWaugCad6kLFTT41WjcYZqVvp93R54sF\nRuXmApXq98WFEUYHH243OlYS686yVMVbBsGfDnaTyoXxKV1llE4KC/VDywtmcSca\nPYh7qMfgc3RJnEBclF6FH1m8WEEo5zL4RRCotlDfctkzmh4Q/wwjDKvQFP2nvMIl\ne5adIgu+jtFF1xnJC4hPn47rOmBqCs6ONCXMJKWyd2d59azT+LhtUQHfZSjS+ZOk\nWTGhweHZuRcqTOj3QyQNA/fFH/Ng/ktx8vBwOvTW2kI0oAM8t1UePem2ViiNzvCg\nHqcur/NPffpEiM7+EuWjCt/Q74hY0nZ0P4AtPjV98gNM1BKdXGsp2uLIg6ctBHqw\nJeatEr1ef5FtANWxyydq\n=+6Fy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0918bcfa6b2f99bfcfed0ec33d85e1cbdd0837bd\nparent 703793c22efc1e47de51703150f5cf16976ff456\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782420968 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782420968 -0700\n\nrelease: publish standalone zsh artifacts (#30114)\n\n## Why\n\nThe patched zsh artifacts rarely change, but\n`.github/workflows/rust-release-zsh.yml` currently runs as part of every\nRust release. Rebuilding the same four binaries for each Codex version\nwastes release capacity and ties an independently versioned runtime\ndependency to the main release cadence.\n\nThis establishes the producer side of a build-once flow. The existing\nRust release workflow remains unchanged until the first standalone\nartifact release has been published and the checked-in DotSlash\nmanifests can be updated with its URLs and checksums.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Run the zsh release workflow for protected `codex-zsh-vX.Y.Z` tags\ninstead of as a reusable workflow.\n- Validate the semantic release tag before starting the platform builds.\n- Publish the four zsh archives to a GitHub prerelease so the release\nnever becomes the repository latest release.\n- Publish the generated `codex-zsh` DotSlash manifest alongside the\narchives.\n- Document how to publish the next artifact version after changing the\npinned zsh commit or patch.\n\n## Tag protection\n\nAn active repository tag ruleset named `codex-zsh-v*.*.*` targets\n`refs/tags/codex-zsh-v*.*.*`. It restricts tag creation, updates,\ndeletion, and non-fast-forward changes; requires linear history; and\nlimits bypass to the configured repository role.\n\nThis was verified with:\n\n```shell\ngh api repos/openai/codex/rulesets/18140982\n```\n\nThe response reported `\"enforcement\":\"active\"`, the expected tag\ncondition, and the `creation`, `update`, `deletion`, `non_fast_forward`,\nand `required_linear_history` rules.\n\n## Rollout\n\nAfter this lands, publish the first `codex-zsh-vX.Y.Z` release. A\nfollow-up can then update the checked-in DotSlash manifests and remove\nthe zsh rebuild from `.github/workflows/rust-release.yml`.\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/30114).\n* #30116\n* __->__ #30114","verified_at":"2026-06-25T20:56:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/891f1f4c8584a082fc4658cabd48f1a8b01354e0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/891f1f4c8584a082fc4658cabd48f1a8b01354e0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/891f1f4c8584a082fc4658cabd48f1a8b01354e0/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"703793c22efc1e47de51703150f5cf16976ff456","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/703793c22efc1e47de51703150f5cf16976ff456","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/703793c22efc1e47de51703150f5cf16976ff456"}]},{"sha":"703793c22efc1e47de51703150f5cf16976ff456","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDcwMzc5M2MyMmVmYzFlNDdkZTUxNzAzMTUwZjVjZjE2OTc2ZmY0NTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:54:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:54:48Z"},"message":"feat(core, mcp): cache codex_apps tools in memory (#29003)\n\n## Description\n\nThis makes Codex Apps tool reads use a shared in-memory snapshot instead\nof rereading the disk cache every time `list_all_tools()` runs. Disk\nstill seeds the cache on startup and gets updated after successful\nfetches, but it is no longer the live read path.\n\nThe core change is that `McpManager` now owns a process-scoped\n`CodexAppsToolsCache`. Codex threads in the same app-server process now\nshare this Codex Apps in-memory tools snapshot. The snapshot is keyed by\nthe Codex home plus the Codex Apps identity: the active Codex auth\nuser/workspace and the effective Codex Apps MCP source config.\n\nThere's already code to hard-refresh the cache, so we respect it in this\nPR.\n\n## Local benchmark\n\nI ran a local steady-state microbenchmark of the exact repeated Codex\nApps cached-tools read this PR removes, using the same real local cache\npayload in both trees: `3,678,138` bytes and `381` tools. The cache file\nwas already warm in the OS page cache, so this measures same-process\nreread/deserialization work rather than cold-disk latency or full turn\nlatency. Each run is 25 iterations (mimicking a turn that makes 25\ninference calls).\n\n| Version | Run 1 | Run 2 | Avg |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `origin/main` disk read + JSON deserialize + `filter_tools` | `50.755\nms` | `52.894 ms` | `51.825 ms` |\n| This branch in-memory `current_tools` + `filter_tools` | `0.740 ms` |\n`0.778 ms` | `0.759 ms` |\n\nThat removes about `51 ms` from each repeated Codex Apps cached-tools\nread on this machine, roughly `68x` faster for that subpath. It is\nuseful evidence for the hot path this PR changes, but not a claim that\nevery production turn gets `51 ms` faster; end-to-end impact also\ndepends on the rest of `list_all_tools()` and tool-payload construction.\n\nThis is on my M2 Max macbook, so with a slower disk this would be much\nworse (and indeed we did see this really blew up turn runtime with a\nslow disk).","tree":{"sha":"e8e94a080bf2487f0d2c6024bde5e4ca5100a848","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e8e94a080bf2487f0d2c6024bde5e4ca5100a848"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/703793c22efc1e47de51703150f5cf16976ff456","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPZWYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC3kQADlGXp/Rh6Ka2X8SpPAdmdHc\nYYJY/xV6jiqN3I3FqhG8+n24aZU7bh5P+Svn62gpKUJBVGGlpFPxYqA05xkTzkk3\nXCzmrCfMJoX+Ee9c70cLljuUN3DnU7ecTUOBu5JrwIRJPuBMye5C9EOizGGViaeg\nQQC6uptGbS5vIkNfduxXPKsAN2rls42CcvGmW2mfK1GzTVxW9wQTmKQFDo4UHdH4\nFit5HmUiN0IpEj4pDy59JJuyfNdSprymndDWhVhdns8ASVCf0GEUFCL3srYZW1s2\nxP//onB2oTCXq1unHseiTALPHg+LdeBDXKvNgDzJyK86Pn0v/em99YX1YDyhtNzh\nakXuV5SjkPXDJQVlHSg0ff1HSvo6aCJC/Ad3b7Oteh7ApwfyRY9ySL3jrbD7sQXY\nSjMlmQOV19pN0kORyGdDral/cAqvwiA8MzErlDeP0v8tkyFpZ/psBGZjAkKGI8wk\nCn/C718EC1cBQOYDIbwML7xVgRyD5muM3H8/Wx3SM5Klo6NKujJjAzoocwv/Ro35\nHfEs1N9XAvSPRePWD85bSMXaZVx8RHJ7PQBQNsQ1DbtYyKU6nwFuFQRL6aMxL3CT\ni8K592K+3TQmnIgARE3jrgu4gIouTzwGRzLpvN0AWlVpLA4al3kzBRHbHV3egRFs\n2+JyqcDI14KNkF+fAHy4\n=URKF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e8e94a080bf2487f0d2c6024bde5e4ca5100a848\nparent 62c7f506d9a8892724ee025da04bfef74f092ccb\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1782420888 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782420888 +0000\n\nfeat(core, mcp): cache codex_apps tools in memory (#29003)\n\n## Description\n\nThis makes Codex Apps tool reads use a shared in-memory snapshot instead\nof rereading the disk cache every time `list_all_tools()` runs. Disk\nstill seeds the cache on startup and gets updated after successful\nfetches, but it is no longer the live read path.\n\nThe core change is that `McpManager` now owns a process-scoped\n`CodexAppsToolsCache`. Codex threads in the same app-server process now\nshare this Codex Apps in-memory tools snapshot. The snapshot is keyed by\nthe Codex home plus the Codex Apps identity: the active Codex auth\nuser/workspace and the effective Codex Apps MCP source config.\n\nThere's already code to hard-refresh the cache, so we respect it in this\nPR.\n\n## Local benchmark\n\nI ran a local steady-state microbenchmark of the exact repeated Codex\nApps cached-tools read this PR removes, using the same real local cache\npayload in both trees: `3,678,138` bytes and `381` tools. The cache file\nwas already warm in the OS page cache, so this measures same-process\nreread/deserialization work rather than cold-disk latency or full turn\nlatency. Each run is 25 iterations (mimicking a turn that makes 25\ninference calls).\n\n| Version | Run 1 | Run 2 | Avg |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `origin/main` disk read + JSON deserialize + `filter_tools` | `50.755\nms` | `52.894 ms` | `51.825 ms` |\n| This branch in-memory `current_tools` + `filter_tools` | `0.740 ms` |\n`0.778 ms` | `0.759 ms` |\n\nThat removes about `51 ms` from each repeated Codex Apps cached-tools\nread on this machine, roughly `68x` faster for that subpath. It is\nuseful evidence for the hot path this PR changes, but not a claim that\nevery production turn gets `51 ms` faster; end-to-end impact also\ndepends on the rest of `list_all_tools()` and tool-payload construction.\n\nThis is on my M2 Max macbook, so with a slower disk this would be much\nworse (and indeed we did see this really blew up turn runtime with a\nslow disk).","verified_at":"2026-06-25T20:54:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/703793c22efc1e47de51703150f5cf16976ff456","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/703793c22efc1e47de51703150f5cf16976ff456","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/703793c22efc1e47de51703150f5cf16976ff456/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"62c7f506d9a8892724ee025da04bfef74f092ccb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/62c7f506d9a8892724ee025da04bfef74f092ccb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/62c7f506d9a8892724ee025da04bfef74f092ccb"}]},{"sha":"62c7f506d9a8892724ee025da04bfef74f092ccb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYyYzdmNTA2ZDlhODg5MjcyNGVlMDI1ZGEwNGJmZWY3NGYwOTJjY2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:46:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:46:42Z"},"message":"[codex] poll external clock during sleep (#30113)\n\n## Summary\n\n- make the external app-server time provider establish sleep deadlines\nusing `currentTime/read`\n- poll the external clock once per second and complete `clock.sleep`\nwhen the deadline is reached\n- keep the system-clock timer and existing steer/agent-message\ninterruption behavior unchanged\n\n## Why\n\nThis lets training control `clock.sleep` through its existing external\nsimulated clock without adding separate sleep/wake protocol methods.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nexternal_sleep_polls_current_time_and_emits_items`","tree":{"sha":"528e7badf7eeb9f342f390a422e0aa1cf38b9d89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/528e7badf7eeb9f342f390a422e0aa1cf38b9d89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/62c7f506d9a8892724ee025da04bfef74f092ccb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPZOyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXQkQABItPq1SEYOeU9bFTcQu9sst\n1BYQ0jjxi8YFQdUXToCQNVHOBQ6hvgHAdDF9Hu1nRzPYU/5AGv0PViURsI4MxUKL\nMEENpwAZvJOHog+fVZkWYb37cv+byAwrndEEJ1fM2iqUqSzN+0vJDsPwhidn17CM\nEzVVCmzFhomstimKNhSkPIo12q4Ou2dC+cx1wAbY8Afb8T8SfoPB+36RfTgB9oZP\n2owLiZh+ZNuX97MUJBR282gtA+2TEbxXD8sI0toZGMMuLtFzBbct3mYQ8EBsg5k6\nY6wTH5rxK38qYjk33VHNBzp7U704mZclpA8S5gACdZOSPX/b3OPp7U8aM74yWOb6\n5fYpwN1WN7MOqFzCWQTPExv0ZWtM7u3BQXauymL5lRLdTQ/VdCIGlpginoEadTdG\n1qmSeYV6RintQcS9vuPxS9bBraP6eaHbM/m++WfMiKbdajnXrntxaZTH/cYxQw0z\nzZto2OkAKpxpdq+g+Mkw5q20WcnZq6YNSVTNswKx+LbOmqykGVXcs/B9aa+o5n3L\nbSjhJzdlq1mW9S/s1hKXanSjGVBhtUAfl3r9YsZPKxVLJkXskNsWKZjJmECdOY7L\nTcES/rHM+RRaHzHfAnwRlYAK1jQwjhcvCZ73vnnuqTiNSLTZ4yGlUc3Bs8B4iHX1\nX76ZApPLXYAlHh53fRa+\n=j9Bf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 528e7badf7eeb9f342f390a422e0aa1cf38b9d89\nparent 3b22498f69112eb1f7dd3061e278e344626e834c\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782420402 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782420402 -0700\n\n[codex] poll external clock during sleep (#30113)\n\n## Summary\n\n- make the external app-server time provider establish sleep deadlines\nusing `currentTime/read`\n- poll the external clock once per second and complete `clock.sleep`\nwhen the deadline is reached\n- keep the system-clock timer and existing steer/agent-message\ninterruption behavior unchanged\n\n## Why\n\nThis lets training control `clock.sleep` through its existing external\nsimulated clock without adding separate sleep/wake protocol methods.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nexternal_sleep_polls_current_time_and_emits_items`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T20:46:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/62c7f506d9a8892724ee025da04bfef74f092ccb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/62c7f506d9a8892724ee025da04bfef74f092ccb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/62c7f506d9a8892724ee025da04bfef74f092ccb/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3b22498f69112eb1f7dd3061e278e344626e834c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b22498f69112eb1f7dd3061e278e344626e834c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b22498f69112eb1f7dd3061e278e344626e834c"}]},{"sha":"3b22498f69112eb1f7dd3061e278e344626e834c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNiMjI0OThmNjkxMTJlYjFmN2RkMzA2MWUyNzhlMzQ0NjI2ZTgzNGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"richardopenai","email":"richardlee@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:42:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:42:40Z"},"message":"[codex] Observe remote exec-server lifecycle (#27470)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Record bounded duration and outcome metrics for remote environment\nregistration and Noise rendezvous connection attempts.\n- Count reconnects by bounded reason: disconnect, connection failure, or\nrejected registration.\n- Trace registration at the owning client boundary without exporting raw\nenvironment or registration identifiers.\n- Replace the stale pre-Noise WebSocket observability design with the\ncurrent remote transport model.\n\n## Stack\n\nReview and land this stack in order:\n\n1. #27466 — trace exec-server JSON-RPC requests\n2. #27467 — record bounded connection, request, and process lifecycle\nmetrics\n3. #27470 — observe remote registration and Noise rendezvous lifecycle\n**(this PR)**\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server --lib` (149 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-cli --test exec_server` (4 passed)\n- `just argument-comment-lint`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server -p codex-cli`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"a8203566b193167b465964f684b4d0aecf0b4d3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a8203566b193167b465964f684b4d0aecf0b4d3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3b22498f69112eb1f7dd3061e278e344626e834c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPZLACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALakQAFogsQ526dnr44PkO1x3AL8y\nnLuwPAYofzMS5M037tzNjlIfmptmMBdLba78B/OR//1EVNGg6HyZIefmvvhX1peg\n5YIv4GxQ8b/aua1fz7qPERKyVjZiir46QhWwtChuUBetw/OLqEBBt1v0pCLdoTW3\nQDj7GLHi4uXU5YMxGnsT8GJ9eAi72mp5pmmv+UuaU+a8IUr90i3raK3nvgoYxcmO\n7eGd3gOkn3SaluDdxfufJGrG46/jLEs6rEV2Y5r3Uu7FnZ9CUUUTgBbnVkgoXXlw\nLnGrdKs3nbtI5r5UY8orjA2DyjFzfsc81tcr93z86jOsPPt1dT1jEwMjUxTmYIpG\nBddiL9996t5+0g5Fg0WqERTYqnTgVVI4rRnfXGJTw61QFcksqxR4ssVx13eNcL8d\n1U1nyFd3y/wKYdGeSgAw/2NmCCWlembP4Opi1hEBC1Rea1gint4+fD7VBiIZtvdH\nksiUXb5S882iwZpiGn2muAHfFLmWbkN5QIQIYVgVWoVn59yGlFPIy/TvQBWROqth\nKHGyogi26DacyjiPT+ULq6TEzRZJKoBCB0taXYJeqKpljqoDf9BTVWfZ4g8uKG9x\nKVQYT0S5OWdqs/tb61B0XqfYCDfzevh2xIJLnLCLWbX0a/hFGSb8ac9brKFMY99K\nlSRmTdpiLzfnY3wvsqyN\n=/WXJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a8203566b193167b465964f684b4d0aecf0b4d3c\nparent 3b78f58fb2e672fc1e5f808963dc65544f571392\nauthor richardopenai <richardlee@openai.com> 1782420160 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782420160 -0700\n\n[codex] Observe remote exec-server lifecycle (#27470)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Record bounded duration and outcome metrics for remote environment\nregistration and Noise rendezvous connection attempts.\n- Count reconnects by bounded reason: disconnect, connection failure, or\nrejected registration.\n- Trace registration at the owning client boundary without exporting raw\nenvironment or registration identifiers.\n- Replace the stale pre-Noise WebSocket observability design with the\ncurrent remote transport model.\n\n## Stack\n\nReview and land this stack in order:\n\n1. #27466 — trace exec-server JSON-RPC requests\n2. #27467 — record bounded connection, request, and process lifecycle\nmetrics\n3. #27470 — observe remote registration and Noise rendezvous lifecycle\n**(this PR)**\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server --lib` (149 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-cli --test exec_server` (4 passed)\n- `just argument-comment-lint`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server -p codex-cli`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T20:42:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b22498f69112eb1f7dd3061e278e344626e834c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b22498f69112eb1f7dd3061e278e344626e834c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b22498f69112eb1f7dd3061e278e344626e834c/comments","author":{"login":"richardopenai","id":272641442,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAtog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272641442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai","html_url":"https://github.com/richardopenai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3b78f58fb2e672fc1e5f808963dc65544f571392","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b78f58fb2e672fc1e5f808963dc65544f571392","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b78f58fb2e672fc1e5f808963dc65544f571392"}]},{"sha":"3b78f58fb2e672fc1e5f808963dc65544f571392","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNiNzhmNThmYjJlNjcyZmMxZTVmODA4OTYzZGM2NTU0NGY1NzEzOTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:26:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T20:26:47Z"},"message":"[codex] extend code-mode host IPC transport (#30108)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add an `EncodedFrame` type so IPC payloads are serialized and\nsize-checked before entering bounded queues\n- add the V1 `operation/cancel` client-to-host message\n- pin the new wire shape with protocol tests\n\n## Why\n\nThe process-owned code-mode host needs bounded, pre-encoded outbound\nmessages and a best-effort cancellation signal. Keeping these wire\nprimitives in a protocol-only change lets their compatibility contract\nbe reviewed independently from either endpoint.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is **1 of 4** in the process-owned code-mode session stack. The\nnext PR targets this branch.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode-protocol` — 22 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode-protocol`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"1bdebce2a769e1941bfacc188cb0703e67cb8236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1bdebce2a769e1941bfacc188cb0703e67cb8236"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3b78f58fb2e672fc1e5f808963dc65544f571392","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPY8HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAApcQAB3tXJYD/8/O0SMUuiIdeT2U\nCB3FHq5UHdV3s7scy0tJTQGeuQiY2+wSa1vF1spx3q+nxqHwB9/PfTs22Mahj7Pt\nqdFiuYpKa4Jamt5ZiopXa72fs9WHhGSlqYHFO+qWzdeSk8wpPC+RK8BSsVvBrZIt\nkRoYldT6xNEHX4KSAH7aZm5RlIZvHQaz1MIqyQZDTop4aMuuehmkHCB3z6ANHjfY\nGPC1ZQZlVHVLcUvtzeLdmUmARtDT8o09LQZUmFsyix1I3IpKs9+WMm2d9w+rMiUw\n+l26GFnYteLwa7KHQ5fqPU7sDWG2CJJXkBFeDeOea+pEXyG4WlKtg2eYslcrMI5K\nLKOJ7OxasD/KbOjRbvKly8NROLRn/tToZn79a7tDc8c3sdBiieIJPnnoUSfTb6Vf\nWT545zV8zTI4UQT5hZj9Y1UsdvbAkGF/KZfHkTSP4PweJAANs6ke8vLT+kn4gmZ9\nT5WfiIKOOCQy0IMK/M4L3uoMeVX40WoxROgKKahL6KKmd0Es4ByEtcSY3EA9RxXP\novZQYjjD14a27EhSRN31WxKnwhEhvS1qyNr4XcsmBv66VmFD2BorOYdBVDFJpJLW\nXVsj63xcDECRaMGp2U3KDoYhg5F/Ugc01hu2E6+q9pEfHihi0Pck0yONAtR/Y7f2\nzivwavIlmaQYBlfxGSuj\n=zvYO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1bdebce2a769e1941bfacc188cb0703e67cb8236\nparent adccb464d075a39d5450d6bc879e3bb6c97ce14b\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782419207 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782419207 -0700\n\n[codex] extend code-mode host IPC transport (#30108)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add an `EncodedFrame` type so IPC payloads are serialized and\nsize-checked before entering bounded queues\n- add the V1 `operation/cancel` client-to-host message\n- pin the new wire shape with protocol tests\n\n## Why\n\nThe process-owned code-mode host needs bounded, pre-encoded outbound\nmessages and a best-effort cancellation signal. Keeping these wire\nprimitives in a protocol-only change lets their compatibility contract\nbe reviewed independently from either endpoint.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is **1 of 4** in the process-owned code-mode session stack. The\nnext PR targets this branch.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode-protocol` — 22 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-code-mode-protocol`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T20:26:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b78f58fb2e672fc1e5f808963dc65544f571392","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b78f58fb2e672fc1e5f808963dc65544f571392","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b78f58fb2e672fc1e5f808963dc65544f571392/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":