://github.com/openai/codex/commit/adccb464d075a39d5450d6bc879e3bb6c97ce14b"}]},{"sha":"adccb464d075a39d5450d6bc879e3bb6c97ce14b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFkY2NiNDY0ZDA3NWEzOWQ1NDUwZDZiYzg3OWUzYmI2Yzk3Y2UxNGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T19:28:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T19:28:50Z"},"message":"[codex] impl delivery_mode: current time reminders on response boundaries (#30033)\n\n## Summary\n- track user-like input and tool-output boundaries in current-time\nreminder state\n- gate reminder injection when delivery_mode is\nafter_user_or_tool_output\n- preserve interval debounce and forced reminders after context-window\nchanges\n\n## Why\nTraining can request reminders only after user or tool-output items\nwhile keeping the existing canonical pre-inference history-injection\npath.\n\n## Validation\n- just test -p codex-core\ncurrent_time_reminders_can_follow_only_user_or_tool_outputs\n- just test -p codex-core\ncurrent_time_reminders_follow_time_interval_and_persist_in_history\n- just test -p codex-core\ncurrent_time_reminder_is_refreshed_after_compaction\n- just fix -p codex-core","tree":{"sha":"bc07ec09a6337c7ced0e2ed2dda7d85166ef7590","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bc07ec09a6337c7ced0e2ed2dda7d85166ef7590"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/adccb464d075a39d5450d6bc879e3bb6c97ce14b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPYFyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0TUQAHEjwrUDXwLE5IX83HIvhwiM\nuuIGTITPpjr5Xrhzao4Gk45fiJhJgMol3dYPPIOtulZxAWWvANrtbHNiKDtvuAd8\ntTlge93UDouF4rtyK14dwsQBxk05eXp4wpAc+kifJdG25vBM0OuT8CP+ukJRaLqO\nSPow5DlHmVzKZOpRLNlGKm0p7mcMAvcztQXeUJZTVfFh9jctRDuCgokb29vPaxtI\nOaTQevki0GR/8W6P6C3WQvvIOqAkF9uF+FhWaz7UZ/qNrF/i1ryDt1Qt8urtA9sZ\nB/4fnePaKKUpthDM0yIHdCGDtV2wUO4JrWuoomejxKDqqhsqj0UEUz0tma4GN5s1\nPCwvidT7mnh5scFo/lho9uGcmvjn44o6xXkV0t8RhgBED8ffWb3QyzIAMJRkfvbl\ny/WZqPiXGqyYIkL2XLhFKVW9MxB94Q/lNwCmVWINhFC//nbMQ5HAjjyh885rOd/6\nI5ImsH536ARpApYogJcDv/TZkRrpjCmft/QTt7a6abjHYEpjfr+NHvY0aallMVbd\nWOMTGo5E2pXFtQRDMoY6u7mRJU2MxmGIB7vFzAAU7VSSxBjbfcLw1+tR2BreQWIB\nhCXlxDZ+nt7GP8FuCl4wLmQAJvKaHHRDTbUWjF3J5iJ9DVE++kGgrMCZ1XfxncR+\nw3rAzO7OBBO8n6l+yfrT\n=y5+w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bc07ec09a6337c7ced0e2ed2dda7d85166ef7590\nparent 964b138c3db16088a3bff5cc599bfd31428d03e9\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782415730 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782415730 +0000\n\n[codex] impl delivery_mode: current time reminders on response boundaries (#30033)\n\n## Summary\n- track user-like input and tool-output boundaries in current-time\nreminder state\n- gate reminder injection when delivery_mode is\nafter_user_or_tool_output\n- preserve interval debounce and forced reminders after context-window\nchanges\n\n## Why\nTraining can request reminders only after user or tool-output items\nwhile keeping the existing canonical pre-inference history-injection\npath.\n\n## Validation\n- just test -p codex-core\ncurrent_time_reminders_can_follow_only_user_or_tool_outputs\n- just test -p codex-core\ncurrent_time_reminders_follow_time_interval_and_persist_in_history\n- just test -p codex-core\ncurrent_time_reminder_is_refreshed_after_compaction\n- just fix -p codex-core","verified_at":"2026-06-25T19:28:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/adccb464d075a39d5450d6bc879e3bb6c97ce14b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/adccb464d075a39d5450d6bc879e3bb6c97ce14b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/adccb464d075a39d5450d6bc879e3bb6c97ce14b/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"964b138c3db16088a3bff5cc599bfd31428d03e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/964b138c3db16088a3bff5cc599bfd31428d03e9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/964b138c3db16088a3bff5cc599bfd31428d03e9"}]},{"sha":"964b138c3db16088a3bff5cc599bfd31428d03e9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk2NGIxMzhjM2RiMTYwODhhM2JmZjVjYzU5OWJmZDMxNDI4ZDAzZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"richardopenai","email":"richardlee@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T19:25:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T19:25:04Z"},"message":"[codex] Retry temporarily offline exec-server recovery (#30098)\n\n## Summary\n\n- retry ERS `409 environment_offline` responses inside the existing\nexec-server recovery loop\n- keep all other registry conflicts terminal\n- add focused coverage for both cases\n\n## Root cause\n\nWhen an exec server disconnects and reconnects, the client already\nstarts recovery and calls ERS `/connect`. During the transient executor\npresence gap, ERS can return `409 environment_offline`. The retry\nclassifier treated every 409 as terminal, so the first response aborted\nthe existing 25-second recovery window before the executor came back\nonline. That then caused active processes to be marked lost.\n\nThis change classifies only the structured `environment_offline`\nconflict as retryable. Recovery continues with the existing bounded\ndeadline, exponential backoff, and jitter.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server client::recovery::tests` — 4 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server` — passed\n- `just fmt` — passed\n- Full `just test -p codex-exec-server` reached unrelated macOS\nfilesystem-sandbox integration failures because nested\n`/usr/bin/sandbox-exec` is denied in this environment (`sandbox_apply:\nOperation not permitted`).","tree":{"sha":"0283f5e05d8443880dc24b4b36cc46b495ea7a15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0283f5e05d8443880dc24b4b36cc46b495ea7a15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/964b138c3db16088a3bff5cc599bfd31428d03e9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPYCQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABIUQAEGo2yXK6Dy/WQaAgOz43sC+\nN8yg7EsUG3gBRzeAFYOiJtRxJOv5Yp3Y/SuG7wTbqhFgZA4Fnm7Wcypxvu4X2CUd\nE0drr/BT9SOZaDnwn1sgvX1xt5rEzyoxyT3AZ4OW4BXRKPGG5zkS01fxKzuDLbj/\nR9e7TddPq1EXdJGj1ebju8aERGUUOa2fY5nQI/TgIG1WrMvL4rkpReko5xvhk0Kc\nrATXcxl3kAB0Spew88WFTwR5CqL3sYzWV+Qb7I9R1wBfPDy0ZypGXKMruS91B9tS\nhDtbm2j6SQ0UHkA/CubBTioU8vqqCFhnleN1Su8U7ZSjGkYxLlHZJ0org6QrVcqa\nsQ5jjoSU7RtSAEXL/HqCORgcFNXFV/ZKLNma8lEHuNEh5GcQQCpJRYwg6mLJDjQZ\n7GeI98hf+j7qYzxZ+erXdKNz9tWkiA+BVQ6D8RQBDMJwICBGJ8OgtsGwJOBABH7b\nR6crGTKbe2y+cyIMw6iwKKlykP9vE+fpK7P4quYsKCGaw0t2DgYJpak7ujDuXc1y\nPhsk4Ii7kcZvGaX9U1EIh3WMMaHgNsjH2TIEbH7OBZc9v0UPZxRFOfLJ3gIqQB5v\nbJCsBugmmvmIf5s1m2swUMP6jdhf1b7rr92dEy/knyj3S4pWtiGDiu8C4Y7B/jtx\nAXVw13M8ZQn+jCgkkj3D\n=1ykS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0283f5e05d8443880dc24b4b36cc46b495ea7a15\nparent e8d4a1a411bbab9be85e704ae3847915916bf347\nauthor richardopenai <richardlee@openai.com> 1782415504 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782415504 +0000\n\n[codex] Retry temporarily offline exec-server recovery (#30098)\n\n## Summary\n\n- retry ERS `409 environment_offline` responses inside the existing\nexec-server recovery loop\n- keep all other registry conflicts terminal\n- add focused coverage for both cases\n\n## Root cause\n\nWhen an exec server disconnects and reconnects, the client already\nstarts recovery and calls ERS `/connect`. During the transient executor\npresence gap, ERS can return `409 environment_offline`. The retry\nclassifier treated every 409 as terminal, so the first response aborted\nthe existing 25-second recovery window before the executor came back\nonline. That then caused active processes to be marked lost.\n\nThis change classifies only the structured `environment_offline`\nconflict as retryable. Recovery continues with the existing bounded\ndeadline, exponential backoff, and jitter.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server client::recovery::tests` — 4 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server` — passed\n- `just fmt` — passed\n- Full `just test -p codex-exec-server` reached unrelated macOS\nfilesystem-sandbox integration failures because nested\n`/usr/bin/sandbox-exec` is denied in this environment (`sandbox_apply:\nOperation not permitted`).","verified_at":"2026-06-25T19:25:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/964b138c3db16088a3bff5cc599bfd31428d03e9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/964b138c3db16088a3bff5cc599bfd31428d03e9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/964b138c3db16088a3bff5cc599bfd31428d03e9/comments","author":{"login":"richardopenai","id":272641442,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAtog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272641442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai","html_url":"https://github.com/richardopenai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e8d4a1a411bbab9be85e704ae3847915916bf347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e8d4a1a411bbab9be85e704ae3847915916bf347","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e8d4a1a411bbab9be85e704ae3847915916bf347"}]},{"sha":"e8d4a1a411bbab9be85e704ae3847915916bf347","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU4ZDRhMWE0MTFiYmFiOWJlODVlNzA0YWUzODQ3OTE1OTE2YmYzNDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T19:06:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T19:06:43Z"},"message":"[codex] add current time reminder delivery mode config (#30031)\n\n```python\ndelivery_mode = \"any_inference\" # default\ndelivery_mode = \"after_user_or_tool_output\" # new mode\n``` \n\n## Validation\n- just test -p codex-core load_config_resolves_current_time_reminder\n- just test -p codex-core\nlock_contains_prompts_and_materializes_features","tree":{"sha":"e14d563f73d0eb0cd8fcccffcdf7772207f16814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e14d563f73d0eb0cd8fcccffcdf7772207f16814"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e8d4a1a411bbab9be85e704ae3847915916bf347","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPXxDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAQkQAIFUDFfMxYL6NbFfs7XJAB2L\n72BTSiTYmfwAcFLEoeCw4QDkhb004F9wbS7OjcbYnX6nCQQXwLeugTdr8s4iiAt+\nZFY0r7iBi+qo0hyAFaGXzJQ5v8GIjQfKZgPuJcjHXkqgRd+kwdts1tksCP5IFwmT\nNb6YHqDNEvkld1NCmfrG3eOEu6he9EhesXh82y5ZjFzlzn6EcEv1M/+bH2Bc6mew\nxnjR79WIGE5/5waMBcgLXHhA6hB3U2iMEGRRsIwVbzks3Gyy5XyzXCjowh6FAUyL\nZCeajysPifF9OHViAe+pXlRQQr3+8gCDXyxW8dxlDHnDQPUek9s66ppIh3+ofP+j\nAFGBE1WQgoc7+r5lxlGfsLn0a1TluQBe4O7tJ7w7NURdpJf+gxwryHTkodfx70pR\n8DqnuNMBNjajdbU/6VMI17f+wvpQ3IjHbVurUDbXxsqNqgjeLyDRWElcB3+/vpco\niwtV5o9yMCf9sMjiih/OnGQhzIO0iHVki2baNqifHUsvWiLbQmzj1myLRj90v1dr\n7PlTSZgBB/a7YaiKnzv5LwPsVGL3sBDNXpS756zzB+hdjEGeZUWOPWrezRHdoVjp\nJ0gX4o+TAN6iHiO/lyA7oTtEiB6T0mU9mJ2SVrImnlRjChw+cOxhLJP/G3bENTBt\nE9cf69fik0iG5NSDIvIc\n=Jsgc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e14d563f73d0eb0cd8fcccffcdf7772207f16814\nparent c65cfeab1478c4c8356b42aca3d06c92b2730334\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782414403 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782414403 +0000\n\n[codex] add current time reminder delivery mode config (#30031)\n\n```python\ndelivery_mode = \"any_inference\" # default\ndelivery_mode = \"after_user_or_tool_output\" # new mode\n``` \n\n## Validation\n- just test -p codex-core load_config_resolves_current_time_reminder\n- just test -p codex-core\nlock_contains_prompts_and_materializes_features","verified_at":"2026-06-25T19:06:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e8d4a1a411bbab9be85e704ae3847915916bf347","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e8d4a1a411bbab9be85e704ae3847915916bf347","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e8d4a1a411bbab9be85e704ae3847915916bf347/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c65cfeab1478c4c8356b42aca3d06c92b2730334","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c65cfeab1478c4c8356b42aca3d06c92b2730334","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c65cfeab1478c4c8356b42aca3d06c92b2730334"}]},{"sha":"c65cfeab1478c4c8356b42aca3d06c92b2730334","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM2NWNmZWFiMTQ3OGM0YzgzNTZiNDJhY2EzZDA2YzkyYjI3MzAzMzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T19:00:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T19:00:23Z"},"message":"core: expose permission profile to shell tools (#29941)\n\n## tl;dr\n\nInject a `CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE` environment variable with the name\nof the current permission profile when invoking a shell tool.\n\n## Why\n\nShell tool owners may need to launch nested commands under the same\nnamed permission profile, including through `codex sandbox -P PROFILE\n--include-managed-config`. Until now, child processes could observe\nsandbox and network metadata but could not identify the active named\npermission profile.\n\nThe `--include-managed-config` flag is essential when a helper\nreconstructs the sandbox from a profile name: it ensures the nested\nsandbox also loads managed enterprise requirements. Without it, using\nthe inherited profile could unintentionally create a sandbox that does\nnot enforce the organization's managed restrictions.\n\nThe new environment value is intentionally informational and **must not\nbe treated as trusted input**. Any process in the ancestry can overwrite\nan environment variable, so a consumer that passes this value to `codex\nsandbox -P` must first validate it against the profiles that helper is\nauthorized to use.\n\n## Example Use Case\n\nSuppose an organization provides a trusted `remote-bash` wrapper that\nlets Codex run a command on an approved build host. The local shell\ncommand uses the named `:workspace` permission profile:\n\n```toml\ndefault_permissions = \":workspace\"\n```\n\nThe command exposed to the model is a small zsh wrapper. It deliberately\ndelegates with `exec`, preserving the original arguments and process\nenvironment:\n\n```zsh\n#!/usr/bin/env zsh\nexec /opt/codex-tools/remote_bash.py \"$@\"\n```\n\nThe model invokes the public wrapper, not its Python implementation:\n\n```sh\n/opt/codex-tools/remote-bash \\\n  --host builder.example.com \\\n  -- printf '%s' 'hello world'\n```\n\nOnly the inner implementation is authorized to escape the local sandbox:\n\n```starlark\nprefix_rule(\n    pattern=[\"/opt/codex-tools/remote_bash.py\"],\n    decision=\"allow\",\n)\n```\n\nWith zsh-fork, execution begins with `remote-bash` inside the\n`:workspace` sandbox. When the wrapper calls `exec`, the exact prefix\nrule matches `remote_bash.py`, so that inner script is restarted\nunsandboxed. The escalated process inherits:\n\n```text\nCODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE=:workspace\n```\n\nInheritance does not make the value trustworthy. `remote_bash.py`\nindependently allowlists both the remote host and the permission profile\nbefore using either value. In particular, a forged value such as\n`:danger-full-access` is rejected before it can reach `codex sandbox\n-P`:\n\n```python\nimport argparse\nimport os\nimport shlex\nimport sys\n\nALLOWED_HOSTS = {\"builder.example.com\"}\nALLOWED_PROFILES = {\":workspace\"}\n\nparser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\nparser.add_argument(\"--host\", required=True)\nseparator = sys.argv.index(\"--\")\nargs = parser.parse_args(sys.argv[1:separator])\ncommand = sys.argv[separator + 1:]\n\nif args.host not in ALLOWED_HOSTS:\n    parser.error(\"host is not allowlisted\")\nif not command:\n    parser.error(\"the remote command must not be empty\")\n\nprofile = os.environ.get(\"CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE\")\nif not profile:\n    raise SystemExit(\"CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE must not be empty\")\nif profile not in ALLOWED_PROFILES:\n    raise SystemExit(\"CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE is not allowlisted\")\n\nremote_command = shlex.join(command)\nsandbox_command = shlex.join([\n    \"codex\", \"sandbox\", \"-P\", profile,\n    \"--include-managed-config\", \"--\",\n    \"bash\", \"-lc\", remote_command,\n])\nprint(shlex.join([\"ssh\", args.host, sandbox_command]))\n```\n\nThis builds each command layer as an argument vector and uses\n`shlex.join()` at the boundary, rather than interpolating untrusted\nshell text. After validation and parsing, the nested command has this\nstructure:\n\n```text\nssh argv:\n  [\"ssh\", \"builder.example.com\", SANDBOX_COMMAND]\n\nSANDBOX_COMMAND argv:\n  [\"codex\", \"sandbox\", \"-P\", \":workspace\",\n   \"--include-managed-config\", \"--\",\n   \"bash\", \"-lc\", \"printf %s 'hello world'\"]\n\nbash -lc payload argv:\n  [\"printf\", \"%s\", \"hello world\"]\n```\n\nA production implementation could execute that SSH command. The\nintegration fixture prints it and parses the result back into arguments,\nverifying the complete flow:\n\n```text\nmodel invokes outer wrapper\n  -> zsh-fork starts wrapper under :workspace\n  -> wrapper execs allowlisted Python script\n  -> prefix rule restarts Python script unsandboxed\n  -> Python script inherits CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE=:workspace\n  -> Python script verifies :workspace is allowlisted\n  -> remote command runs codex sandbox -P :workspace\n     with --include-managed-config\n  -> nested sandbox honors managed enterprise requirements\n```\n\nThis gives the trusted helper access to resources outside the local\nsandbox—such as SSH credentials—while ensuring that it can select only\nan explicitly authorized profile and that work on the remote host\nremains subject to the organization's managed requirements.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Inject `CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE` after shell environment policy\nevaluation so the active profile wins over inherited or configured stale\nvalues.\n- Apply the variable to both `shell_command` and unified `exec_command`,\nincluding local, zsh-fork, and remote exec-server paths.\n- Remove stale values when the session has no active named profile.\n- Preserve the current profile value when loading a shell snapshot so a\nparent snapshot cannot restore an older profile.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added classic-shell integration coverage proving an exact prefix rule\ncan run a `require_escalated` script outside the `:workspace` sandbox\nwhile preserving `CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE=:workspace`.\n- Added zsh-fork integration coverage in which the model invokes an\nouter zsh wrapper, an inner allowlisted `remote_bash.py` runs\nunsandboxed, and its printed SSH command reconstructs the inherited\n`:workspace` sandbox with `--include-managed-config` while preserving\nevery argument after `--`.\n- The example helper treats `CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE` as untrusted and\nvalidates it against `ALLOWED_PROFILES` before constructing the nested\ncommand.\n- Assert that the reconstructed sandbox command includes\n`--include-managed-config` so nested use of the inherited profile cannot\nbypass managed enterprise requirements.\n- Added coverage for overriding and removing stale profile values.\n- Verified `shell_command` receives the selected active profile.\n- Added shell snapshot coverage using `printenv\nCODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE`.","tree":{"sha":"acc50dd8d98dd3b17d833d7f5ef8b2a1e1aea87b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/acc50dd8d98dd3b17d833d7f5ef8b2a1e1aea87b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c65cfeab1478c4c8356b42aca3d06c92b2730334","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPXrHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABW4QAFlVhdHpUe0C3ecsaewrwkW7\nevfNtRHQ8uAXX0Rq/bOCy5IYTgCgSYq+6HO8hma56QX+rFEYDtnVRU0imQdnNcB2\nthqfmoTPpbtnGOBPyaX9sbX+RUHoWPfjEHnkYjcO8J4+Tj3fZsMmBveaT1rP5Wqq\nBegahYq0PIsWq7G1cwvgj76m2nLb2xK6OM/uhRSTfgAIUzqdCFQ2p1bCSjUeGn1d\nCdN806BCUlCrf75mHjZ3phFEV5AQTK82tcg3PhMRJKmsK5Yo+tA6oohmEuISDYbP\nP9z4FMZHQaK/vodz37Ir8zctf6tovNFGOsF7hYnf6BUJYFx9s0kRN23HtC/UC3Ku\nez51gd82uOODiJRCCKp1NlG0qiFF38gRxrLuQfy7tLnQZV7zd4XmHhEjgqloNjkU\nKkRB+riCze2YMEReuDHBw7T0c9IIRK4wjjfLnk98+mA6izymokvzLBkCXztMoI5p\n5Im0qDwOkE+KkDXrj/NHTBkBTvT3ULrYPOgZ5o142pUFbf3lvL+eZ38pIryGt/Vx\nUdXX8pacVLmK85tXh1589xtwNJuUNghzS1uJa/IpqKHoJbBsceRRN5WD16nmJnIj\nNIQ2I4VceZHOB+hjp+l8awdczYgtrlziGpnYjj92eHOtEGmdUD0BEaVapM66Kk2o\nMvvHv/sqQ9GBV/hYPiJ3\n=g6Ua\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree acc50dd8d98dd3b17d833d7f5ef8b2a1e1aea87b\nparent cc78903379773233264ae9e3ccd3740439d70b51\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782414023 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782414023 +0000\n\ncore: expose permission profile to shell tools (#29941)\n\n## tl;dr\n\nInject a `CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE` environment variable with the name\nof the current permission profile when invoking a shell tool.\n\n## Why\n\nShell tool owners may need to launch nested commands under the same\nnamed permission profile, including through `codex sandbox -P PROFILE\n--include-managed-config`. Until now, child processes could observe\nsandbox and network metadata but could not identify the active named\npermission profile.\n\nThe `--include-managed-config` flag is essential when a helper\nreconstructs the sandbox from a profile name: it ensures the nested\nsandbox also loads managed enterprise requirements. Without it, using\nthe inherited profile could unintentionally create a sandbox that does\nnot enforce the organization's managed restrictions.\n\nThe new environment value is intentionally informational and **must not\nbe treated as trusted input**. Any process in the ancestry can overwrite\nan environment variable, so a consumer that passes this value to `codex\nsandbox -P` must first validate it against the profiles that helper is\nauthorized to use.\n\n## Example Use Case\n\nSuppose an organization provides a trusted `remote-bash` wrapper that\nlets Codex run a command on an approved build host. The local shell\ncommand uses the named `:workspace` permission profile:\n\n```toml\ndefault_permissions = \":workspace\"\n```\n\nThe command exposed to the model is a small zsh wrapper. It deliberately\ndelegates with `exec`, preserving the original arguments and process\nenvironment:\n\n```zsh\n#!/usr/bin/env zsh\nexec /opt/codex-tools/remote_bash.py \"$@\"\n```\n\nThe model invokes the public wrapper, not its Python implementation:\n\n```sh\n/opt/codex-tools/remote-bash \\\n  --host builder.example.com \\\n  -- printf '%s' 'hello world'\n```\n\nOnly the inner implementation is authorized to escape the local sandbox:\n\n```starlark\nprefix_rule(\n    pattern=[\"/opt/codex-tools/remote_bash.py\"],\n    decision=\"allow\",\n)\n```\n\nWith zsh-fork, execution begins with `remote-bash` inside the\n`:workspace` sandbox. When the wrapper calls `exec`, the exact prefix\nrule matches `remote_bash.py`, so that inner script is restarted\nunsandboxed. The escalated process inherits:\n\n```text\nCODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE=:workspace\n```\n\nInheritance does not make the value trustworthy. `remote_bash.py`\nindependently allowlists both the remote host and the permission profile\nbefore using either value. In particular, a forged value such as\n`:danger-full-access` is rejected before it can reach `codex sandbox\n-P`:\n\n```python\nimport argparse\nimport os\nimport shlex\nimport sys\n\nALLOWED_HOSTS = {\"builder.example.com\"}\nALLOWED_PROFILES = {\":workspace\"}\n\nparser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\nparser.add_argument(\"--host\", required=True)\nseparator = sys.argv.index(\"--\")\nargs = parser.parse_args(sys.argv[1:separator])\ncommand = sys.argv[separator + 1:]\n\nif args.host not in ALLOWED_HOSTS:\n    parser.error(\"host is not allowlisted\")\nif not command:\n    parser.error(\"the remote command must not be empty\")\n\nprofile = os.environ.get(\"CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE\")\nif not profile:\n    raise SystemExit(\"CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE must not be empty\")\nif profile not in ALLOWED_PROFILES:\n    raise SystemExit(\"CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE is not allowlisted\")\n\nremote_command = shlex.join(command)\nsandbox_command = shlex.join([\n    \"codex\", \"sandbox\", \"-P\", profile,\n    \"--include-managed-config\", \"--\",\n    \"bash\", \"-lc\", remote_command,\n])\nprint(shlex.join([\"ssh\", args.host, sandbox_command]))\n```\n\nThis builds each command layer as an argument vector and uses\n`shlex.join()` at the boundary, rather than interpolating untrusted\nshell text. After validation and parsing, the nested command has this\nstructure:\n\n```text\nssh argv:\n  [\"ssh\", \"builder.example.com\", SANDBOX_COMMAND]\n\nSANDBOX_COMMAND argv:\n  [\"codex\", \"sandbox\", \"-P\", \":workspace\",\n   \"--include-managed-config\", \"--\",\n   \"bash\", \"-lc\", \"printf %s 'hello world'\"]\n\nbash -lc payload argv:\n  [\"printf\", \"%s\", \"hello world\"]\n```\n\nA production implementation could execute that SSH command. The\nintegration fixture prints it and parses the result back into arguments,\nverifying the complete flow:\n\n```text\nmodel invokes outer wrapper\n  -> zsh-fork starts wrapper under :workspace\n  -> wrapper execs allowlisted Python script\n  -> prefix rule restarts Python script unsandboxed\n  -> Python script inherits CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE=:workspace\n  -> Python script verifies :workspace is allowlisted\n  -> remote command runs codex sandbox -P :workspace\n     with --include-managed-config\n  -> nested sandbox honors managed enterprise requirements\n```\n\nThis gives the trusted helper access to resources outside the local\nsandbox—such as SSH credentials—while ensuring that it can select only\nan explicitly authorized profile and that work on the remote host\nremains subject to the organization's managed requirements.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Inject `CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE` after shell environment policy\nevaluation so the active profile wins over inherited or configured stale\nvalues.\n- Apply the variable to both `shell_command` and unified `exec_command`,\nincluding local, zsh-fork, and remote exec-server paths.\n- Remove stale values when the session has no active named profile.\n- Preserve the current profile value when loading a shell snapshot so a\nparent snapshot cannot restore an older profile.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added classic-shell integration coverage proving an exact prefix rule\ncan run a `require_escalated` script outside the `:workspace` sandbox\nwhile preserving `CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE=:workspace`.\n- Added zsh-fork integration coverage in which the model invokes an\nouter zsh wrapper, an inner allowlisted `remote_bash.py` runs\nunsandboxed, and its printed SSH command reconstructs the inherited\n`:workspace` sandbox with `--include-managed-config` while preserving\nevery argument after `--`.\n- The example helper treats `CODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE` as untrusted and\nvalidates it against `ALLOWED_PROFILES` before constructing the nested\ncommand.\n- Assert that the reconstructed sandbox command includes\n`--include-managed-config` so nested use of the inherited profile cannot\nbypass managed enterprise requirements.\n- Added coverage for overriding and removing stale profile values.\n- Verified `shell_command` receives the selected active profile.\n- Added shell snapshot coverage using `printenv\nCODEX_PERMISSION_PROFILE`.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T19:00:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c65cfeab1478c4c8356b42aca3d06c92b2730334","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c65cfeab1478c4c8356b42aca3d06c92b2730334","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c65cfeab1478c4c8356b42aca3d06c92b2730334/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.