GIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPXPdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1REQAJVDj+5GaLHfg/xm0tG/wqiu\nG5b9WGetTJFZbITUEteu857dPHHkKFb81ZIPVSBTQ1nXvKZwg0Rrdgswa4UZXNEg\nj1qYsOL7F/UwA77K25vEg/w+9PSX3hz5jGyAd+d4CDr0ic5q8SeA8mwYrf5QuXbt\nvTU+B/LzR9muqZpr/82wRsXZAgPa6VCJmUpbWech416y3NwoI1f7FnriE+EgNfCA\nMNXF8/QSjeFGAQ2P4EpxhMYD4PQwohJ803dYPxBsYcnPNCcVt8XukOGPrjS5TXqI\nIPUm28ugnqeO3u4nBmXsSq38gpCcpH5aC1ZDMRn5kVuI26v5yooAXR5FmNppDI0o\nygduZKiKpCFzs8ncpTX/Nh5CAOfkfGFB0rgF83OHJAyhKp1WzFgVduDJTy1vzYgu\nlSw7eMJGVGlD+y5L9KJVTGG4VGVehROX4C3iJVDB7a7YwgItF3qzqkYNjLSFiQRo\nQd+MwkD87eR4TJri/M4O5dxBzmKcrhRQEMbBnpqB1R/iSLA9YwYBT/Zv3Jt3djPa\nLaHFMz4/tu2Y7pF1zBDxkkzZqDPdbC54dhdELJ7vwURowvm9OLHYJAybHVIIsp9+\nKdLesnJx6sude0b/GA5sFCdnYZhiWk6yL5sF1eU4tFMJAksYGgqPwPlwNzlI6YWh\n6MCWaKCvGAyzE8OYEEmx\n=1tAg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 622eac16992a0b6c01342ec4d5e4ba07d90271ed\nparent 31b99f65cf4b3eaf9180f625b48b5614806cd121\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782412253 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782412253 +0000\n\n[codex] current time reminder interval to be set to 0 (#30029)\n\nA zero interval lets callers request a reminder at every\notherwise-eligible inference boundary.\n\n## Validation\n- just test -p codex-core load_config_resolves_current_time_reminder","verified_at":"2026-06-25T18:30:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cc78903379773233264ae9e3ccd3740439d70b51","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cc78903379773233264ae9e3ccd3740439d70b51","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cc78903379773233264ae9e3ccd3740439d70b51/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"31b99f65cf4b3eaf9180f625b48b5614806cd121","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/31b99f65cf4b3eaf9180f625b48b5614806cd121","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/31b99f65cf4b3eaf9180f625b48b5614806cd121"}]},{"sha":"31b99f65cf4b3eaf9180f625b48b5614806cd121","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMxYjk5ZjY1Y2Y0YjNlYWY5MTgwZjYyNWI0OGI1NjE0ODA2Y2QxMjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T18:25:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T18:25:19Z"},"message":"cli: rename sandbox permission profile flag (#30095)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex sandbox` accepts a single named permissions profile, so the\nexisting plural `--permissions-profile` spelling is misleading. The\ncanonical flag and its help text should use the singular form without\nbreaking scripts that already use the old spelling.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `--permission-profile` the canonical flag for all sandbox\nbackends.\n- Keep `--permissions-profile` as a hidden backwards-compatible alias.\n- Cover the canonical spelling, legacy alias, and help visibility with\nregression tests.\n\n## Testing\n\nRan `just c sandbox --help` and verified I saw:\n\n```shell\n  -P, --permission-profile <NAME>\n          Named permissions profile to apply from the active configuration stack\n```","tree":{"sha":"fa60e6b5af2927f85f2785b1f262b311231f592c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fa60e6b5af2927f85f2785b1f262b311231f592c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/31b99f65cf4b3eaf9180f625b48b5614806cd121","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPXKPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+kMQAGZsGzf+gwx2Xp3yBYbdk4NA\nJj2HIgS+LeUcLkRcJB5Vilk2QWd8rmW1mvr1cV61H7NKVHswo8r9Uaw8ipptaf8d\nXDrkuC+GU8otY9qQtHVCAxCzUnfzQLYuMrOMUFXsLcPhd/LozrViZhxKAnNdL6Dc\nGorYpIz2GrwbOx5qIvH4WoUr1lSlOzEuQm7ucug34JANqhGm2i71kxeKT1j5LAvA\nRG3fQ29cNjrM4Q80bCQE0x4ccVUGe6jGqLfDO7mqgYpLh+XAvLYu1t7YnjI9Jze+\nl3e2W4259iToYa2hhVi32LXJvT8ziJZeuQ8MAncXB6Mk4t54etKQQBIIicfDFAXz\ns77dx7zkVd35EZGWjhXsWdGErF3JAVTzCgGrjabg4KYi5Fq/qDA82dUQ9W7jNeCi\nJfvihY/YgY/QIcoNHiMg++8eaDqZaeUPyvyDbsN41CbjyjQ7mEASzD9NhRwKNxpQ\nxuagWijsGY6xT+YKLtZmdvdO51xmirdI6keXKURImGABgLzp5U6kPsFlmKu51P+7\nMm7NVyXOO9xsZK3kadhI1czLhy4e7eUF0YurNTBr+JLhNc2k1O5ALRfnJ4ax4SG1\nEhUDjgika84aNOkGhThS6lhbs4rIgwGVeqBzMZuU7YYIwZJVsoJZCv8y/m3FGj9x\nhV41eng/uplDpHmM1ziM\n=p7xG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fa60e6b5af2927f85f2785b1f262b311231f592c\nparent 6d9dbacf1af69fc9b633132e34d63be202556a24\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782411919 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782411919 -0700\n\ncli: rename sandbox permission profile flag (#30095)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex sandbox` accepts a single named permissions profile, so the\nexisting plural `--permissions-profile` spelling is misleading. The\ncanonical flag and its help text should use the singular form without\nbreaking scripts that already use the old spelling.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `--permission-profile` the canonical flag for all sandbox\nbackends.\n- Keep `--permissions-profile` as a hidden backwards-compatible alias.\n- Cover the canonical spelling, legacy alias, and help visibility with\nregression tests.\n\n## Testing\n\nRan `just c sandbox --help` and verified I saw:\n\n```shell\n  -P, --permission-profile <NAME>\n          Named permissions profile to apply from the active configuration stack\n```","verified_at":"2026-06-25T18:25:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/31b99f65cf4b3eaf9180f625b48b5614806cd121","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/31b99f65cf4b3eaf9180f625b48b5614806cd121","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/31b99f65cf4b3eaf9180f625b48b5614806cd121/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6d9dbacf1af69fc9b633132e34d63be202556a24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d9dbacf1af69fc9b633132e34d63be202556a24","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d9dbacf1af69fc9b633132e34d63be202556a24"}]},{"sha":"6d9dbacf1af69fc9b633132e34d63be202556a24","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkOWRiYWNmMWFmNjlmYzliNjMzMTMyZTM0ZDYzYmUyMDI1NTZhMjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T18:24:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T18:24:34Z"},"message":"feat: add provider-aware model fallback to thread start (#29942)\n\n## Why\n\nHelper threads such as task title generation can request a model ID that\nis valid for the default OpenAI provider but unavailable from the active\nprovider. With Amazon Bedrock, `gpt-5.4-mini` is rejected while the\nprovider static catalog exposes Bedrock model IDs such as\n`openai.gpt-5.5` and `openai.gpt-5.4`. This causes repeated background\n404s and can surface a misleading turn error even when the main turn\nsucceeds.\n\nClients need an explicit way to ask app-server to resolve an unavailable\nhelper model to the active provider default. That fallback must remain\nlimited to providers with an authoritative static catalog so custom or\ndynamically discovered model IDs are not rewritten based on an\nincomplete catalog.\n\nFixes #28741.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the experimental `allowProviderModelFallback` option to\n`thread/start`, defaulting to `false` to preserve existing behavior.\n- Thread the option through thread creation and model selection.\n- When enabled for a static model manager, preserve requested models\npresent in the catalog and replace unavailable models with the provider\ndefault.\n- Continue preserving explicit model IDs for dynamic model managers\nwithout fetching a catalog solely to validate them.\n- Document the new `thread/start` behavior in the app-server API\noverview.\n\n## Test\nTemporary test-client harness:\n```\nThreadStartParams {\n    model: Some(\"gpt-5.4-mini\".to_string()),\n    allow_provider_model_fallback: true,\n    ..Default::default()\n}\n```\nCommand:\n```\nCODEX_HOME=/tmp/codex-bedrock-thread-start-home \\\nCODEX_E2E_BEDROCK_THREAD_START_ONLY=1 \\\n./target/debug/codex-app-server-test-client \\\n  --codex-bin ./target/debug/codex \\\n  -c 'model_provider=\"amazon-bedrock\"' \\\n  send-message-v2 --experimental-api ignored\n```\nRelevant output:\n```\n> \"method\": \"thread/start\",\n> \"params\": {\n>   \"model\": \"gpt-5.4-mini\",\n>   \"modelProvider\": null,\n>   \"allowProviderModelFallback\": true,\n>   ...\n> }\n\n< \"result\": {\n<   \"model\": \"openai.gpt-5.5\",\n<   \"modelProvider\": \"amazon-bedrock\",\n<   ...\n< }\n```","tree":{"sha":"8e1178e4b818043ea5cc4eff373b141cae5cdd72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8e1178e4b818043ea5cc4eff373b141cae5cdd72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6d9dbacf1af69fc9b633132e34d63be202556a24","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPXJiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0pwQADjZKT6C5WfCq4XfxbSVaK2J\nSbD7uEtHtK4YHHCRW6HAa+ZZDjMAtmdNFH57z8waZ+pKA+flbREdFPKtQ8m9QfPU\nuWvXHF2AV+LUyZOmpzo0Kr0/H677Do0PsNFBapnwazjOb707huXxwQZMxdg7vw83\nj2p9aqYhHELVKZ6YEGEiHUoBAGXwM8INbFO4GQrYT4ZLatm9/qex2xHxDMSdToMa\ngT4zmWMuvwIaxwxlBPwaG/EH5mdOC6VZGGQCseWwMHyhWwvBoeU2OiVDOAZWDN5l\nFBHlxhHteUY8NN5dalZI/8lO35VzzErxs0m7CPfA671zsrLYnaZPphKs/ftj2V3H\n7SAKs9zpC2K8SoABafaUrxr/zzfo6c7Qd6UPJgENH+YndLvZ/37dKdRFTbMmQieB\nTY1o+YYpLuNsI3WS3ltwRGyb7KDxjdaqyOhzNhUn/ojBBCta60u1rPQFbmVfchD5\n1uWDvQfXmifG7HCEwFco1NAfV5xX9eBAa+nPt//uiBXa4hg21cLMMDrUF7Fb+3o9\nWKfAf/nlLJusN8vNJN4WnDvZVXEWGDvjR+5uvL0roZn/PHdhwd2noG/EiPKGTKQl\nMPRdcbTytgFk9z4nhsncZRSNiM/LNxceoa+fq/YE4wch37CaGTaOa0WGXOe7Tm7R\nGYsR0xdj2VRflz8b0CHX\n=4YSz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8e1178e4b818043ea5cc4eff373b141cae5cdd72\nparent 2dec46e30ae81aa4844cc7a5474ff5c95c6998c0\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1782411874 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782411874 +0000\n\nfeat: add provider-aware model fallback to thread start (#29942)\n\n## Why\n\nHelper threads such as task title generation can request a model ID that\nis valid for the default OpenAI provider but unavailable from the active\nprovider. With Amazon Bedrock, `gpt-5.4-mini` is rejected while the\nprovider static catalog exposes Bedrock model IDs such as\n`openai.gpt-5.5` and `openai.gpt-5.4`. This causes repeated background\n404s and can surface a misleading turn error even when the main turn\nsucceeds.\n\nClients need an explicit way to ask app-server to resolve an unavailable\nhelper model to the active provider default. That fallback must remain\nlimited to providers with an authoritative static catalog so custom or\ndynamically discovered model IDs are not rewritten based on an\nincomplete catalog.\n\nFixes #28741.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the experimental `allowProviderModelFallback` option to\n`thread/start`, defaulting to `false` to preserve existing behavior.\n- Thread the option through thread creation and model selection.\n- When enabled for a static model manager, preserve requested models\npresent in the catalog and replace unavailable models with the provider\ndefault.\n- Continue preserving explicit model IDs for dynamic model managers\nwithout fetching a catalog solely to validate them.\n- Document the new `thread/start` behavior in the app-server API\noverview.\n\n## Test\nTemporary test-client harness:\n```\nThreadStartParams {\n    model: Some(\"gpt-5.4-mini\".to_string()),\n    allow_provider_model_fallback: true,\n    ..Default::default()\n}\n```\nCommand:\n```\nCODEX_HOME=/tmp/codex-bedrock-thread-start-home \\\nCODEX_E2E_BEDROCK_THREAD_START_ONLY=1 \\\n./target/debug/codex-app-server-test-client \\\n  --codex-bin ./target/debug/codex \\\n  -c 'model_provider=\"amazon-bedrock\"' \\\n  send-message-v2 --experimental-api ignored\n```\nRelevant output:\n```\n> \"method\": \"thread/start\",\n> \"params\": {\n>   \"model\": \"gpt-5.4-mini\",\n>   \"modelProvider\": null,\n>   \"allowProviderModelFallback\": true,\n>   ...\n> }\n\n< \"result\": {\n<   \"model\": \"openai.gpt-5.5\",\n<   \"modelProvider\": \"amazon-bedrock\",\n<   ...\n< }\n```","verified_at":"2026-06-25T18:24:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d9dbacf1af69fc9b633132e34d63be202556a24","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d9dbacf1af69fc9b633132e34d63be202556a24","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d9dbacf1af69fc9b633132e34d63be202556a24/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2dec46e30ae81aa4844cc7a5474ff5c95c6998c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2dec46e30ae81aa4844cc7a5474ff5c95c6998c0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2dec46e30ae81aa4844cc7a5474ff5c95c6998c0"}]},{"sha":"2dec46e30ae81aa4844cc7a5474ff5c95c6998c0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJkZWM0NmUzMGFlODFhYTQ4NDRjYzdhNTQ3NGZmNWM5NWM2OTk4YzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"richardopenai","email":"richardlee@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T18:02:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T18:02:11Z"},"message":"[codex] Record exec-server lifecycle metrics (#27467)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Record bounded connection, request, and process lifecycle metrics.\n- Report active gauges from callbacks on every collection, including\ndelta exports.\n- Serialize active-count updates so concurrent starts and finishes\ncannot publish stale values.\n- Serialize process exit, explicit termination, and shutdown through the\nprocess registry so exactly one completion result wins.\n- Keep the implementation small with single-owner RAII guards and one\nreal OTLP/HTTP integration test using the existing `wiremock`\ndependency.\n\n## Root cause\n\nProcess exit and session shutdown previously used cloned completion\nstate. That avoided duplicate emission, but it duplicated lifecycle\nownership and made the ordering harder to reason about. The process\nregistry mutex already defines the lifecycle ordering, so the final\nimplementation stores the metric guard and termination flag directly on\nthe process entry. Whichever path claims the entry first owns the\ncompletion result.\n\nProduction metric export uses delta temporality. Event-only synchronous\ngauge recordings disappear after the next collection when no count\nchanges, so active counts now use observable callbacks that report\ncurrent state on every collection.\n\nThe cleanup also removes the constant `result=\"accepted\"` connection\ntag, redundant route and response assertions, a custom HTTP collector,\nand fallback initialization machinery that did not add behavior.\n\n## Stack\n\nReview and land this stack in order:\n\n1. #27466 — trace exec-server JSON-RPC requests\n2. #27467 — record bounded connection, request, and process lifecycle\nmetrics **(this PR)**\n3. #27470 — observe remote registration and Noise rendezvous lifecycle\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server --lib` (158 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-cli --test exec_server` (3 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-otel\nobservable_gauge_is_collected_on_every_delta_snapshot` (1 passed)\n- `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1 just fix -p codex-otel -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"bced378e48bdac82eb7f85d5f709624ed9180084","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bced378e48bdac82eb7f85d5f709624ed9180084"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2dec46e30ae81aa4844cc7a5474ff5c95c6998c0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPW0jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0YQQAJI2dHAu5rCS4wPO0UZzSeuo\n+4ClvNvERwSEViDwY1ye0icgrmz+u0pivv4njKFpr/+MlM7tvOY3Bi9vpt1e9rjB\n2Zp/VEqfSs2hquGZsPtHrSMTsfsI/rQ2BUtfayNxdKx04VKMUzkLHIrccyL5tF1f\nrJKZCbR4E1N86IE/PA/YN6mZC2jawIz5ApKo+P5jSIQKrLKqkv7xW03+VIO09Rs2\nNzeSgQkSn9M9uS7dONP6au6Pxkhg3uLjBD1EMHttn39mZGx3QmoCeMQTsP30SAxy\neahbdtsnKm9OXaSUjavrIip6zNNET2cy9OsJhBVaviGN8zumakT9XWMV3dVUE1JD\nFLnyT1UAA8lBtrTHj1KaVNODBDKY6ACeB4MLjXiPqx69gqfgxILj2xNqMATKiBXz\nHuqBoFyB167Ih06oDxvhvAmiSvmXw0mXPQngMo+Qd2fFr3hQ8CFohICmJdsR3obv\nWfJaKegqMVUBpFcZpcvnWErE1O5YXtU8ZuVYz58jqZ/4Kg1hRAvcG4t0+zdDhopJ\nX9+5vlxnmWifFbGXQtGub8WgDw83BUjz1Xd/Ydh4PmZjN+XSgmLkF8uu627CWOdn\n2FY5Zfz96+fyZILtjOOWHIKR1rtA3JqQo7Su8/1fGA22zrodkY2jmCD5gR1g4jED\n/3MukxzNCF8VjBhEumYz\n=Waff\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bced378e48bdac82eb7f85d5f709624ed9180084\nparent 8f02973d2541fb98d9a626f07d8f3661cb2a9e71\nauthor richardopenai <richardlee@openai.com> 1782410531 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782410531 -0700\n\n[codex] Record exec-server lifecycle metrics (#27467)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Record bounded connection, request, and process lifecycle metrics.\n- Report active gauges from callbacks on every collection, including\ndelta exports.\n- Serialize active-count updates so concurrent starts and finishes\ncannot publish stale values.\n- Serialize process exit, explicit termination, and shutdown through the\nprocess registry so exactly one completion result wins.\n- Keep the implementation small with single-owner RAII guards and one\nreal OTLP/HTTP integration test using the existing `wiremock`\ndependency.\n\n## Root cause\n\nProcess exit and session shutdown previously used cloned completion\nstate. That avoided duplicate emission, but it duplicated lifecycle\nownership and made the ordering harder to reason about. The process\nregistry mutex already defines the lifecycle ordering, so the final\nimplementation stores the metric guard and termination flag directly on\nthe process entry. Whichever path claims the entry first owns the\ncompletion result.\n\nProduction metric export uses delta temporality. Event-only synchronous\ngauge recordings disappear after the next collection when no count\nchanges, so active counts now use observable callbacks that report\ncurrent state on every collection.\n\nThe cleanup also removes the constant `result=\"accepted\"` connection\ntag, redundant route and response assertions, a custom HTTP collector,\nand fallback initialization machinery that did not add behavior.\n\n## Stack\n\nReview and land this stack in order:\n\n1. #27466 — trace exec-server JSON-RPC requests\n2. #27467 — record bounded connection, request, and process lifecycle\nmetrics **(this PR)**\n3. #27470 — observe remote registration and Noise rendezvous lifecycle\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server --lib` (158 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-cli --test exec_server` (3 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-otel\nobservable_gauge_is_collected_on_every_delta_snapshot` (1 passed)\n- `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1 just fix -p codex-otel -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T18:02:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2dec46e30ae81aa4844cc7a5474ff5c95c6998c0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2dec46e30ae81aa4844cc7a5474ff5c95c6998c0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2dec46e30ae81aa4844cc7a5474ff5c95c6998c0/comments","author":{"login":"richardopenai","id":272641442,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAtog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272641442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai","html_url":"https://github.com/richardopenai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8f02973d2541fb98d9a626f07d8f3661cb2a9e71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f02973d2541fb98d9a626f07d8f3661cb2a9e71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f02973d2541fb98d9a626f07d8f3661cb2a9e71"}]},{"sha":"8f02973d2541fb98d9a626f07d8f3661cb2a9e71","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhmMDI5NzNkMjU0MWZiOThkOWE2MjZmMDdkOGYzNjYxY2IyYTllNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T17:49:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T17:49:43Z"},"message":"Persist selected capability roots and resolve availability per model step (#29856)\n\n## Why\n\n`selectedCapabilityRoots` is durable thread intent: “use this capability\nroot from environment `worker`.”\n\nThe important product assumption is:\n\n> One environment ID always names the same logical executor and stable\ncontents.\n\n`worker` does not silently change from executor A to an unrelated\nexecutor B. The process-local connection handle for `worker` can still\nbe replaced while Codex is running, though, for example when\n`environment/add` registers a fresh handle for the same logical\nenvironment.\n\nThe thread should persist only the stable selection. Each model step\nshould pair that selection with the exact ready handle captured for that\nstep.\n\n## The boundary\n\n```text\npersisted thread intent\n  plugin@1 -> environment \"worker\"\n                |\n                | capture the current step\n                v\nmodel-step view\n  unavailable, or\n  plugin@1 + worker's exact captured ready handle\n```\n\nThe environment ID is the stable identity and cache key. The\n`Arc<Environment>` is only a process-local handle retained so consumers\nof one model step use the same captured environment. It is never\npersisted and it does not imply different environment contents.\n\n## What changes\n\n### Persist the stable selection\n\nSelected roots are written into `SessionMeta` and restored with the\nthread. Forked subagents inherit the same selections, including\nbounded-history forks.\n\nOnly stable data is persisted: root ID, environment ID, and root path.\n\n### Capture readiness together with the exact handle\n\nThe environment snapshot records:\n\n```rust\nenvironment_id -> Some(Arc<Environment>) // ready in this step\nenvironment_id -> None                   // still starting in this step\n```\n\nThis prevents readiness and execution from coming from different\nregistry snapshots.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nstep snapshot: worker -> handle A, ready\nenvironment/add: worker -> fresh handle B for the same logical environment\ncurrent step: plugin@1 still uses captured handle A\n```\n\nWithout carrying handle A in the snapshot, the resolver could combine “A\nwas ready” with handle B and treat B as ready before it had finished\nstarting.\n\nThis does not change cache invalidation. Stable capability metadata\nremains identified by environment ID and capability root. Replacing a\nprocess-local handle under the same stable environment ID does not\ninvalidate or rediscover that metadata.\n\n### Resolve availability per model step\n\n- A ready captured environment produces resolved roots using its\ncaptured handle.\n- A starting, missing, or failed environment is omitted from that step.\n- A selected lazy environment that is outside the turn's captured\nenvironment set is asked to start, and a later step can observe it as\nready.\n- No capability files are scanned here.\n\nTransient transport disconnects remain the remote client's reconnect\nconcern. This PR models initial attachment/readiness; it does not add\nlive socket-connectivity state.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nthread selection: plugin@1 -> environment \"worker\"\n\nstep 1: worker is starting -> plugin@1 unavailable\nstep 2: worker is ready    -> plugin@1 resolves through worker's captured handle\nstep 3: fresh local handle -> current step remains pinned; a later step captures its own view\n```\n\nTemporary unavailability does not discard the durable selection. Later\nPRs can retain stable metadata caches while projecting only currently\navailable capabilities into model-visible World State.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nThe app-server request shape does not change. Older rollouts without\n`selected_capability_roots` deserialize to an empty list.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **This PR:** persist stable selected roots and resolve them through\nan exact model-step handle.\n2. #29960: cache stable skill metadata and project available skills into\nWorld State.\n3. #29946: cache stable plugin declarations and manage the separate live\nMCP runtime.","tree":{"sha":"3221991447fbac0ba96c22413763cc357a9c7e84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3221991447fbac0ba96c22413763cc357a9c7e84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8f02973d2541fb98d9a626f07d8f3661cb2a9e71","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPWo3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6gUQABC1FFl7uSaG2dmssO146Z/1\n98g5HI2Z+AbEM6386RgO7pVbCcE307To0Cipf2SOi/VeUUEfYivHShvqDKK6PzwE\nguAGQf9YxSi3ITirksBqwP0WVwEETPiXItP7Z4hYW3rhksmgf9npnXsyxp+qxCjk\nts73gm3Qhd5lfm8UIXQYUqitEjUWj6HPDq40QEQdVJ1fbkrLvKA9kred5EpNtixz\nxRcFaAyfkfaNPf3Y70V2+Pze9YggZVEDKM/uq5Tm0oYf+Zc1PXn3LzXb9LXGE82T\ng0Kvgh3IpFO6RxfqQBd/bbdfsY24gWE8sPu8HQDYvrLFtsAUornc1xyo5BRCom5y\nTRGhRluUG9InjRFSnxW9snESImn7SlVAseoOkZQshU1SgbxrETII05t+TvwoV8K8\nvway+JQtKtGs3BwW3bgBVKJjLPHFzCIueeH0A8s1rbRD9+dqu2FLPwGJB5oBKEiJ\nhTPDSYuKnx7MiqM6aTBsnlftZdHgzxC6SKrybvzKCwOioNjeWrF1KSHNPvxfeI+v\nJxTOqy/wSFjrDFOgv2DwvoSx+6ANshyN7Jh/n73ax11rrzC9Wkk3YR6WYb8XD9BS\nG14kZ1Q+WsHDWYwvcNoL48iqNz19SQvIr9+Gr7B1PgB8SUZcCpSM3nG+9c5ftezS\nmw6HZJgP7nZQwheG9yET\n=+nMN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3221991447fbac0ba96c22413763cc357a9c7e84\nparent 268328001f899ec02cebab238fdeafda052525b6\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782409783 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782409783 +0000\n\nPersist selected capability roots and resolve availability per model step (#29856)\n\n## Why\n\n`selectedCapabilityRoots` is durable thread intent: “use this capability\nroot from environment `worker`.”\n\nThe important product assumption is:\n\n> One environment ID always names the same logical executor and stable\ncontents.\n\n`worker` does not silently change from executor A to an unrelated\nexecutor B. The process-local connection handle for `worker` can still\nbe replaced while Codex is running, though, for example when\n`environment/add` registers a fresh handle for the same logical\nenvironment.\n\nThe thread should persist only the stable selection. Each model step\nshould pair that selection with the exact ready handle captured for that\nstep.\n\n## The boundary\n\n```text\npersisted thread intent\n  plugin@1 -> environment \"worker\"\n                |\n                | capture the current step\n                v\nmodel-step view\n  unavailable, or\n  plugin@1 + worker's exact captured ready handle\n```\n\nThe environment ID is the stable identity and cache key. The\n`Arc<Environment>` is only a process-local handle retained so consumers\nof one model step use the same captured environment. It is never\npersisted and it does not imply different environment contents.\n\n## What changes\n\n### Persist the stable selection\n\nSelected roots are written into `SessionMeta` and restored with the\nthread. Forked subagents inherit the same selections, including\nbounded-history forks.\n\nOnly stable data is persisted: root ID, environment ID, and root path.\n\n### Capture readiness together with the exact handle\n\nThe environment snapshot records:\n\n```rust\nenvironment_id -> Some(Arc<Environment>) // ready in this step\nenvironment_id -> None                   // still starting in this step\n```\n\nThis prevents readiness and execution from coming from different\nregistry snapshots.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nstep snapshot: worker -> handle A, ready\nenvironment/add: worker -> fresh handle B for the same logical environment\ncurrent step: plugin@1 still uses captured handle A\n```\n\nWithout carrying handle A in the snapshot, the resolver could combine “A\nwas ready” with handle B and treat B as ready before it had finished\nstarting.\n\nThis does not change cache invalidation. Stable capability metadata\nremains identified by environment ID and capability root. Replacing a\nprocess-local handle under the same stable environment ID does not\ninvalidate or rediscover that metadata.\n\n### Resolve availability per model step\n\n- A ready captured environment produces resolved roots using its\ncaptured handle.\n- A starting, missing, or failed environment is omitted from that step.\n- A selected lazy environment that is outside the turn's captured\nenvironment set is asked to start, and a later step can observe it as\nready.\n- No capability files are scanned here.\n\nTransient transport disconnects remain the remote client's reconnect\nconcern. This PR models initial attachment/readiness; it does not add\nlive socket-connectivity state.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nthread selection: plugin@1 -> environment \"worker\"\n\nstep 1: worker is starting -> plugin@1 unavailable\nstep 2: worker is ready    -> plugin@1 resolves through worker's captured handle\nstep 3: fresh local handle -> current step remains pinned; a later step captures its own view\n```\n\nTemporary unavailability does not discard the durable selection. Later\nPRs can retain stable metadata caches while projecting only currently\navailable capabilities into model-visible World State.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nThe app-server request shape does not change. Older rollouts without\n`selected_capability_roots` deserialize to an empty list.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **This PR:** persist stable selected roots and resolve them through\nan exact model-step handle.\n2. #29960: cache stable skill metadata and project available skills into\nWorld State.\n3. #29946: cache stable plugin declarations and manage the separate live\nMCP runtime.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T17:49:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f02973d2541fb98d9a626f07d8f3661cb2a9e71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f02973d2541fb98d9a626f07d8f3661cb2a9e71","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f02973d2541fb98d9a626f07d8f3661cb2a9e71/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"268328001f899ec02cebab238fdeafda052525b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/268328001f899ec02cebab238fdeafda052525b6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/268328001f899ec02cebab238fdeafda052525b6"}]},{"sha":"268328001f899ec02cebab238fdeafda052525b6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI2ODMyODAwMWY4OTllYzAyY2ViYWIyMzhmZGVhZmRhMDUyNTI1YjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-25T17:15:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T17:15:46Z"},"message":"chore(app-server): mark thread/rollback as deprecated (#29928)\n\nWe will drop support for this in the near future due to the complexity\nit introduces.","tree":{"sha":"6a4ddea1b440daae1f2eefe7fae8b21fd5ed904e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6a4ddea1b440daae1f2eefe7fae8b21fd5ed904e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/268328001f899ec02cebab238fdeafda052525b6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPWJCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPz0QAErjOf7rzNE/OAHnA7UVS+LB\ntUY+wHL430Wdc1nds4fSYSb5OYiMsWJONqPzKHBwzOqSVsS1ZXKNwjkEbDIEL0nE\nQq4B9MvUALMjDn0QECWoUjmMMxtZt+J3BnoBxyBzQB8x5L4XDOfxPoub7aUmyu3B\n