s://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c38b2e9ba69cb57d197c6e5ba78b5e52ae0870f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c38b2e9ba69cb57d197c6e5ba78b5e52ae0870f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c38b2e9ba69cb57d197c6e5ba78b5e52ae0870f9"}]},{"sha":"c38b2e9ba69cb57d197c6e5ba78b5e52ae0870f9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMzOGIyZTliYTY5Y2I1N2QxOTdjNmU1YmE3OGI1ZTUyYWUwODcwZjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T09:45:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T09:45:20Z"},"message":"Test executor-routed MCP OAuth token exchange (#29656)\n\n## Why\n\n#28529 proves OAuth discovery uses the selected executor, but its\nend-to-end test stops before the callback and token exchange.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add an executor-only mock token endpoint\n- complete the OAuth callback using the authorization URL's `state` and\n`redirect_uri`\n- assert the PKCE token exchange reaches the executor-only endpoint\n- assert the completion notification reports the selected thread and\nsucceeds\n\nDepends on #28529.","tree":{"sha":"90e0914efc64cca9307df684f581a63a280701b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/90e0914efc64cca9307df684f581a63a280701b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c38b2e9ba69cb57d197c6e5ba78b5e52ae0870f9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPPiwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKvsQAHy1vQ0twe/f0UJmid4Uc0lR\nvsk9uz8d+oBhGbFN0jJrkcEfW2pFmONZlfGeFcpH9kARQHwvjG/QB+IQdN1nCjy6\njV+C7R+O0ns6CR5idGsvxa1dNSUcKoF9H7iaOHkWMSdmC+bn9CSXgV+/+ySyR8yy\nzoaGphpRtVbp7QnGpERm27x4k0dAqDB2hyNk+/3pdC/mlEen/AqjJ1fFRNEWUh7K\nYjULhdupB0YddrH7u6RYi/5cX4W/XsyqcBd/GZC0imn1XXGR/C70Cg2HXyALknMo\nlqI/rUONObLPDEokV0gusTwwAqZO1FFeYNrcSD9990Hi+dgV2thAyV+md5S5dVq5\n6ACthCTCy679MNhPqK9EZPlkQbfSXvDjJ0fM9PWLwyxL2WfwrNFuuzl3UC33yMjU\n0RFpgwulFUpjRJOa94o8Td0dPAVX6nwO5rULmohUuDH4YBb8Irftltg3N6p+Y9S8\ntH83P7njRQDJnaPzgfwXfbrU3hK0KwDe4L5rtvhAn1Ne8kvap1pYVATOliJtHvvH\n6+3Eo0NMjVNvvOrC9GLLdoSysU8genaV/s2MMCfhNHzSPRL+xHZ6Rd2ZDwcSMmsR\nPpewP1sg9LS1KVIb79FdZm/QSTd83EIyBMCxs1C6lecb2yzuhK1uWLJyXz3P/Xk7\nAJ+oGBbw65Bt918Ow0WH\n=anL9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 90e0914efc64cca9307df684f581a63a280701b0\nparent b215961a56b2553a4612a22a812747403c08a58b\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782380720 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782380720 +0000\n\nTest executor-routed MCP OAuth token exchange (#29656)\n\n## Why\n\n#28529 proves OAuth discovery uses the selected executor, but its\nend-to-end test stops before the callback and token exchange.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add an executor-only mock token endpoint\n- complete the OAuth callback using the authorization URL's `state` and\n`redirect_uri`\n- assert the PKCE token exchange reaches the executor-only endpoint\n- assert the completion notification reports the selected thread and\nsucceeds\n\nDepends on #28529.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T09:45:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c38b2e9ba69cb57d197c6e5ba78b5e52ae0870f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c38b2e9ba69cb57d197c6e5ba78b5e52ae0870f9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c38b2e9ba69cb57d197c6e5ba78b5e52ae0870f9/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b215961a56b2553a4612a22a812747403c08a58b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b215961a56b2553a4612a22a812747403c08a58b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b215961a56b2553a4612a22a812747403c08a58b"}]},{"sha":"b215961a56b2553a4612a22a812747403c08a58b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIyMTU5NjFhNTZiMjU1M2E0NjEyYTIyYTgxMjc0NzQwM2MwOGE1OGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T09:31:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T09:31:17Z"},"message":"Support OAuth for HTTP MCP servers from selected executor plugins (#28529)\n\n## Why\n\n#28522 routes selected-plugin HTTP MCP traffic through the owning\nexecutor, but OAuth bootstrap and refresh still used host-local clients.\nExecutor-only servers therefore cannot complete discovery or login\nthrough the same network boundary as the MCP connection.\n\n## What changed\n\n- adapt `codex_exec_server::HttpClient` to RMCP 1.8's `OAuthHttpClient`\ncontract\n- let RMCP own discovery, dynamic registration, PKCE, token exchange,\nand refresh\n- route auth status, persisted-token startup, and app-server login\nthrough the server runtime while preserving the existing local discovery\npath\n- add optional `threadId` to `mcpServer/oauth/login` and echo it in the\ncompletion notification\n- implement RMCP's redirect policy and 1 MiB OAuth response limit over\nexecutor HTTP\n- cover selected-thread OAuth discovery and login through an\nexecutor-only route\n\nDepends on #28522.","tree":{"sha":"c153b96cbd4d8c318f9bf64a3937f919e6019f2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c153b96cbd4d8c318f9bf64a3937f919e6019f2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b215961a56b2553a4612a22a812747403c08a58b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPPVlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoCkQAGjk1kMcqC327xkEOX4j+C5L\n+OnXjWnXF8mVGMd0NWWH4UpZLk5/7N8AOxGXQfYf6tbWQ4UfveR4kL9fbuvAcOzH\nMgfMC+39jpwlwA9ctBOkOaUY6/WMF9nWOWCHBjEKfSk4HLQDTNRLGxTuXAKsgJrk\notW51IMRr7XEz9P7NV196dxHl/D5p1o8lhFixquEwXukhOgfDKxLZIfDa6hbbm7u\nV6ql+ZYMBTJN/G+OB1dj4Fpqx5mv4EFvTBM3cuLm4aRed27XVslchZ3CtnhxWEw9\nR77aYcU2/do8qH/ZqbjwBdrqVQLI80XFsUUfiDp58Ch8QquwnMwlCVrPpJ1GfDf9\nbBx+boCNHjpVS9NNJefGppPHfkysH7VjZPWFTo4/LQSjyoEh8L5yon2jd6Kbd40v\npHI1/C6mMUlC0PFX0ocxW8SWqUEWj9J/q0G+D+GeLk7Nfoa0RKki9v/hVH+bSrim\nBiN6Rw4vyrOgApknb8MMgi9C/MKBd0h46A4c96COUKO27GuZ71L92sXbal4ySfB/\njUCs75m7n7qtINy5BSF6fkz2bxgeBEV856feefhQ6VHjsrmdMYAvASLTGigWX3dx\n5LXwnHDBMfKQrXRjOvGZ/r10agaDIPL1st8oCuXyL+uxUvVv6XofJfcgCdf/F04K\n6x60RI0DUvo2ZzXdqvGZ\n=vDi/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c153b96cbd4d8c318f9bf64a3937f919e6019f2b\nparent 6368937939dceb07b4a3c47c4448027d0d1a85a6\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782379877 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782379877 +0100\n\nSupport OAuth for HTTP MCP servers from selected executor plugins (#28529)\n\n## Why\n\n#28522 routes selected-plugin HTTP MCP traffic through the owning\nexecutor, but OAuth bootstrap and refresh still used host-local clients.\nExecutor-only servers therefore cannot complete discovery or login\nthrough the same network boundary as the MCP connection.\n\n## What changed\n\n- adapt `codex_exec_server::HttpClient` to RMCP 1.8's `OAuthHttpClient`\ncontract\n- let RMCP own discovery, dynamic registration, PKCE, token exchange,\nand refresh\n- route auth status, persisted-token startup, and app-server login\nthrough the server runtime while preserving the existing local discovery\npath\n- add optional `threadId` to `mcpServer/oauth/login` and echo it in the\ncompletion notification\n- implement RMCP's redirect policy and 1 MiB OAuth response limit over\nexecutor HTTP\n- cover selected-thread OAuth discovery and login through an\nexecutor-only route\n\nDepends on #28522.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T09:31:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b215961a56b2553a4612a22a812747403c08a58b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b215961a56b2553a4612a22a812747403c08a58b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b215961a56b2553a4612a22a812747403c08a58b/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6368937939dceb07b4a3c47c4448027d0d1a85a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6368937939dceb07b4a3c47c4448027d0d1a85a6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6368937939dceb07b4a3c47c4448027d0d1a85a6"}]},{"sha":"6368937939dceb07b4a3c47c4448027d0d1a85a6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYzNjg5Mzc5MzlkY2ViMDdiNGEzYzQ3YzQ0NDgwMjdkMGQxYTg1YTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T09:10:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T09:10:36Z"},"message":"Support HTTP MCP servers from selected executor plugins (#28522)\n\n## Why\n\nSelected executor plugins can declare both stdio and Streamable HTTP MCP\nservers, but only stdio registrations were retained. That silently drops\npart of the plugin's tool surface and prevents HTTP traffic from using\nthe owning executor's network.\n\n## What changed\n\n- retain selected-plugin Streamable HTTP MCP declarations alongside\nstdio declarations\n- route their HTTP clients through the owning executor environment\n- preserve local auth-header environment references while rejecting them\nfor executor-hosted declarations\n- cover thread isolation, refresh, and an executor-only HTTP route end\nto end","tree":{"sha":"4d01b729844dd191d703dad7e422cecfa323334d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4d01b729844dd191d703dad7e422cecfa323334d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6368937939dceb07b4a3c47c4448027d0d1a85a6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPPCMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyJsQAGoJJMu+R6TP0M81iPyBAlU8\n2eZcV99f8pio/jh23cq4nCwHwV51eEdbqomSWr4J9DW1EqseSQXybjiLwp6/7K5Q\nQ3uStcc51r/6d1hSIt8YNNX4s+9YPxVFEiujf8HKGiHetrD11lV81r95y5kd7L8s\npHPDIj312wCLogiScMbsy1Y81Kol6lmgniXHK/WWazfQZXGkvdN+ziZ30lB8asxt\n9+jYzX/6Orc3mVBnWzgIPyQUTuIwT8jb0zq71vqtQDAzH3a97K4Lmth/qY48qP3A\nJt60qAwieK/fgfIAcuAQ4nmZb2Pw6a/lPHsB253RFM8vvDDC9K2NaF61oebRn1zs\nLoTHOCgIzrGD06hrknZpTNC2XjbwASsKHIeuDTqXjbrwUOk1JooQdGZjkpeguyCe\nzNM1KtIhBgAACTPx7ozKIZelrkWIF/kyWyR3YQK3mMBu4WdeSBm3GvmRzH/94p3u\npdm+1D7SqZHgTk3IjOV2E3DKYIIDooL9YHpfUCID8yhHytfurrWyJ2qyjZvr5s+v\nLgOJcTfAkcT6hU2IzJT0Lx5LEcHHV0xXN3AV3r3gbNGHuLzj6CWbqjrd9E+AmKTL\nng3uA6Bwh4B0/0Q1UoyrtqgUGIH4s9VLbJtLiItasNUwo9omSFzkRzxrBjgft/7B\nwIu4yyLxSANPGgzMk8Wq\n=VNx3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4d01b729844dd191d703dad7e422cecfa323334d\nparent 5579792b3b881b44ba42139f9fcd191c4a944128\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782378636 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782378636 +0100\n\nSupport HTTP MCP servers from selected executor plugins (#28522)\n\n## Why\n\nSelected executor plugins can declare both stdio and Streamable HTTP MCP\nservers, but only stdio registrations were retained. That silently drops\npart of the plugin's tool surface and prevents HTTP traffic from using\nthe owning executor's network.\n\n## What changed\n\n- retain selected-plugin Streamable HTTP MCP declarations alongside\nstdio declarations\n- route their HTTP clients through the owning executor environment\n- preserve local auth-header environment references while rejecting them\nfor executor-hosted declarations\n- cover thread isolation, refresh, and an executor-only HTTP route end\nto end","verified_at":"2026-06-25T09:10:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6368937939dceb07b4a3c47c4448027d0d1a85a6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6368937939dceb07b4a3c47c4448027d0d1a85a6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6368937939dceb07b4a3c47c4448027d0d1a85a6/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5579792b3b881b44ba42139f9fcd191c4a944128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5579792b3b881b44ba42139f9fcd191c4a944128","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5579792b3b881b44ba42139f9fcd191c4a944128"}]},{"sha":"5579792b3b881b44ba42139f9fcd191c4a944128","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU1Nzk3OTJiM2I4ODFiNDRiYTQyMTM5ZjlmY2QxOTFjNGE5NDQxMjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T09:02:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T09:02:07Z"},"message":"Parallelize environment skill loading (#29990)\n\n## Why\n\nAvoid a request waterfall for loading lots of skills at once by hiding\nlatency in concurrent tasks.\n\n## What changed\n\nPoll the per-skill parse futures concurrently with an order-preserving\nstream capped at 64 in-flight loads. Results retain discovery order, and\nthe existing filtering, warnings, and final catalog sorting are\nunchanged.","tree":{"sha":"4e0e09d5ee5116b38e920badfa8ccd8b7a9b7038","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4e0e09d5ee5116b38e920badfa8ccd8b7a9b7038"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5579792b3b881b44ba42139f9fcd191c4a944128","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPO6PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvrsQAKlzMU7rDWcu811UkDm0uZyg\nPj4Q6vVs2o86HHyWLzMJ1++Vu2M3sYdIupefZzYFAUhdyXisK/CH+JwAXkBf8nfP\n5dqwTzG7ia+V6qFi+ktCEVoXiJrsfZzoE9IWYFdFFHmDVse9PEKohKdw1pB+quWf\n3JZX3/6DxjqUQbhgeiltzXfsWFOajeXy50W1L3EsQYQzDWCvJbM/CMYjUJIs8+Rp\nhssTGoMaPAbU8v/T2iLETQFH/8JiuAJOtPddtDxSVRrnYhhmIJv19k0W/g0pLqGf\nc6W1ydSQVXEVbKgHmJmgoBFDuGhlhFAoVtnFuNotd+PYYiTrBhvDe9oag6SZYy5S\nEZDhDMwwITPqqivnRs6L8nwRuGoKCQoZjMHlq6hIqKBsPblJhhyOW3UEPiq/OnbZ\nbJtRAX+FNW3HnswVUPwWGfvXHtZMWbOKE6SLKWOSd+Rh8Og0zbgM0D/eGdpJ+Ovx\ngRQT4lNWOXZMEW5wygicRb+NgqaRaQlTeu5ud0jIbp2BS7LyMij0BpOY98Z7Lnsb\n2Rn/k48HjUsWqzTRiZUhSf42CvTivZqYSSlZ9xovq/XFstqQLVC8H6/pkHl9A4fc\nXPbbMyRhMQVQPzgnSo+N3RnjU3Ybzr9GrNY4nYum9hNXRm2evjolJv+IWLFxFdu3\nF6uPBQx108LsjauqYhtE\n=8HAQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4e0e09d5ee5116b38e920badfa8ccd8b7a9b7038\nparent ab80d4d484609719621826946cd9e137a3558862\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782378127 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782378127 +0100\n\nParallelize environment skill loading (#29990)\n\n## Why\n\nAvoid a request waterfall for loading lots of skills at once by hiding\nlatency in concurrent tasks.\n\n## What changed\n\nPoll the per-skill parse futures concurrently with an order-preserving\nstream capped at 64 in-flight loads. Results retain discovery order, and\nthe existing filtering, warnings, and final catalog sorting are\nunchanged.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T09:02:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5579792b3b881b44ba42139f9fcd191c4a944128","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5579792b3b881b44ba42139f9fcd191c4a944128","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5579792b3b881b44ba42139f9fcd191c4a944128/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ab80d4d484609719621826946cd9e137a3558862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab80d4d484609719621826946cd9e137a3558862","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ab80d4d484609719621826946cd9e137a3558862"}]},{"sha":"ab80d4d484609719621826946cd9e137a3558862","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFiODBkNGQ0ODQ2MDk3MTk2MjE4MjY5NDZjZDllMTM3YTM1NTg4NjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T07:03:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T07:03:52Z"},"message":"core: reconcile legacy WorldState sections (#29997)\n\n## Why\n\nOlder rollouts can retain model-visible context for a WorldState section\nwithout having a persisted snapshot for that section. Treating the\nmissing snapshot as definitely absent can duplicate old context or fail\nto tell the model that it was replaced or removed.\n\nThis provides a generic migration path for sections moving into\nWorldState, beginning with AGENTS.md.\n\nBuilds on #29810.\n\n## What changed\n\n- distinguish section state that is absent, known from a persisted\nsnapshot, or unknown because matching legacy context remains in history\n- let WorldState sections identify their own legacy fragments while\n`ContextManager` owns history reconciliation and baseline persistence\n- make AGENTS.md emit one conservative replacement or removal update for\nlegacy history, then deduplicate from the newly persisted baseline\n- preserve existing environment rendering when persisted section data is\nmissing or malformed\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core world_state`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncold_resume_invalidates_deleted_legacy_agents_md_once -- --exact`","tree":{"sha":"c348b981f9f41eb219306970b0d8cea13e3fd497","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c348b981f9f41eb219306970b0d8cea13e3fd497"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ab80d4d484609719621826946cd9e137a3558862","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPNLYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD7IQAEJd1h0JatqZWe075vIA53BV\n9YKV0moWeIzLJTt559qCvu++cPCRwaRhdLP4QVyWloBY+lMP4LS+YGGF4LuBReVL\nEMXEc/8gh5pNZqMImB5itYx6x/gz17MJ3RfNwiMBsRfuEDXfju8ZtbNSAkhjn0H6\nwNp9sfsFn8Q9gqXUoSvpmSJTUnWj2ul25FAl0lKFVbT4pDHwd2FWlB1Ol4B19CA+\npV4jwKuw9AuFYebXFR/fHRKXYOpBvYWGHm5Mvrwh1g8lgRrxE8X4upbob460PsQV\n8exQAeAjkOpavcJRtgI1mQd5y3HiavR37JK0im4fjhcwkLzo4mldex7ESgmdr0w8\nxbDBb/F2A+0EksSOPe4+LR3llnImnqYmueqy660gxZNdjCXvwNJ+8/J3dlCoL7s8\nhOcijhA4kQWgQnDj52gXpBSsLJvhuUXLs+R0P+WHsoW47S73frxYb1OCQ1aqP8Tv\nveMY0C6tyyZfG3Gs8sgYbyU9lGCG7060NpaVO18tg504YQhrX2Xe2J0VvPMDcj+l\neM/mq92M39XvwKi7NAevP68FHFvOj2RNhulntzftcJHU1f+JAFlGF2AGx40fty0o\nqntabcKfofGnTP8vEekn5MQ0T2HbtuZMsNE5B0BkCFHeI/1ByDsjiTRMAWAE+Dmg\n/aACjPmhVR+va6BQzcaa\n=6I4P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c348b981f9f41eb219306970b0d8cea13e3fd497\nparent f2f80ef442ff84612004bad064991283eb17cdb5\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782371032 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782371032 +0000\n\ncore: reconcile legacy WorldState sections (#29997)\n\n## Why\n\nOlder rollouts can retain model-visible context for a WorldState section\nwithout having a persisted snapshot for that section. Treating the\nmissing snapshot as definitely absent can duplicate old context or fail\nto tell the model that it was replaced or removed.\n\nThis provides a generic migration path for sections moving into\nWorldState, beginning with AGENTS.md.\n\nBuilds on #29810.\n\n## What changed\n\n- distinguish section state that is absent, known from a persisted\nsnapshot, or unknown because matching legacy context remains in history\n- let WorldState sections identify their own legacy fragments while\n`ContextManager` owns history reconciliation and baseline persistence\n- make AGENTS.md emit one conservative replacement or removal update for\nlegacy history, then deduplicate from the newly persisted baseline\n- preserve existing environment rendering when persisted section data is\nmissing or malformed\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core world_state`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncold_resume_invalidates_deleted_legacy_agents_md_once -- --exact`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T07:03:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab80d4d484609719621826946cd9e137a3558862","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ab80d4d484609719621826946cd9e137a3558862","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab80d4d484609719621826946cd9e137a3558862/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f2f80ef442ff84612004bad064991283eb17cdb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f2f80ef442ff84612004bad064991283eb17cdb5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f2f80ef442ff84612004bad064991283eb17cdb5"}]},{"sha":"f2f80ef442ff84612004bad064991283eb17cdb5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYyZjgwZWY0NDJmZjg0NjEyMDA0YmFkMDY0OTkxMjgzZWIxN2NkYjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:57:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:57:42Z"},"message":"core: make AGENTS.md react to environment changes (#29810)\n\n## Why\n\nWith deferred executors, a turn can begin before a remote environment\nattaches. AGENTS.md discovery previously ran only during session setup,\nso instructions from a later environment never reached the model or the\nsession instruction sources.\n\nWorldState persistence has now landed, so this uses the durable\nmodel-visible baseline directly instead of carrying a temporary\nresume/fork compatibility path.\n\n## What\n\n- Add an `AgentsMdManager` in `SessionServices` to own host\ninstructions, loaded state, and refresh caching.\n- When `DeferredExecutor` is enabled, refresh AGENTS.md when attached\nenvironment selections change and freeze the result in the corresponding\n`StepContext`.\n- Represent AGENTS.md as a persisted WorldState section for every\nsession, with bounded initial, replacement, and removal updates.\n- Remove duplicate AGENTS.md state and rendering from\n`SessionConfiguration` and `TurnContext`.\n- Build initial context, per-request updates, and compaction context\nfrom the same step-scoped value.\n- On resume and fork, compare current instructions with the restored\nWorldState baseline and inject a replacement exactly once when they\ndiffer.\n\nBuilds on #29833, #29835, and #29837.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Covers a remote environment becoming ready mid-turn, with AGENTS.md\nappearing on the next request exactly once and updating canonical\ninstruction sources.\n- Covers full, unchanged, replaced, and removed AGENTS.md WorldState\nrendering.\n- Covers changed instructions across cold resume and fork without\nduplicate reinjection.\n- Covers remote-v2 compaction retaining creation-time instructions in\nthe live session and cold resume appending one replacement when the\nsource changed.\n- Ran focused `codex-core` AGENTS.md, WorldState, and context-update\ntest suites.","tree":{"sha":"d1ff2a0dd12b7df26c9d0aac30bd45bb88769bd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d1ff2a0dd12b7df26c9d0aac30bd45bb88769bd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f2f80ef442ff84612004bad064991283eb17cdb5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPMNWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKgMQAG/HbyDTq+Lr48BzdtUd0ahi\nrbxN6Uw+klHXuy/vNZ8EsDwdr14M7fiSE+/jmLGLXe9uYmaTsc+sKkxYnpplP38J\nLHdTlZKjMC2JmpvKlC+2nUO6n3g1sOVPtVZKXq/2HOuvbisEG6wlvOaJupXIIDM2\nr2ax/qTJ0NGVuNZ6YtqirbGvAWq4Ee28BcUtHrRCwZ4VDxKYt7CwL/Zv7+X4iznC\nyKdOekyEqcQfLctj+7Hi0IE7TAZQFwpD29PV8o/aoZ/nrQK2QFNRL68b/GX4ZkLD\n+MH1SyC4K2ZFBVI1REgc096eJFn9W0FLwXVAj0n91KGxmGlVU0WSqyyloYFzMIuX\nkjWREkDT3gjN+EJBN1poik8uaEXot0cC50ZhCkhgAV89RNYl3pcFrPNAstDEUJyn\ncHfOtdUV2neBKBL2S1BicV+mIiWfmY7mdbHMoHhELplFr1s7CjfrTrwGgOBBVuGL\nO1MmJbMrnQazhc/tkVE5oi4nOmyOjsnj00QC1iEgSxu11i+z8CIqTcEDAUOecKRV\n2FhZ9NDhEoNbfXe/vawp1NjpolQP8+Y3dqj0gQq7DoMKBMR3LrFjOK9lHGlFFZux\nC1PkDzTvPsFFtAXEtosNpLpQSqi+NUr7bEAkRagoUsWb5/PLsON8sPr9dPYQGMXV\n0iEPCRYNaPliwpINQkW+\n=vz+i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d1ff2a0dd12b7df26c9d0aac30bd45bb88769bd3\nparent 51864b0b4b4105ce1503dd80d9c93c0c9b4d9085\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782367062 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782367062 -0700\n\ncore: make AGENTS.md react to environment changes (#29810)\n\n## Why\n\nWith deferred executors, a turn can begin before a remote environment\nattaches. AGENTS.md discovery previously ran only during session setup,\nso instructions from a later environment never reached the model or the\nsession instruction sources.\n\nWorldState persistence has now landed, so this uses the durable\nmodel-visible baseline directly instead of carrying a temporary\nresume/fork compatibility path.\n\n## What\n\n- Add an `AgentsMdManager` in `SessionServices` to own host\ninstructions, loaded state, and refresh caching.\n- When `DeferredExecutor` is enabled, refresh AGENTS.md when attached\nenvironment selections change and freeze the result in the corresponding\n`StepContext`.\n- Represent AGENTS.md as a persisted WorldState section for every\nsession, with bounded initial, replacement, and removal updates.\n- Remove duplicate AGENTS.md state and rendering from\n`SessionConfiguration` and `TurnContext`.\n- Build initial context, per-request updates, and compaction context\nfrom the same step-scoped value.\n- On resume and fork, compare current instructions with the restored\nWorldState baseline and inject a replacement exactly once when they\ndiffer.\n\nBuilds on #29833, #29835, and #29837.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Covers a remote environment becoming ready mid-turn, with AGENTS.md\nappearing on the next request exactly once and updating canonical\ninstruction sources.\n- Covers full, unchanged, replaced, and removed AGENTS.md WorldState\nrendering.\n- Covers changed instructions across cold resume and fork without\nduplicate reinjection.\n- Covers remote-v2 compaction retaining creation-time instructions in\nthe live session and cold resume appending one replacement when the\nsource changed.\n- Ran focused `codex-core` AGENTS.md, WorldState, and context-update\ntest suites.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T05:57:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f2f80ef442ff84612004bad064991283eb17cdb5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f2f80ef442ff84612004bad064991283eb17cdb5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f2f80ef442ff84612004bad064991283eb17cdb5/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"51864b0b4b4105ce1503dd80d9c93c0c9b4d9085","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/51864b0b4b4105ce1503dd80d9c93c0c9b4d9085","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/51864b0b4b4105ce1503dd80d9c93c0c9b4d9085"}]},{"sha":"51864b0b4b4105ce1503dd80d9c93c0c9b4d9085","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUxODY0YjBiNGI0MTA1Y2UxNTAzZGQ4MGQ5YzkzYzBjOWI0ZDkwODU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adrian","email":"145513011+adrian-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:31:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:31:41Z"},"message":"feat: use run agent task auth for inference (#19051)\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 3 of the simplified HAI single-run-task stack:\n\n- [#19047](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19047) Agent Identity\nassertion and task-registration primitives, including the shared\nrun-task helper used by existing Agent Identity JWT auth.\n- [#19049](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19049)\nDisabled-by-default ChatGPT auth opt-in that provisions/reuses persisted\nAgent Identity runtime auth and its single run task.\n- [#19051](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19051) Run-scoped\nprovider auth that uses one backend-owned task id for first-party\ninference and compaction requests.\n\n[#19054](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19054) collapsed out of\nthe active stack because the simplified design no longer needs a\nseparate background/control-plane task helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR moves Agent Identity usage into provider auth resolution. That\nkeeps `AgentAssertion` auth tied to first-party OpenAI provider requests\ninstead of applying a late session-wide override that could affect\nlocal, custom, Bedrock, API-key, or external-bearer providers.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- adds a small `ProviderAuthScope` struct carrying the run auth policy\nand session source needed by provider-scoped auth resolution\n- lets `Session` opt the existing `ModelClient` into `ChatGptAuth`\npolicy when `use_agent_identity` is enabled, without adding a second\nmodel-client constructor\n- resolves Agent Identity only for first-party OpenAI provider auth\npaths\n- uses the persisted run task id from the `AgentIdentityAuth` record to\nbuild `AgentAssertion` auth for Responses requests\n- routes shared request setup through scoped provider auth so unary\ncompact requests use the same run-task assertion path as inference turns\n- keeps local/custom/Bedrock/env-key/external-bearer provider auth\nunchanged\n- lets missing run-task state surface through the existing model-request\nerror path instead of silently falling back to bearer auth\n\nThis PR intentionally does not create thread-scoped, target-scoped, or\nbackground-scoped task identities. The run task is the only task Codex\nregisters in this POC shape.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-model-provider`\n- `just test -p codex-core client::tests::provider_auth_scope_uses`\n- `just test -p codex-core remote_compact_uses_agent_identity_assertion`","tree":{"sha":"00f8f0ec3e9507d057a2bd6c85aa51d14d0ee4f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/00f8f0ec3e9507d057a2bd6c85aa51d14d0ee4f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/51864b0b4b4105ce1503dd80d9c93c0c9b4d9085","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPL09CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHA8QAAHVMMLbvJsjfK4juj9eqair\nzzEEd/dImxg12QOaWtMnXUozyS2Rpgbe5Cz6uaYvgbhnZKqLDR8wAH25LpNLgamT\nj3XZ1EfT7h5vzBcrUNuThtH+pZ4etkEwSKGAKtnMmq258buCvUQhM/2n7e2pr8rN\n+Qqx3TaYq9rZnzB2sawcqQ1u9KxtZuXwo4OO22uDGbsRXd4hnDVm4M9HirFjjVk+\nCjpD4p8vuMqQn4meHOG0H2BdrLX+YeQBsVqn/NRQXpBII5RoigbCEaLoOEvItvZc\nIstm+ONDD7Uo3laFjZT9VaHJH9rQWo/2VND3ngLJpRkFOn5DXnR6uiWHhGBAhhe7\ntPt3exko1wCRzRyPmQ1shcxtIjyxndxCj44FzZskwLluqplo/Bvk0gfNdHMizMgG\n5zUmrIEjTl4wL7OBXdTxxRFKGl7s38bjNT/BQ8ic4XEKmcQKgGDXIIEOOlhYrPpQ\nzi+PxxvC/W0Bwjb/4H3/YTCnVSbuXASKfnCx68JSy4LeR5cFvSWZKsaOLGtUZXoe\n5fCAf1wJk7c6I6tp2mpcUl6flP55bLtCItXyxwwlw//3QFSyEf3JuKkipFnWDV83\nOsQIQoVBMqSty7p+Q+dg9NFgOJy2ljyWnLOMHrMyJIxRBa4E5qR/8YucuwYUre2Q\nVkW3S2E/juBOtqfgRQes\n=olMO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 00f8f0ec3e9507d057a2bd6c85aa51d14d0ee4f9\nparent f66d793a2d78287c8c28a5f41f39c58ac49bcc25\nauthor Adrian <145513011+adrian-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1782365501 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782365501 -0700\n\nfeat: use run agent task auth for inference (#19051)\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 3 of the simplified HAI single-run-task stack:\n\n- [#19047](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19047) Agent Identity\nassertion and task-registration primitives, including the shared\nrun-task helper used by existing Agent Identity JWT auth.\n- [#19049](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19049)\nDisabled-by-default ChatGPT auth opt-in that provisions/reuses persisted\nAgent Identity runtime auth and its single run task.\n- [#19051](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19051) Run-scoped\nprovider auth that uses one backend-owned task id for first-party\ninference and compaction requests.\n\n[#19054](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19054) collapsed out of\nthe active stack because the simplified design no longer needs a\nseparate background/control-plane task helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR moves Agent Identity usage into provider auth resolution. That\nkeeps `AgentAssertion` auth tied to first-party OpenAI provider requests\ninstead of applying a late session-wide override that could affect\nlocal, custom, Bedrock, API-key, or external-bearer providers.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- adds a small `ProviderAuthScope` struct carrying the run auth policy\nand session source needed by provider-scoped auth resolution\n- lets `Session` opt the existing `ModelClient` into `ChatGptAuth`\npolicy when `use_agent_identity` is enabled, without adding a second\nmodel-client constructor\n- resolves Agent Identity only for first-party OpenAI provider auth\npaths\n- uses the persisted run task id from the `AgentIdentityAuth` record to\nbuild `AgentAssertion` auth for Responses requests\n- routes shared request setup through scoped provider auth so unary\ncompact requests use the same run-task assertion path as inference turns\n- keeps local/custom/Bedrock/env-key/external-bearer provider auth\nunchanged\n- lets missing run-task state surface through the existing model-request\nerror path instead of silently falling back to bearer auth\n\nThis PR intentionally does not create thread-scoped, target-scoped, or\nbackground-scoped task identities. The run task is the only task Codex\nregisters in this POC shape.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-model-provider`\n- `just test -p codex-core client::tests::provider_auth_scope_uses`\n- `just test -p codex-core remote_compact_uses_agent_identity_assertion`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T05:31:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/51864b0b4b4105ce1503dd80d9c93c0c9b4d9085","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/51864b0b4b4105ce1503dd80d9c93c0c9b4d9085","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/51864b0b4b4105ce1503dd80d9c93c0c9b4d9085/comments","author":{"login":"adrian-openai","id":145513011,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKxaMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145513011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/adrian-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f66d793a2d78287c8c28a5f41f39c58ac49bcc25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f66d793a2d78287c8c28a5f41f39c58ac49bcc25","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f66d793a2d78287c8c28a5f41f39c58ac49bcc25"}]},{"sha":"f66d793a2d78287c8c28a5f41f39c58ac49bcc25","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY2NmQ3OTNhMmQ3ODI4N2M4YzI4YTVmNDFmMzljNThhYzQ5YmNjMjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:17:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:17:43Z"},"message":"[codex] route sleep through time providers (#29973)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add a cancellable sleep operation to `TimeProvider`\n- route `clock.sleep` through the configured provider\n- extend the supported sleep duration to 12 hours\n- complete the sleep turn item before propagating provider failures\n\n## Why\n\nThis isolates the core clock abstraction needed by external clock\nintegrations. Existing system and app-server behavior remains wall-clock\nbased in this PR; the stacked follow-up supplies app-server sleeps from\nan external clock.","tree":{"sha":"afc97a9165318e093e002bffe3089f5e9b27e7ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/afc97a9165318e093e002bffe3089f5e9b27e7ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f66d793a2d78287c8c28a5f41f39c58ac49bcc25","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPLn3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA30YQADXMfl6LCMOqhDld3B2dNIki\nCHcZiDRdK5aq4mSXuETUpfuUzara9ey/MDBXyekP5m3xLfliS5hovsjdETgIlDMX\nJIpyZinLWIQq4cfr/jwMOmVeQUmyeo4i4mku0ZUCoRhnLZOGeDuQkS8eUQRf5w/R\niZPBQgiYqnWMrlyprGefEc/nKjw+DN/qcqJhfJq3n87Rb0gvU9msvUdViueGXtvk\nQXgtOYXNQomZb5hY+1/VPUI5GXPe+cuUMsS3VQkTi07+rxvJ7yZNDv/BEJAO+OFm\nc7b2I4D987FfS+/YxoBsUG0dddMBe7Kj/31IuYZYmOFW+2VRQZhxDjiyDDf8dhhN\nPUuKOLaATRUFNRMlD3LjaXPftBgPgpXQB2M58rbK0ZppSF7qckCh9VN3xcroi/5E\nGjYT69wiUVAdiGmM5dn7Oi8zF2qBgUa8Rl4p5kIEsuBv4sUlIbJKgoRzftCCS0K7\n/rqCL2ThLCBl7Vi5RQiM+DbajNwdhiUKq5+M0bYlYQr8Esfz8nHSbvBUGkWWVXty\nrzAOmt4S+ip0JYYgWnIG5ifSMUVD6NIQtmcx23QvWzhKW3GpliajGndY+KpcDHd7\nPZIhNiDjCMGbtIEHjWgPvucKEn3djVf7Kbcn6b1wdhGlOqwgHphB1YBVSvCgTdQN\n/2dUSktL6yjZXr6qL/7e\n=yk+p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree afc97a9165318e093e002bffe3089f5e9b27e7ca\nparent 22f12568e1f5d4fe72c5201c3d1f1fc103fc8ea5\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782364663 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782364663 -0700\n\n[codex] route sleep through time providers (#29973)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add a cancellable sleep operation to `TimeProvider`\n- route `clock.sleep` through the configured provider\n- extend the supported sleep duration to 12 hours\n- complete the sleep turn item before propagating provider failures\n\n## Why\n\nThis isolates the core clock abstraction needed by external clock\nintegrations. Existing system and app-server behavior remains wall-clock\nbased in this PR; the stacked follow-up supplies app-server sleeps from\nan external clock.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T05:17:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f66d793a2d78287c8c28a5f41f39c58ac49bcc25","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f66d793a2d78287c8c28a5f41f39c58ac49bcc25","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f66d793a2d78287c8c28a5f41f39c58ac49bcc25/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"22f12568e1f5d4fe72c5201c3d1f1fc103fc8ea5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22f12568e1f5d4fe72c5201c3d1f1fc103fc8ea5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/22f12568e1f5d4fe72c5201c3d1f1fc103fc8ea5"}]},{"sha":"22f12568e1f5d4fe72c5201c3d1f1fc103fc8ea5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIyZjEyNTY4ZTFmNWQ0ZmU3MmM1MjAxYzNkMWYxZmMxMDNmYzhlYTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:05:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:05:32Z"},"message":"core: raise token budget message limits (#29970)\n\n## Why\n\nToken-budget reminder and guidance messages can require more than 1,000\nbytes to provide useful model-facing instructions. At the same time,\nthese strings are injected into model-visible context, so their size\nmust remain tightly bounded in response to the P0 context-growth\nconcern. A 2,000-byte runtime cap provides additional room without\nallowing the substantially larger context growth of a 4 KiB limit.\n\n## What changed\n\n- raises the runtime byte limits for token-budget reminder templates and\nguidance messages from 1,000 to 2,000\n- raises the corresponding JSON Schema `maxLength` values to 2,000\n- regenerates `codex-rs/core/config.schema.json`\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-core load_config_resolves_token_budget_config\nload_config_rejects_invalid_token_budget_reminder_template`\n\nThe full `codex-core` test run completed 2,858 tests successfully and\nencountered seven unrelated environment-sensitive failures involving\nSeatbelt/network environment assertions, MCP capability setup, and abort\ntiming.","tree":{"sha":"f9a9890232917f0c665ef2b57cde208b4b431c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f9a9890232917f0c665ef2b57cde208b4b431c28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/22f12568e1f5d4fe72c5201c3d1f1fc103fc8ea5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPLccCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGBQQAIUjwcpa1DJ/KsCIjvOfU+3y\nUFZgmFSE65sEXGC8c5bueC++3N0vGoNimTqRNpzrPfY6Sf5X22E9LNV+LSLE3Dxd\nPDLZTBaO3kCIdNKTVMf859/0foZu28/J1S6C7n+cWee6DpcE0Y9tACbJWfWxWhXo\n607jM5bREVjhSJ+Q4xBFyUet4UmPakrWkqglhaC8Z5FcM77TPPY9xHjNRcpUtU7r\nMRp/6WbZUNGOaj4RcrzLDr22FYENnnZPDezxMjMpAybWV5jVAl53P6GG1zvLxvvj\n137Qs/9A6OyYskUVArBF8pgVv78e7aN2mjJR4c+58DdDYm8CVj31ysIpdEiiMjEe\nmEuIoE3j/0P8xhDvNsCK3UhKoM49HHGmYaFxkERkfyMXxDg3xdihICgkr+WK87q5\nb4jBbC6gYbpG6dn9PqLkeZWMwfUHvIdlSa2IGvDE0h6MQbaTwu+UvBwGH5ZHCydH\nIscDS8221Qhza3C0DvKnPPzpY3Su2D4z1mUC4XuxKKyk08OEqMFCOsaNdGlojgSA\nmUbCLmwSaN430WUs6F7ODhuqqTOfUNA7WsN2vRSDx0YF/rwJnedfD0EAeDCbYiho\njSvEFQhhRw7VRUxGeH7ldmufgLW+zmQuyXSL3x8UzcjGhkxeUZU6q95nPem+ab4T\nVAMt+8m3GetDmTt1IIaP\n=fPrR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f9a9890232917f0c665ef2b57cde208b4b431c28\nparent cef5444a80ac5a94d435ab780fba5d6f433c504f\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782363932 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782363932 +0000\n\ncore: raise token budget message limits (#29970)\n\n## Why\n\nToken-budget reminder and guidance messages can require more than 1,000\nbytes to provide useful model-facing instructions. At the same time,\nthese strings are injected into model-visible context, so their size\nmust remain tightly bounded in response to the P0 context-growth\nconcern. A 2,000-byte runtime cap provides additional room without\nallowing the substantially larger context growth of a 4 KiB limit.\n\n## What changed\n\n- raises the runtime byte limits for token-budget reminder templates and\nguidance messages from 1,000 to 2,000\n- raises the corresponding JSON Schema `maxLength` values to 2,000\n- regenerates `codex-rs/core/config.schema.json`\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-core load_config_resolves_token_budget_config\nload_config_rejects_invalid_token_budget_reminder_template`\n\nThe full `codex-core` test run completed 2,858 tests successfully and\nencountered seven unrelated environment-sensitive failures involving\nSeatbelt/network environment assertions, MCP capability setup, and abort\ntiming.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T05:05:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22f12568e1f5d4fe72c5201c3d1f1fc103fc8ea5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/22f12568e1f5d4fe72c5201c3d1f1fc103fc8ea5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22f12568e1f5d4fe72c5201c3d1f1fc103fc8ea5/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cef5444a80ac5a94d435ab780fba5d6f433c504f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cef5444a80ac5a94d435ab780fba5d6f433c504f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cef5444a80ac5a94d435ab780fba5d6f433c504f"}]},{"sha":"cef5444a80ac5a94d435ab780fba5d6f433c504f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNlZjU0NDRhODBhYzVhOTRkNDM1YWI3ODBmYmE1ZDZmNDMzYzUwNGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T04:08:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T04:08:39Z"},"message":"Report MCP error codes with server attribution (#29969)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP error-code telemetry special-cased Codex Apps: its reported error\ncodes were retained, while codes from every other MCP server were\nreplaced with `unknown`. Error reporting should behave consistently for\nevery MCP server. The server name already identifies where an error came\nfrom, so telemetry does not need a separate Codex Apps classification.\n\nThis follows up on [#28976](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28976),\nwhich introduced MCP error-code telemetry.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the MCP server name to call, duration, and error metrics.\n- Retain bounded, sanitized tool error codes from every MCP server.\n- Remove `McpErrorCodeSource` and the Codex Apps ownership lookup from\ntelemetry collection.\n- Use the same metric-tagging path for blocked, rejected, and executed\nMCP calls.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Verify the complete metric tag set includes the sanitized MCP server\nname.\n- Verify error codes from ordinary MCP servers are retained, bounded,\nand sanitized.\n- Preserve coverage for request failures, tool-result failures, nested\nauth failures, and span attributes.","tree":{"sha":"33c4299dda595415cfcdf35fa39a23e7bfce7d84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/33c4299dda595415cfcdf35fa39a23e7bfce7d84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cef5444a80ac5a94d435ab780fba5d6f433c504f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPKnHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARfcQAH2iVy28xJR9RPYvJslNQc9Z\new6Wqa0YB2sozsH/RaB/PRlqQwv40wN7RviH7eVmYI7okpHw6jovrxsFBB/zv/ZJ\nOzIY60/2iFXSa/NnS8dP8JF2PsRmE16+3fhbkhAqkf17Xf3UB62hO+CxDpUbmuUn\nN95bTA03J6ccORGML+SD2ixyNF1h47Lns6IemOzYJ56G641ez8usoGb67b+5pJib\nw0R/OpYPGAE4/iYJFjyLh7uKC6Qvzc7pyc5GCJvd65LJa+uni4H4p06L/inmicIt\ndolGbHWfbb7WWQXlGyuD/eprEkVeg/2wXkpv4OOuYTfOSLOvU0w6Gd4BaesEpGLx\nT1H0U097Raz5KPJ9iQ8OOEFoccW1BsneyuLUc5i/cDNld6nd7f1XLsTJ+QYaTdUI\nC2d7Jj0BMJFovVTZDj8Xd7Df5+BVjHv+Zzo/K2KkYMT8VG3lXW2+q4LKHktnxeuU\nLWsnuzIzyLMZ/oAXqfKFRSuKsCmEz0xqNVgnUYlwixM/kck0lK9JplxO/uXr4OjO\nBqCoVItryV4FEwvSe2Dwn8VIyULMPID2550WdqXqU9v8wJr7StNRa0UIaeeZit8+\nfwNwB+517eLDSgFUbH79kOkuWc3DJxXvrtmjujuW41CWHoQS+i6kIu0HKDBvA2xE\npAa6NlCPnRpwpnVOKtUH\n=DQr2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 33c4299dda595415cfcdf35fa39a23e7bfce7d84\nparent a74771340db6eb81db39e81445a706346f14c139\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1782360519 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782360519 -0700\n\nReport MCP error codes with server attribution (#29969)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP error-code telemetry special-cased Codex Apps: its reported error\ncodes were retained, while codes from every other MCP server were\nreplaced with `unknown`. Error reporting should behave consistently for\nevery MCP server. The server name already identifies where an error came\nfrom, so telemetry does not need a separate Codex Apps classification.\n\nThis follows up on [#28976](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28976),\nwhich introduced MCP error-code telemetry.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the MCP server name to call, duration, and error metrics.\n- Retain bounded, sanitized tool error codes from every MCP server.\n- Remove `McpErrorCodeSource` and the Codex Apps ownership lookup from\ntelemetry collection.\n- Use the same metric-tagging path for blocked, rejected, and executed\nMCP calls.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Verify the complete metric tag set includes the sanitized MCP server\nname.\n- Verify error codes from ordinary MCP servers are retained, bounded,\nand sanitized.\n- Preserve coverage for request failures, tool-result failures, nested\nauth failures, and span attributes.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T04:08:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cef5444a80ac5a94d435ab780fba5d6f433c504f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cef5444a80ac5a94d435ab780fba5d6f433c504f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cef5444a80ac5a94d435ab780fba5d6f433c504f/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a74771340db6eb81db39e81445a706346f14c139","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a74771340db6eb81db39e81445a706346f14c139","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a74771340db6eb81db39e81445a706346f14c139"}]},{"sha":"a74771340db6eb81db39e81445a706346f14c139","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE3NDc3MTM0MGRiNmViODFkYjM5ZTgxNDQ1YTcwNjM0NmYxNGMxMzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:32:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:32:08Z"},"message":"[3/3] core: replay persisted world state (#29837)\n\n## Why\n\nPersisting `WorldState` snapshots and patches is only useful if resume\nand fork restore that exact comparison baseline. Rebuilding it from\n`TurnContextItem` loses section state and can either repeat or suppress\nmodel-visible updates.\n\nThis is the third PR in the WorldState persistence stack, built on\n#29835.\n\n## What\n\n- Replay full WorldState snapshots and RFC 7386 patches through the\nexisting rollout reconstruction segments.\n- Discard state from rolled-back turns and treat compaction as a\nbaseline reset.\n- Hydrate `ContextManager` from the reconstructed snapshot on resume and\nfork.\n- Remove the synthetic `TurnContextItem` to WorldState conversion path.\n- Leave legacy or malformed rollouts without a baseline so the next\nupdate safely emits a full snapshot.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core world_state`\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_reconstruction_tests`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just test -p codex-core` *(the changed tests passed; the full run\nalso hit unrelated existing/test-environment failures, primarily a\nmissing `test_stdio_server` binary)*","tree":{"sha":"6d2db943a2ff8d7817e150597cd26a3f8c7ac16b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6d2db943a2ff8d7817e150597cd26a3f8c7ac16b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a74771340db6eb81db39e81445a706346f14c139","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPKE4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs5EQAHa2VlrNyCNTftiBjhD393kI\nQLkpBBEc4xAcW14IuRFU3pY0TD+ZqX/dA6MLMF9pYdT87cakQOr73PsXsDXk60JA\nNDJ75jxNKyR57ataIJ/wSL7hATvYfSwymGmd6+G+ElY8ZEObdmL/nWOHyWg9xyep\nbebnBSm4bNrWMYixL+vtDyLkgnCIJh1qZW/iEPVcVYchGwNdMV9mV5Lni9/IgFNK\nAS9toiPsRsK+96hafPGEfoyFsuoalromPnLhh8Vk3S+3Q1AtHVhBzYyH3YP3tHEY\nJI/iuGa2odLjHZckZ0AkeFzinCr+bpWEmGufzfbX525RfJHOhw99o56lx+i2QM6u\npR0piS4NiHwoZ0YQ9uCfgDV1+tkUND+6bg15SwgtZ2tPSFOluM6D6A+687NwI1p7\nK00hoixfb5GYtpwN+T/QuNvGNDho8Qm8YrqyY30kHQ3XD7uTtAx29gHLQFFDJBZM\n7+XS/6ieY/TA/uF9y0FquHlM5uUw9PeBvH23xEaKwsVGE3xRtG3X3tDrn7fEhlv6\np/dUuNqDl4FNZkV0h0aieDlX0Yanbf1Rhp9x+CnrKmiBwDWDVIaNL+L2hoRkQ+c4\n0CwRojefIv0Ft3BlPs2d/g5dEG8zpgNRqHrMSjWh7IQW6wxkLC1wPTIVd44Nau22\nVFLGDqGgWKjxnKlsW1h+\n=Zmzm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6d2db943a2ff8d7817e150597cd26a3f8c7ac16b\nparent df1199fddb0c41441b7cd5a1f48bc48514a617dd\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782358328 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782358328 +0000\n\n[3/3] core: replay persisted world state (#29837)\n\n## Why\n\nPersisting `WorldState` snapshots and patches is only useful if resume\nand fork restore that exact comparison baseline. Rebuilding it from\n`TurnContextItem` loses section state and can either repeat or suppress\nmodel-visible updates.\n\nThis is the third PR in the WorldState persistence stack, built on\n#29835.\n\n## What\n\n- Replay full WorldState snapshots and RFC 7386 patches through the\nexisting rollout reconstruction segments.\n- Discard state from rolled-back turns and treat compaction as a\nbaseline reset.\n- Hydrate `ContextManager` from the reconstructed snapshot on resume and\nfork.\n- Remove the synthetic `TurnContextItem` to WorldState conversion path.\n- Leave legacy or malformed rollouts without a baseline so the next\nupdate safely emits a full snapshot.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core world_state`\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_reconstruction_tests`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just test -p codex-core` *(the changed tests passed; the full run\nalso hit unrelated existing/test-environment failures, primarily a\nmissing `test_stdio_server` binary)*","verified_at":"2026-06-25T03:32:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a74771340db6eb81db39e81445a706346f14c139","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a74771340db6eb81db39e81445a706346f14c139","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a74771340db6eb81db39e81445a706346f14c139/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"df1199fddb0c41441b7cd5a1f48bc48514a617dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df1199fddb0c41441b7cd5a1f48bc48514a617dd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/df1199fddb0c41441b7cd5a1f48bc48514a617dd"}]},{"sha":"df1199fddb0c41441b7cd5a1f48bc48514a617dd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRmMTE5OWZkZGIwYzQxNDQxYjdjZDVhMWY0OGJjNDg1MTRhNjE3ZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:13:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:13:52Z"},"message":"[codex] Add Ultra reasoning effort (#29899)\n\n## Why\n\nUltra should be one user-facing reasoning selection for work that\nbenefits from both maximum reasoning and proactive multi-agent\ndelegation. Without it, clients must coordinate maximum reasoning with\nthe experimental `multiAgentMode` setting, even though the inference\nbackend still expects its existing `max` effort value.\n\nThis change makes reasoning effort the source of truth: clients select\n`ultra`, core derives proactive multi-agent behavior when the turn is\neligible for multi-agent V2, and inference requests continue to use the\nbackend-compatible `max` value.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `ultra` as a first-class reasoning effort and preserve\nmodel-catalog ordering when exposing it to clients.\n- Convert `ultra` to `max` at the inference request boundary, including\nResponses HTTP/WebSocket requests, startup prewarm, compaction, and\nmemory summarization.\n- Derive effective multi-agent mode per turn from effective reasoning\neffort:\n  - eligible multi-agent V2 + `ultra` → `proactive`\n  - eligible multi-agent V2 + any other effort → `explicitRequestOnly`\n- V1 or otherwise ineligible sessions → no multi-agent mode instruction\n- Keep the derived effective mode in turn context history so successive\nturns can emit a developer-message update only when the effective mode\nchanges.\n- Remove selected multi-agent mode from core session configuration, turn\nconstruction, thread settings, resume/fork restoration, and subagent\nspawn plumbing. Subagents inherit reasoning effort and derive their own\neffective mode.\n- Retain the experimental app-server `multiAgentMode` fields for wire\ncompatibility while marking them deprecated. Request values are accepted\nbut ignored; compatibility response fields report `explicitRequestOnly`.\n- Display Ultra in the TUI using the order supplied by `model/list`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core ultra_reasoning_uses_max_for_requests`\n- `just test -p codex-tui model_reasoning_selection_popup`","tree":{"sha":"b00e79115c7ea6f61de227e8b96214870073c105","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b00e79115c7ea6f61de227e8b96214870073c105"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/df1199fddb0c41441b7cd5a1f48bc48514a617dd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPJzwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7sEQAGTMkB6qWW3XhmF3XwG5ww7m\nsY2IHAb1GWbdtt82DFUCsLeOFy4A3LMDXD7qUphgbuJKEfrgBydvRCZv89dO8boL\nhWnG/hR1Q3lEQ1niYVMBeB5gKPW2D+DpFLxFG/pQAJv5us6rjkkM13EXj/Pi1mRk\nA9ShhTNAZBN9yfLiYfZn545l7hX19lyTbPqexkdpPXTF8BFT41nBQBQaOTWd7pAo\nSY2wpJZ4vBk3XPKirJt6ksNR9/o94iLr7GBbEyA9VHsGbPuHS235OG1jWMcxbhAB\nqxyWecxkNQ1CpB2IduIELjBKIFaEH0k/f52pPsvQbypCVl18jcSUuN9YHVw+es7d\n/Uiwl7RYg9emTTPQ0HxMIa9zpMmDj4MkDJAC77J3nay3LSiatwIsVqlgy/Ni2SHR\nrnmxb8n72gVXhvFt+LG50tK9x2pamkRBBiZSzwFjTD4i8Oez4cxjdbHkkw3Q9tcl\n9Y6rJSXvhxRRA5LetY0L9e1yus0aPHQsL9NpgguqvM3P39fVjs8QooRJqZSD79Z0\n2nHowYlbE/wH8/ZsQ0bnvd5j3AeC+9vpRbi18GjZevBHCgVjjhjNmLbiGFkKNNfq\nszAsxYtvV4YXd6RFetqKBxRGMEbH6TVHcGnSbBfdmj/JoSfNAhxXsjwSlIVu63UC\nQ00xgM31vcjs9IEM7bUB\n=haf0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b00e79115c7ea6f61de227e8b96214870073c105\nparent fa036d39aadb160f819198d512efd1a2151a761b\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1782357232 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782357232 -0700\n\n[codex] Add Ultra reasoning effort (#29899)\n\n## Why\n\nUltra should be one user-facing reasoning selection for work that\nbenefits from both maximum reasoning and proactive multi-agent\ndelegation. Without it, clients must coordinate maximum reasoning with\nthe experimental `multiAgentMode` setting, even though the inference\nbackend still expects its existing `max` effort value.\n\nThis change makes reasoning effort the source of truth: clients select\n`ultra`, core derives proactive multi-agent behavior when the turn is\neligible for multi-agent V2, and inference requests continue to use the\nbackend-compatible `max` value.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `ultra` as a first-class reasoning effort and preserve\nmodel-catalog ordering when exposing it to clients.\n- Convert `ultra` to `max` at the inference request boundary, including\nResponses HTTP/WebSocket requests, startup prewarm, compaction, and\nmemory summarization.\n- Derive effective multi-agent mode per turn from effective reasoning\neffort:\n  - eligible multi-agent V2 + `ultra` → `proactive`\n  - eligible multi-agent V2 + any other effort → `explicitRequestOnly`\n- V1 or otherwise ineligible sessions → no multi-agent mode instruction\n- Keep the derived effective mode in turn context history so successive\nturns can emit a developer-message update only when the effective mode\nchanges.\n- Remove selected multi-agent mode from core session configuration, turn\nconstruction, thread settings, resume/fork restoration, and subagent\nspawn plumbing. Subagents inherit reasoning effort and derive their own\neffective mode.\n- Retain the experimental app-server `multiAgentMode` fields for wire\ncompatibility while marking them deprecated. Request values are accepted\nbut ignored; compatibility response fields report `explicitRequestOnly`.\n- Display Ultra in the TUI using the order supplied by `model/list`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core ultra_reasoning_uses_max_for_requests`\n- `just test -p codex-tui model_reasoning_selection_popup`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T03:13:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df1199fddb0c41441b7cd5a1f48bc48514a617dd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/df1199fddb0c41441b7cd5a1f48bc48514a617dd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df1199fddb0c41441b7cd5a1f48bc48514a617dd/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fa036d39aadb160f819198d512efd1a2151a761b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fa036d39aadb160f819198d512efd1a2151a761b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fa036d39aadb160f819198d512efd1a2151a761b"}]},{"sha":"fa036d39aadb160f819198d512efd1a2151a761b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZhMDM2ZDM5YWFkYjE2MGY4MTkxOThkNTEyZWZkMWEyMTUxYTc2MWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:13:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:13:49Z"},"message":"[2/3] core: persist world state in rollouts (#29835)\n\n## Why\n\n`WorldState` currently remembers its model-visible diff baseline only in\nmemory. That leaves no durable source for restoring the exact baseline\nafter resume, fork, rollback, or compaction.\n\nThis is the second PR in the WorldState persistence stack, built on\n#29833 and following #29249. It records durable state transitions; the\nnext PR will replay them during rollout reconstruction.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a `world_state` rollout item containing either a full snapshot or\nan RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch.\n- Persist a full snapshot after initial context and after compaction\nestablishes a new context window.\n- Persist non-empty patches when later sampling steps or turns advance\nthe WorldState baseline.\n- Write model-visible history before its matching WorldState record, so\nan interrupted write can only cause a safe repeated update on replay.\n- Preserve WorldState records for full-history forks while excluding\nthem from thread previews, metadata, and app-server history\nmaterialization.\n\nOlder binaries read rollout lines independently, so they skip the\nunknown `world_state` records while retaining the rest of the thread.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsnapshot_merge_patch_changes_and_removes_nested_values`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nworld_state_baseline_deduplicates_until_history_is_replaced`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndeferred_executor_compaction_preserves_then_updates_environment_once`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-state`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`","tree":{"sha":"d742d11ac285e4c861b9a20a394539b871de0031","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d742d11ac285e4c861b9a20a394539b871de0031"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fa036d39aadb160f819198d512efd1a2151a761b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPJztCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwUgQAIzmDppclf+xSzZ1R2voEhVm\nSwTSRDPlmgqLzleSHf1KBxi63/QGwWF4qjKNzDTAzKgnqz5/O3K9AinHndxw1wWK\niaNIJm/5Bz1gcTutA+vMcyYv1sFNI9Gb086oKEpa7dkb2xc5u7XI2W4LNsp0GoVk\nW9mKZp3mI4UoPBdi/L2mbFjI2LfyjSTH6F3nIPUUinaZuv6wnmjr826wbjzpFMpb\noCW4UtRlVi0EKH+LfwQjPa32cavHeL9rzEYk7GOWrj/OUJ4i+BCv7peu+HcHxtc7\nrS5qENDeUXrq2Gng3xGc7+laEXA+bHIWcClzm6e1sXFv/0lx4561ZIGNPt20r2tN\nQjVv3lRBM5C0mUpIQMVs/K/LHJ7bIr1b1TaPFzDTqKsLk+TAbaBsIUwrQHxB+xlm\nk9ZU/ITnkL56loPf7uuiLFpwQtKiqpySnsuCIXbuTyC2D6QLQwozsbY6phFQTLkQ\nO7kR6XZub4py3Y+HPVl+665a12EbU5wxhVPvSx5SkF7Xw612Lu/ze9EAz/dzL20I\nSomAII/iIjboYEWEo0enjU2fS4p26agSGlTLC+JQVK+5mxPp7CR6Hz/bw6QiX8W1\nicQ+VToTldgHUUGAdhE4l+ETj7/VEPtntcoFtZ+jpWaotRxJNWgP1jqx0S9K792S\n+Rt2spz3BbtglGbRhSWF\n=OVoz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d742d11ac285e4c861b9a20a394539b871de0031\nparent 6db937275fd610f3964b935b46144c74a0e0b55c\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782357229 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782357229 -0700\n\n[2/3] core: persist world state in rollouts (#29835)\n\n## Why\n\n`WorldState` currently remembers its model-visible diff baseline only in\nmemory. That leaves no durable source for restoring the exact baseline\nafter resume, fork, rollback, or compaction.\n\nThis is the second PR in the WorldState persistence stack, built on\n#29833 and following #29249. It records durable state transitions; the\nnext PR will replay them during rollout reconstruction.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a `world_state` rollout item containing either a full snapshot or\nan RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch.\n- Persist a full snapshot after initial context and after compaction\nestablishes a new context window.\n- Persist non-empty patches when later sampling steps or turns advance\nthe WorldState baseline.\n- Write model-visible history before its matching WorldState record, so\nan interrupted write can only cause a safe repeated update on replay.\n- Preserve WorldState records for full-history forks while excluding\nthem from thread previews, metadata, and app-server history\nmaterialization.\n\nOlder binaries read rollout lines independently, so they skip the\nunknown `world_state` records while retaining the rest of the thread.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsnapshot_merge_patch_changes_and_removes_nested_values`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nworld_state_baseline_deduplicates_until_history_is_replaced`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndeferred_executor_compaction_preserves_then_updates_environment_once`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-state`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T03:13:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fa036d39aadb160f819198d512efd1a2151a761b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fa036d39aadb160f819198d512efd1a2151a761b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fa036d39aadb160f819198d512efd1a2151a761b/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6db937275fd610f3964b935b46144c74a0e0b55c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6db937275fd610f3964b935b46144c74a0e0b55c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6db937275fd610f3964b935b46144c74a0e0b55c"}]},{"sha":"6db937275fd610f3964b935b46144c74a0e0b55c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkYjkzNzI3NWZkNjEwZjM5NjRiOTM1YjQ2MTQ0Yzc0YTBlMGI1NWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Abhinav","email":"abhinav@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:13:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:13:03Z"},"message":"[codex] Populate remote plugin local versions (#29956)\n\n# What\n\n- Carry installed remote release versions through remote plugin\nsummaries as `localVersion`.\n- Keep the app-server mapping a pure adapter by populating that value in\nthe remote catalog layer.\n\n# Why\n\nRemote plugin summaries always returned `localVersion: null` even after\ntheir versioned bundles had been installed locally. Consumers such as\nscheduled-task template discovery use `localVersion` to resolve a\nplugin's materialized root, so templates from remote curated plugins\nwere silently skipped.","tree":{"sha":"a1d818662ef18cee1822a4b84704015bd7096e9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a1d818662ef18cee1822a4b84704015bd7096e9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6db937275fd610f3964b935b46144c74a0e0b55c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPJy/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkrgQAKy/XsW/JPt2va3ZpBvIWYGX\nhSL++HJdRMPBAXgi5oMaqIZBVAGFVfHC8N2fS08EVy5CPFv2AdVsQD3JlbLaq85a\nQGMwaGFjR2yvR9O/2SwpVrECrkAWdgIN/powLpNNyewTZMXMjNjQznKafuKTF4CF\nl/wPG+GVXokzpxhkCGnyxtg+/UC8RrLwh6Z8SQmqBpDtBQXoRySiEp4cCMEuOWx2\n7Cpj6MC+30ifseB0mCvq2cZVP2WPTQMaWVJomJQUwlpbSeNocUbDh2tRwnNuCXkD\nJuARlwfu+IAmvlW25jrdXnmfwpNWdEQrT9/RreGCxzziOpnGH+GZF4+Dq3+5IHXW\ndh2pOuFkEX+mpA6p2R1jwGPa38GlqgiOHzJHsW/gXAVezAgVc8yO0fUXvS5/Zp+N\ne6cx1bl1bfOHj1jw97zMRAZ9gQeAuflHXh70rnSjHuIiXCde+nOPwa27Q3/GExjU\n7YxhGSayl2LXWzu4M93HNMxnJ4+Szp6NARTQse0Hpfg2Z3drKYxjkkAE6+W0OSxe\ntqAVeKztAGlhjJHgTV5XJZu/M8XgxRWgPnjXC0gi2pt0902LBgs6+8khfGNkfsee\n6IA1623oDXHrqeEU4I5Bu7TX9ciHW+m9SVA7mRYlYgSqDYFUfCbQNqTHDW9XhK2D\nSZdubUPy4qC4CUO2VTBF\n=VS9V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a1d818662ef18cee1822a4b84704015bd7096e9b\nparent b3e1c33776466d6b393e5b8700c322cd9897b929\nauthor Abhinav <abhinav@openai.com> 1782357183 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782357183 +0000\n\n[codex] Populate remote plugin local versions (#29956)\n\n# What\n\n- Carry installed remote release versions through remote plugin\nsummaries as `localVersion`.\n- Keep the app-server mapping a pure adapter by populating that value in\nthe remote catalog layer.\n\n# Why\n\nRemote plugin summaries always returned `localVersion: null` even after\ntheir versioned bundles had been installed locally. Consumers such as\nscheduled-task template discovery use `localVersion` to resolve a\nplugin's materialized root, so templates from remote curated plugins\nwere silently skipped.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T03:13:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6db937275fd610f3964b935b46144c74a0e0b55c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6db937275fd610f3964b935b46144c74a0e0b55c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6db937275fd610f3964b935b46144c74a0e0b55c/comments","author":{"login":"abhinav-oai","id":274334565,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFoDZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274334565?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/abhinav-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b3e1c33776466d6b393e5b8700c322cd9897b929","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b3e1c33776466d6b393e5b8700c322cd9897b929","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b3e1c33776466d6b393e5b8700c322cd9897b929"}]},{"sha":"b3e1c33776466d6b393e5b8700c322cd9897b929","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIzZTFjMzM3NzY0NjZkNmIzOTNlNWI4NzAwYzMyMmNkOTg5N2I5Mjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:03:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:03:22Z"},"message":"code-mode: define process host wire protocol (#29804)\n\n## Why\n\nThe process-owned code mode implementation needs an explicit, bounded\nwire contract before either side depends on it. Keeping framing and\nmessage semantics in `codex-code-mode-protocol` gives the client and\nsidecar one shared source of truth and makes compatibility failures\ndetectable during connection setup.\n\n## What changed\n\n- adds a versioned client/host handshake with required and optional\ncapabilities\n- defines operation requests and responses for session lifecycle and\ncell control\n- defines reverse delegate request, response, cancellation, and\ncell-closure messages\n- adds a four-byte little-endian length-prefixed JSON codec with a hard\nframe cap\n- rejects malformed frames, unknown fields, invalid identifiers, and\nunsupported protocol states\n- locks the wire representation down with explicit JSON round-trip tests\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode-protocol`\n\n## Stack\n\nPart 1 of 6. Followed by\n[#29805](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29805).","tree":{"sha":"3b1c3b47271550ec058b58f94860572ad956676a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3b1c3b47271550ec058b58f94860572ad956676a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b3e1c33776466d6b393e5b8700c322cd9897b929","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPJp6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJTsQAGHJHsOiqBnB1IgpeRTXSlym\nDRy9J3ZO8Vz05n3MK+wRU1GrevjfZ/tmKme7s7k6RaVGYMk5bFQj7KaF6lywKPxW\n9C4NrhQgQ+izPE0Moo8H1evtYnAXkD5ahO5gZb0BLM8Utwawagsmk+y5/ieqsKKb\nqRtTFnuS6jLjEnz6K/ApXTeWIJifodgChUYGD0RjKEhMJQcHR/G69wWZ0ZYhF27n\nuQk7qj0zGwEMDBmB9GUTixY1NXkYA4Q62RishsOnCF6NRJdU/VYXqVMOYrfB8nKh\nNpzXQLF04vW9sosVOGYl2yEC/fRKET4+xO7S606buVOFID/mq3DJqSj09ecUdpK1\nDnTtPqIjtbimyHP6CipNtxo4ALvcZxT7UYixe6Fy8Vp1+mY7hVQ4HSh3oK3b3EOW\nYVyY07qNG2yESVcG9YAjv0/3MGwB4tN45ErgchdWlGxv56r8bFewzvAAdiGwSP2/\nHaFLvaWuMtoOc/OAEw8hdW4HqpwPhBZIaHU4sc4mlJqk8lUG1vVJePD+Fho7Ug1z\nn+omeLAyDHgOvuJo1juhFI4XJEUMZN82SAlnyKYXKyuyfjAUR86y5gsiwQtu1llt\nJLOGKwODq6dUuj8MRCKzyaIKICaepRKMgAkKogxa+ljxUUIcTKRR3LX0qKOrSi9t\nFDmk/SoujbN7R8CPlDup\n=kWLl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3b1c3b47271550ec058b58f94860572ad956676a\nparent f8937b7d862e3d507fe22918e5daa35c7da993e9\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782356602 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782356602 -0700\n\ncode-mode: define process host wire protocol (#29804)\n\n## Why\n\nThe process-owned code mode implementation needs an explicit, bounded\nwire contract before either side depends on it. Keeping framing and\nmessage semantics in `codex-code-mode-protocol` gives the client and\nsidecar one shared source of truth and makes compatibility failures\ndetectable during connection setup.\n\n## What changed\n\n- adds a versioned client/host handshake with required and optional\ncapabilities\n- defines operation requests and responses for session lifecycle and\ncell control\n- defines reverse delegate request, response, cancellation, and\ncell-closure messages\n- adds a four-byte little-endian length-prefixed JSON codec with a hard\nframe cap\n- rejects malformed frames, unknown fields, invalid identifiers, and\nunsupported protocol states\n- locks the wire representation down with explicit JSON round-trip tests\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode-protocol`\n\n## Stack\n\nPart 1 of 6. Followed by\n[#29805](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29805).","verified_at":"2026-06-25T03:03:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b3e1c33776466d6b393e5b8700c322cd9897b929","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b3e1c33776466d6b393e5b8700c322cd9897b929","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b3e1c33776466d6b393e5b8700c322cd9897b929/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f8937b7d862e3d507fe22918e5daa35c7da993e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f8937b7d862e3d507fe22918e5daa35c7da993e9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f8937b7d862e3d507fe22918e5daa35c7da993e9"}]},{"sha":"f8937b7d862e3d507fe22918e5daa35c7da993e9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY4OTM3YjdkODYyZTNkNTA3ZmUyMjkxOGU1ZGFhMzVjN2RhOTkzZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-25T02:51:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T02:51:51Z"},"message":"Represent MCP authentication with an enum (#29924)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP authentication has distinct OAuth and ChatGPT-session flows.\nRepresenting that choice as `use_chatgpt_auth` makes one flow implicit\nand allows the configuration model to express the distinction only\nthrough a boolean.\n\nChatGPT credential forwarding also needs a first-party trust boundary. A\nconfigurable `chatgpt_base_url` controls routing, but must not grant an\nMCP server permission to receive session credentials.\n\nThis change builds on #29733, where the boolean was introduced.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace `use_chatgpt_auth` with an `auth` field backed by the\nexhaustive `McpServerAuth` enum.\n- Support `auth = \"oauth\"` and `auth = \"chatgpt\"`, with OAuth remaining\nthe default.\n- Trust only the origin derived from the existing hardcoded\n`CHATGPT_CODEX_BASE_URL` when granting ChatGPT auth to an MCP server.\n- Keep configured bearer tokens and authorization headers ahead of the\nselected authentication flow.\n- Update config writers, schema output, fixtures, and integration-test\nsetup to use the enum.\n\n## Verification\n\nIntegration coverage exercises the complete streamable HTTP startup path\nin two independent configurations:\n\n- A directly constructed MCP configuration verifies that matching an\noverridden `chatgpt_base_url` does not grant ChatGPT auth.\n- A persisted `config.toml` containing an attacker-controlled\n`chatgpt_base_url` and `auth = \"chatgpt\"` verifies the same boundary\nthrough normal config parsing.\n\nBoth tests complete MCP initialization and tool listing and assert that\nthe full captured request sequence contains no authorization headers.\nSeparate integration coverage verifies that configured authorization\ntakes precedence over ChatGPT auth.","tree":{"sha":"87e954615f8c466f90f4730aa7b00004b8fc6937","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/87e954615f8c466f90f4730aa7b00004b8fc6937"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f8937b7d862e3d507fe22918e5daa35c7da993e9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPJfHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkjwQAEVR5hrhYHXcSfNLFf2wdlNI\nSub6tzhZdCUY+4BG3/vPxWx5l/T0nl77rYGbx2l9IvFC1Yem8F4rMEpS3ZpnvK3n\nwe0P+AyhHYi8eWWDtcHAPY8mL5vGZqhP1JnJjkV/a3Ztlh1ohllS7YXYNisqFOMC\nFxvEx9pPUWfqWt9XXnZ4T2m9sdTw55D3lT2jN1nKtiYJn0PoTIpK0tLFSPtHkksa\nYZ9OoEFXSZ2mTkzIFrFpWbjlU6Pvekiev515iLfgxItTsBHYGGmpCSOn0KdIBXgO\nTAw8rd4Xa+0B9tY+JX63NmZoVDTUBwxgSAVesvZ3PUpgKvw/i/J5amcoERCaGPqT\n5OEQ8vRftca8NXa3gx/LyXflEoVTks4WhMzH5l68jSJmofQK4GsZIeP/i2LjHkw4\nKRZq+qKcXnyZPN3Xh07X4jXdmn19W8iLbb6slzB0Cp96NP0bcAvwLvYAHJJsrNbx\n3xkMYe+eLNM/CDRhUwDzj8IMo/FFb9J5VXtQy5dTRxVHDqe+wfgQKDlXCm8PALC3\nQNjyVk5fNoP5Gkqv5MB3hR6OKaIlTpeLJng8ecqx+/dVCrHoW2HncEhM34LxDm1d\nfFnIO9N58sLFsA/MekTl4TZN0fK1zcGV925liNM/2HmoqrlEUJF/snrg65Gzf6Bs\n8Jt2U18zzNC4v56NjthW\n=hz7D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 87e954615f8c466f90f4730aa7b00004b8fc6937\nparent 6801941cfea0a09721041daa24f47f70a5fc4aae\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1782355911 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782355911 -0700\n\nRepresent MCP authentication with an enum (#29924)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP authentication has distinct OAuth and ChatGPT-session flows.\nRepresenting that choice as `use_chatgpt_auth` makes one flow implicit\nand allows the configuration model to express the distinction only\nthrough a boolean.\n\nChatGPT credential forwarding also needs a first-party trust boundary. A\nconfigurable `chatgpt_base_url` controls routing, but must not grant an\nMCP server permission to receive session credentials.\n\nThis change builds on #29733, where the boolean was introduced.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace `use_chatgpt_auth` with an `auth` field backed by the\nexhaustive `McpServerAuth` enum.\n- Support `auth = \"oauth\"` and `auth = \"chatgpt\"`, with OAuth remaining\nthe default.\n- Trust only the origin derived from the existing hardcoded\n`CHATGPT_CODEX_BASE_URL` when granting ChatGPT auth to an MCP server.\n- Keep configured bearer tokens and authorization headers ahead of the\nselected authentication flow.\n- Update config writers, schema output, fixtures, and integration-test\nsetup to use the enum.\n\n## Verification\n\nIntegration coverage exercises the complete streamable HTTP startup path\nin two independent configurations:\n\n- A directly constructed MCP configuration verifies that matching an\noverridden `chatgpt_base_url` does not grant ChatGPT auth.\n- A persisted `config.toml` containing an attacker-controlled\n`chatgpt_base_url` and `auth = \"chatgpt\"` verifies the same boundary\nthrough normal config parsing.\n\nBoth tests complete MCP initialization and tool listing and assert that\nthe full captured request sequence contains no authorization headers.\nSeparate integration coverage verifies that configured authorization\ntakes precedence over ChatGPT auth.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T02:51:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f8937b7d862e3d507fe22918e5daa35c7da993e9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f8937b7d862e3d507fe22918e5daa35c7da993e9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f8937b7d862e3d507fe22918e5daa35c7da993e9/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"http